window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0119", [{"word":"ocean basin","ipa_uk":"/ˈəʊʃən ˈbeɪsn/","ipa_us":"/ˈoʊʃən ˈbeɪsn/","definition_zh":"洋盆；海盆；大洋盆地；（海底）沉积盆地；深海盆地；海洋管理单元","definition_en":"a large bowl-shaped depression in the ocean floor, together with the seawater and sediment it holds","core_image":"海底一只巨大的浅碗，碗壁是大陆坡，碗底铺着细软的沉积物","scene":"海洋学家在考察船上盯着声呐屏幕，海底的轮廓像一只巨大的浅碗。The survey mapped a vast ocean basin beneath the Pacific.","sceneCN":"这里指「海底的大型凹陷单元」（第 1 个义项：海底地壳下凹、被海水与沉积物填充的巨大盆地）；句意为勘测船在太平洋海底测绘出一片辽阔的洋盆。场景物件：声呐屏幕、海底剖面线、大陆坡、沉积物。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"洋盆；海盆；大洋盆地（可数；复数 ocean basins）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the Pacific ocean basin","zh":"太平洋洋盆"},{"phrase":"deep ocean basin","zh":"深海盆地"},{"phrase":"ocean basin sediments","zh":"洋盆沉积物"},{"phrase":"the formation of an ocean basin","zh":"洋盆的形成"},{"phrase":"ocean basin circulation","zh":"洋盆环流"},{"phrase":"a closed ocean basin","zh":"封闭洋盆"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"ocean basins"},{"label":"定语形式（洋盆的）","form":"ocean-basin"},{"label":"相关形容词（海洋的）","form":"oceanic"},{"label":"相关名词（海洋）","form":"ocean"},{"label":"相关名词（盆；流域）","form":"basin"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"ocean","pos":"n.","zh":"海洋；大洋"},{"word":"oceanic","pos":"adj.","zh":"海洋的；远洋的"},{"word":"basin","pos":"n.","zh":"盆；盆地；流域"},{"word":"basinal","pos":"adj.","zh":"盆地的；盆内的"},{"word":"oceanography","pos":"n.","zh":"海洋学"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Depression in the sea floor","titleCN":"海底的大型凹陷","definition":"a broad, bowl-shaped depression in the ocean floor","definitionCN":"海底宽阔、碗状的凹陷","example":"The survey mapped a vast ocean basin beneath the Pacific.","exampleCN":"勘测船在太平洋海底测绘出一片辽阔的洋盆。","why":"A basin is a bowl, so when the word is applied to the sea floor it names the bowl itself, not the water inside it.","whyCN":"basin 本义是「盆」，用于海底时命名的就是这只盆，而不是盆里的水。"},{"no":"02","title":"One of the named major basins","titleCN":"具名的大洋分区","definition":"one of the large named divisions of the world ocean, such as the Pacific or Atlantic basin","definitionCN":"世界大洋中被命名的大分区，如太平洋洋盆或大西洋洋盆","example":"Each ocean basin has its own pattern of deep circulation.","exampleCN":"每个洋盆都有各自的深层环流格局。","why":"Geographers needed countable units, so the term was fixed to the named bowls that partition the global ocean.","whyCN":"地理学家需要可数的单元，于是这个词被固定到划分全球大洋的那些具名盆地上。"},{"no":"03","title":"The water held in the bowl","titleCN":"盆中容纳的海水","definition":"the volume of seawater held within such a depression, treated as a reservoir","definitionCN":"这样一处凹陷中容纳的海水量，被视为一个储库","example":"Warming has changed the heat content of the whole ocean basin.","exampleCN":"变暖改变了整个洋盆的热含量。","why":"In climate accounting the container and its contents are spoken of together, so the basin comes to mean the water it holds.","whyCN":"在气候核算中，容器与内容常被合在一起说，于是洋盆也指它所盛的水。"},{"no":"04","title":"Sedimentary basin under the sea","titleCN":"海底沉积盆地","definition":"a depression beneath the sea in which sediments accumulate over geological time","definitionCN":"海底在漫长地质时间内堆积沉积物的凹陷","example":"Drilling reached ancient layers in the ocean basin.","exampleCN":"钻探触及了洋盆中的古老地层。","why":"Geologists care about what fills the bowl, so the term shifted from the shape to the sediment body that records its history.","whyCN":"地质学家关心盆里填了什么，于是词义从形状转向记录历史的沉积体。"},{"no":"05","title":"Tectonic basin opened by rifting","titleCN":"裂谷张开的构造盆地","definition":"a basin formed where the sea floor spreads or a continental margin stretches","definitionCN":"海底扩张或大陆边缘拉伸所形成的盆地","example":"The rift opened a new ocean basin between the continents.","exampleCN":"裂谷在大陆之间打开了一个新的洋盆。","why":"Plate tectonics explained how the bowl came to exist, so the term gained a process meaning alongside its shape meaning.","whyCN":"板块构造解释了这只盆如何产生，词义便在形状之外多了一层过程义。"},{"no":"06","title":"Deep-sea floor province","titleCN":"深海海底分区","definition":"the abyssal part of the sea floor, away from trenches and continental shelves","definitionCN":"海底中远离海沟与大陆架的深海部分","example":"Fine sediment covers much of the deep ocean basin.","exampleCN":"细颗粒沉积物覆盖了深海盆地的大部分。","why":"Oceanographers divide the floor into provinces, and the flat abyssal plains are the basin proper.","whyCN":"海洋学家把海底分成若干区域，平坦的深海平原正是「盆」的本体。"},{"no":"07","title":"Regional marine management unit","titleCN":"区域海洋管理单元","definition":"a large sea area treated as one unit for pollution control or fisheries policy","definitionCN":"在污染控制或渔业政策中被当作一个单元的大片海域","example":"The treaty set catch limits for the entire ocean basin.","exampleCN":"该条约对整个洋盆设定了捕捞上限。","why":"Governments manage water at the scale of the bowl, so a physical term became an administrative one.","whyCN":"各国按盆的尺度管理水域，物理词便成了行政词。"},{"no":"08","title":"Figurative vast receptacle","titleCN":"比喻义：巨大的容器","definition":"any very large enclosing space that seems to gather things into itself","definitionCN":"任何巨大、包围性的空间，仿佛把事物收拢其中","example":"The old library was an ocean basin of forgotten journals.","exampleCN":"那座旧图书馆像一只洋盆，收着被遗忘的期刊。","why":"Once a basin is felt as a container, it can name any broad hollow that collects, even one far from the sea.","whyCN":"一旦盆被感觉为容器，它就能命名任何广阔的收拢之处，哪怕远离海洋。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Ocean basin joins Greek ōkeanos, the stream believed to encircle the world, to Old French bacin 'bowl'. The phrase itself is a modern geological compound. Dates are approximate.","cn":"ocean basin 把希腊 ōkeanos「被认为环绕世界的大河」与古法语 bacin「盆」并置；整个短语是近代地质学的复合词。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK OKEANOS","en":"Greek ōkeanos named the great river thought to run around the inhabited world; the word's pre-Greek source is unknown and every older root proposed for it is a reconstruction.","cn":"希腊 ōkeanos 指被认为环绕有人居住世界的大河；该词在前希腊语中的来源不明，凡为其拟出的更早词根都是重构形式。"},{"era":"LATIN OCEANUS","en":"Latin took the Greek word as oceanus and used it for the outer sea, the great body of water beyond the known lands.","cn":"拉丁语借入希腊词作 oceanus，用来指外海，即已知陆地之外的巨大水域。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH BACIN","en":"Bacin 'bowl' came from late Latin baccinum; a Gaulish source *bacca 'container' has been proposed, but it is a reconstructed form and not a demonstrated origin.","cn":"bacin「盆」来自晚期拉丁 baccinum；有说法认为出自高卢语 *bacca「容器」，但这只是重构形式，并非已证实的来源。"},{"era":"ENGLISH BASIN","en":"English basin first meant a washing bowl, then any hollow vessel or hollow place, and geologists later extended it to layered rock depressions.","cn":"英语 basin 最初指洗脸盆，随后指任何中空器皿或凹地，地质学家后来把它扩展到成层的岩石凹陷。"},{"era":"THE PHRASE","en":"Ocean basin became standard in nineteenth-century oceanography, after deep soundings showed that the sea floor is divided into broad bowls rather than one flat plain.","cn":"十九世纪海洋学测得海底并非一整块平原，而是分成若干宽阔的盆，ocean basin 由此成为标准术语。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin and first date): the pre-Greek source of ōkeanos is unknown, the Gaulish *bacca is a reconstruction, and the exact first printed use of the full phrase is not recorded.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源与首见年代）：ōkeanos 的前希腊语来源不明，高卢语 *bacca 属重构形式，完整短语最早的印刷记录也未确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the same-root or easily swapped sea and bowl words; group two holds neighbouring sea-floor features that are often mistaken for a basin.","cn":"第一组是同根或容易被替换的海与盆相关词；第二组是常被误当作洋盆的邻近海底地貌。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"ocean","ipa":"/ˈəʊʃən/","tag":"the water, not the hollow","definition":"The body of seawater itself; an ocean basin is the depression that holds it, so the two stand as container and contents.","definitionCN":"指海水本身；ocean basin 指盛住它的凹陷，两者是容器与内容的关系。"},{"word":"basin","ipa":"/ˈbeɪsn/","tag":"general hollow","definition":"Any bowl-shaped depression on land or under the sea; ocean basin narrows the general word to the marine case.","definitionCN":"陆上或海底任何碗状凹陷；ocean basin 把这个通用词收窄到海洋情形。"},{"word":"oceanic","ipa":"/əˈsiːənɪk/","tag":"adjective from the same stock","definition":"An adjective describing ocean features; it modifies a noun and cannot itself name the depression.","definitionCN":"描述海洋特征的形容词；它修饰名词，本身不能命名那处凹陷。"},{"word":"oceanography","ipa":"/ˌəʊʃəˈnɒɡrəfi/","tag":"the science, not the object","definition":"The scientific study of the ocean; the basin is what the science studies, not the science itself.","definitionCN":"研究海洋的科学；洋盆是它研究的对象，而不是这门学科本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"seafloor","ipa":"/ˈsiːflɔː/","tag":"the surface, not the shape","definition":"The surface of the sea bottom; a basin is one particular depression in that surface.","definitionCN":"指海底的表面；洋盆是这一表面上的一处特定凹陷。"},{"word":"abyssal plain","ipa":"/əˈbɪsl pleɪn/","tag":"flat province inside a basin","definition":"A broad flat area of the deep sea floor; it is the floor of a basin, not the whole bowl.","definitionCN":"深海海底宽阔平坦的区域；它是盆底，而不是整只盆。"},{"word":"trench","ipa":"/trentʃ/","tag":"deep narrow cut","definition":"A long, narrow, very deep depression; a basin is broad and bowl-shaped, while a trench is a slot.","definitionCN":"狭长而极深的凹陷；洋盆宽阔如碗，海沟则像一道窄槽。"},{"word":"watershed","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtəʃed/","tag":"land drainage, another sense of basin","definition":"The land area draining into a river or sea; it uses basin in the drainage sense, not the sea-floor sense.","definitionCN":"河流或海洋的集水陆地；它用的是 basin 的流域义，不是海底义。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real morphemes, real relatives and real collocations, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的语素、真实的同族词与真实搭配，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"Basin is a bowl, so an ocean basin is the sea's bowl.","cn":"basin 是盆，ocean basin 就是大海的那只盆。"},{"en":"Ocean descends from Greek ōkeanos, the river thought to encircle the world.","cn":"ocean 出自希腊 ōkeanos，即被认为环绕世界的大河。"},{"en":"Geologists read the basin as an archive of sediment layers.","cn":"地质学家把洋盆读成一部沉积层档案。"},{"en":"The named basins are the Pacific, Atlantic, Indian, Arctic and Southern.","cn":"具名的洋盆包括太平洋、大西洋、印度洋、北冰洋与南大洋。"},{"en":"A basin holds water, heat and sediment, so it is both container and record.","cn":"洋盆盛着水、热与沉积物，因此既是容器也是记录。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a huge stone bowl sunk into the sea floor, its rim the continental slope.","cn":"想象一只巨大的石盆沉在海底，盆沿就是大陆坡。"},{"en":"Picture a library whose shelves are layers of sediment laid down over ages.","cn":"想象一座图书馆，书架就是千百年来铺下的沉积层。"},{"en":"Picture a world map divided into five enormous bowls, each with its own weather.","cn":"想象一张被分成五只巨盆的世界地图，每只盆都有自己的天气。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The Pacific is the deepest ocean basin on Earth.","cn":"太平洋是地球上最深的洋盆。"},{"en":"Sediment cores from the ocean basin revealed a long climate record.","cn":"取自洋盆的沉积柱芯揭示了一段漫长的气候记录。"},{"en":"Treaties now manage fisheries across the whole ocean basin.","cn":"各项条约如今在整个洋盆范围内管理渔业。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「ocean（海洋）+ basin（盆）」——海里那只巨大的盆 → 洋盆、海盆","word":"ocean basin"},"root":"希腊 ōkeanos「环绕世界的大河」（更深来源不确定）→ 拉丁 oceanus → 英语 ocean；古法语 bacin「盆」← 晚期拉丁 baccinum，高卢语 *bacca「容器」为重构假说 → basin。两词在十九世纪海洋学中合为 ocean basin。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one bowl: it is a shape on the sea floor, a named division of the world ocean, the water inside, the sediment filling it, a tectonic opening, a deep-sea province, a management unit and finally any vast receptacle.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一只「盆」展开：它是海底的形状、世界大洋的具名分区、盆中的水、填入的沉积、构造张开的凹陷、深海分区、管理单元，最后引申为任何巨大的容器。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a vast shallow bowl sunk into the sea floor, its rim the continental slope and its bottom lined with sediment.","cn":"核心意象：一只巨大的浅碗沉在海底，盆沿是大陆坡，盆底铺着沉积物。"},"chain":["SEA-FLOOR DEPRESSION","NAMED OCEAN UNIT","WATER RESERVOIR","SEDIMENTARY BASIN","TECTONIC BASIN","DEEP-SEA PROVINCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04","en":"SEDIMENT RECORD: the same hollow that gives shape also stores layers, so a landform becomes an archive.","cn":"沉积记录：给出形状的同一处凹陷也存下层层沉积，地貌因此成为档案。"},{"senses":"02","en":"THE NAMED BOWLS: a handful of great basins carry proper names.","cn":"具名洋盆：少数几个大盆各有专名。"},{"senses":"03 · 08","en":"CONTAINER METAPHOR: once treated as a vessel, the basin can hold heat, water or even forgotten papers.","cn":"容器比喻：一旦被当作器皿，洋盆就能盛住热量、海水，甚至被遗忘的纸张。"},{"senses":"05 · 06","en":"PLATE TO FLOOR: rifting explains how the bowl opens, and the abyssal plain is its mature deep-sea expression.","cn":"从板块到海底：裂谷说明盆如何张开，深海平原是它成熟的深海形态。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE GOVERNED AREA: the basin becomes the unit treaties and agencies work in.","cn":"治理区域：洋盆成为条约与机构工作的单元。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Ocean basin is a transparent two-word compound: a Greek-derived sea word plus a Romance-derived bowl word. Its parts teach more than its inflection does.","cn":"ocean basin 是一个透明的双词复合体：一个源自希腊语的海洋词，加一个源自罗曼语的盆字。它的构词部分比屈折变化更值得注意。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin layer supplies oceanus and baccinum, while the Greek layer supplies ōkeanos; no single Latin verb lies behind the whole phrase.","cn":"拉丁层提供 oceanus 与 baccinum，希腊层提供 ōkeanos；整个短语背后并没有单一拉丁动词。"},"items":[{"word":"ocean","structure":"Greek ōkeanos via Latin oceanus","meaning":"the great body of sea water","meaningCN":"巨大的海水体","example":"The ocean covers most of the planet.","exampleCN":"海洋覆盖了行星的大部分。"},{"word":"basin","structure":"Old French bacin 'bowl'","meaning":"a bowl or hollow","meaningCN":"盆；凹地","example":"Rain filled the stone basin.","exampleCN":"雨水注满了石盆。"},{"word":"oceanic","structure":"ocean + -ic (adjective suffix)","meaning":"relating to the ocean","meaningCN":"与海洋有关的","example":"Oceanic currents move heat poleward.","exampleCN":"洋流把热量带向两极。"},{"word":"basinal","structure":"basin + -al (adjective suffix)","meaning":"relating to a basin","meaningCN":"与盆地有关的","example":"Basinal sediments thicken toward the centre.","exampleCN":"盆内沉积物向中心增厚。"},{"word":"oceanography","structure":"ocean + -graphy (writing, description)","meaning":"the scientific description of the ocean","meaningCN":"对海洋的科学描述与研究","example":"Oceanography relies on ships and satellites.","exampleCN":"海洋学依靠船只与卫星。"},{"word":"ocean basin","structure":"ocean + basin (compound noun)","meaning":"the sea-floor bowl and its contents","meaningCN":"海底的盆及其内容","example":"The ocean basin stores carbon in its sediment.","exampleCN":"洋盆把碳储存在沉积物中。"},{"word":"basin-wide","structure":"basin + wide (compound adjective)","meaning":"extending across a whole basin","meaningCN":"遍及整个盆地的","example":"The survey was basin-wide.","exampleCN":"这次调查覆盖整个盆地。"},{"word":"oceanic basin","structure":"oceanic + basin (variant term)","meaning":"a basin in oceanic crust","meaningCN":"洋壳中的盆地","example":"The oceanic basin lies beyond the shelf break.","exampleCN":"洋壳盆地位于陆架坡折之外。"},{"word":"baccinum","structure":"late Latin baccinum (neuter noun)","meaning":"a basin or bowl","meaningCN":"盆；碗","example":"The word entered French as bacin.","exampleCN":"这个词以 bacin 进入法语。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"oceanus","structure":"oceanus, oceanī (m., second declension)","meaning":"the outer sea, the ocean","meaningCN":"外海；大洋"},{"word":"baccinum","structure":"baccinum, baccinī (n., second declension; late Latin)","meaning":"a basin, a bowl","meaningCN":"盆；碗"}]}},{"word":"coastal erosion","ipa_uk":"/ˌkəʊstl ɪˈrəʊʒn/","ipa_us":"/ˌkoʊstl ɪˈroʊʒn/","definition_zh":"海岸侵蚀；海岸冲刷；岸线后退；海滩与崖壁的流失；海岸灾害","definition_en":"the wearing away and removal of coastal land by waves, currents, tides and weather","core_image":"波浪一次次扑向崖脚，掏空底部，上面的土块随即塌落","scene":"测绘人员在退潮时沿着崖脚拉尺，记录一年来岸线退了多少。Waves have cut the cliff back so fast that coastal erosion now threatens the village road.","sceneCN":"这里指「海水与波浪对陆地的磨损与带走」（第 1 个义项：海岸带陆地物质被波浪、潮流与风化持续剥离的过程）；句意为海浪把崖壁切退得太快，海岸侵蚀如今威胁着村里的道路。场景物件：崖脚、卷尺、退潮滩面、塌落的土块。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"海岸侵蚀（不可数；指多起事件时偶用复数 coastal erosions）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"accelerated coastal erosion","zh":"加速的海岸侵蚀"},{"phrase":"coastal erosion rate","zh":"海岸侵蚀速率"},{"phrase":"control coastal erosion","zh":"控制海岸侵蚀"},{"phrase":"coastal erosion control structures","zh":"海岸侵蚀防治工程"},{"phrase":"a hotspot of coastal erosion","zh":"海岸侵蚀热点区"},{"phrase":"coastal erosion and sea-level rise","zh":"海岸侵蚀与海平面上升"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（少见，指多次事件）","form":"coastal erosions"},{"label":"相关动词（侵蚀）","form":"erode"},{"label":"相关形容词（侵蚀形成的）","form":"erosional"},{"label":"相关名词（侵蚀）","form":"erosion"},{"label":"相关名词（海岸）","form":"coast"},{"label":"定语形式（海岸侵蚀的）","form":"coastal-erosion"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"coast","pos":"n./v.","zh":"海岸；沿海航行"},{"word":"coastal","pos":"adj.","zh":"海岸的；沿海的"},{"word":"erode","pos":"v.","zh":"侵蚀；逐渐削弱"},{"word":"erosion","pos":"n.","zh":"侵蚀；腐蚀"},{"word":"erosional","pos":"adj.","zh":"侵蚀的；侵蚀形成的"},{"word":"erosive","pos":"adj.","zh":"有侵蚀力的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The general wearing away of the coast","titleCN":"海岸侵蚀总称","definition":"the wearing away and removal of coastal land by waves, currents, tides and weather","definitionCN":"海岸带陆地物质被波浪、潮流、潮汐与风化持续剥离的过程","example":"Waves have cut the cliff back so fast that coastal erosion now threatens the village road.","exampleCN":"海浪把崖壁切退得太快，海岸侵蚀如今威胁着村里的道路。","why":"Coastal locates the process at the edge of the sea, and erosion names the biting away, so the phrase is simply the geological process in its marine setting.","whyCN":"coastal 把过程定位到海陆边缘，erosion 指「啃掉」，因此这个短语就是发生在海边的侵蚀过程。"},{"no":"02","title":"Cliff retreat","titleCN":"崖壁后退","definition":"the backward movement of a cliff as waves cut away its base","definitionCN":"波浪掏空崖脚、崖壁随之向陆地方向后退","example":"Coastal erosion left a fresh notch at the base of the chalk cliff.","exampleCN":"海岸侵蚀在白垩崖脚留下了一道新切口。","why":"When the process works on solid rock, its most visible result is a cliff sliding back, so the phrase names that retreat.","whyCN":"当这一过程作用于坚硬岩石，最显眼的结果就是崖壁后退，于是这个短语也指这种后退。"},{"no":"03","title":"Beach and dune loss","titleCN":"海滩与沙丘流失","definition":"the removal of sand and sediment from beaches and dunes faster than it is replaced","definitionCN":"海滩与沙丘的沙和沉积物被带走的速度快于补充","example":"Coastal erosion has narrowed the beach to a few metres at high tide.","exampleCN":"海岸侵蚀已使高潮时的海滩缩到几米宽。","why":"On soft shores the same process removes loose sand, so the phrase shifts from rock to the beach that disappears.","whyCN":"在松软海岸上，同一过程带走的是散沙，词义便从岩石转到消失的海滩。"},{"no":"04","title":"Measured shoreline retreat","titleCN":"实测岸线后退","definition":"a measured landward shift of the shoreline over a period of time","definitionCN":"一段时间内岸线向陆地方向的可测移动","example":"The survey records coastal erosion of about two metres a year.","exampleCN":"这项测量记录到每年约两米的海岸侵蚀。","why":"Once surveyors fixed a baseline, the process became a number, so the phrase also names the measured displacement rather than the process itself.","whyCN":"当测量员定下基线，过程就变成一个数字，因此这个短语也指实测的位移本身。"},{"no":"05","title":"A sediment budget deficit","titleCN":"沉积物收支赤字","definition":"a coastal sediment budget in which more material leaves than arrives","definitionCN":"海岸沉积物输出多于输入的收支状态","example":"Dams upstream have deepened coastal erosion by cutting the sand supply.","exampleCN":"上游水坝切断沙源，加深了海岸侵蚀。","why":"Coastal science explains retreat as a budget problem, so the phrase can name the deficit that drives the visible loss.","whyCN":"海岸科学把后退解释为收支问题，因此这个短语也能指驱动可见流失的赤字。"},{"no":"06","title":"Storm-driven episodic erosion","titleCN":"风暴引起的突发侵蚀","definition":"rapid erosion caused by a single storm, surge or flood","definitionCN":"由单次风暴、风暴潮或洪水造成的快速侵蚀","example":"One winter storm caused more coastal erosion than a decade of ordinary waves.","exampleCN":"一场冬季风暴造成的海岸侵蚀超过十年平常波浪。","why":"Most loss happens in short bursts, so the phrase also marks episodic events rather than the slow average.","whyCN":"大部分流失发生在短促的爆发中，因此这个短语也标记突发事件，而非缓慢的平均值。"},{"no":"07","title":"Hazard and property loss","titleCN":"灾害与财产损失","definition":"the risk and actual loss of land, homes and infrastructure to coastal retreat","definitionCN":"土地、房屋与基础设施因岸线后退而面临的风险与实际损失","example":"Insurance premiums rose as coastal erosion reached the sea front.","exampleCN":"随着海岸侵蚀逼近海滨一线，保险费上涨了。","why":"Planners turned the natural process into a hazard category, so the phrase now names what people stand to lose.","whyCN":"规划者把自然过程转成灾害类别，于是这个短语现在指人们可能失去的东西。"},{"no":"08","title":"Figurative gradual attrition","titleCN":"比喻义：渐进的消磨","definition":"gradual, repeated loss that wears something down as waves wear rock","definitionCN":"反复而缓慢的损失，像波浪磨石一样把事物消磨掉","example":"Budget cuts produced a slow coastal erosion of public trust.","exampleCN":"预算削减造成公众信任缓慢的「海岸侵蚀」。","why":"Because erosion is already a metaphor for slow loss, the full phrase can be borrowed whenever an edge is worn away.","whyCN":"侵蚀本就比喻缓慢的丧失，因此整个短语可借来形容任何被一点点磨掉的边缘。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Coastal erosion pairs Latin costa 'rib, side' with Latin erodere 'to gnaw out'; both entered English through French and learned borrowing. The phrase is a modern technical collocation. Dates are approximate.","cn":"coastal erosion 把拉丁 costa「肋骨、侧边」与拉丁 erodere「啃掉」配在一起；两者分别经法语与学术借入英语。整个短语是近代技术搭配。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN COSTA","en":"Costa meant 'rib' and then 'side, flank'; speakers applied it to the land beside the sea, giving Old French coste and English coast.","cn":"costa 本指「肋骨」，再指「侧面、侧翼」；人们把它用于海旁的陆地，形成古法语 coste 与英语 coast。"},{"era":"COASTAL","en":"English added the adjective suffix -al to coast, producing coastal 'of the coast'; the suffix comes from Latin -alis.","cn":"英语给 coast 加上形容词后缀 -al，构成 coastal「海岸的」；该后缀源自拉丁 -alis。"},{"era":"LATIN RODERE","en":"Erodere combines e- 'out' with rodere 'to gnaw'; classical Latin used it for gnawing away or eating into a surface.","cn":"erodere 由 e-「出」与 rodere「啃、啮」组成；古典拉丁用它表示啃掉或侵蚀进表面。"},{"era":"EROSION IN ENGLISH","en":"Erosion entered English in the early modern period as a learned noun; geology then made it the standard term for land worn away by water, ice and wind.","cn":"erosion 在近代早期作为学术名词进入英语；地质学随后把它定为水、冰与风磨损陆地的标准术语。"},{"era":"THE PHRASE","en":"Coastal erosion became a fixed collocation in twentieth-century coastal engineering, once sea walls and groynes were planned against measured retreat.","cn":"二十世纪海岸工程开始按实测后退规划海堤与丁坝之后，coastal erosion 成为固定搭配。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin): the pre-Latin source of costa is unknown and proposed roots are reconstructions; rodere also has no settled deeper etymology; the phrase's first printed use is not exactly dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源）：costa 在拉丁语之前的来源不明，所拟词根都是重构形式；rodere 的更深词源也无定论；短语最早的印刷记录未确定。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds same-root forms that are often swapped; group two holds other shore processes that remove or move coastal material.","cn":"第一组是同根、常被互换的形式；第二组是其他搬走或移动海岸物质的岸边过程。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"erosion","ipa":"/ɪˈrəʊʒn/","tag":"the general process","definition":"Wearing away by any agent; coastal erosion is the same process confined to the shore, so erosion is the wider term.","definitionCN":"任何营力的磨损；coastal erosion 是把同一过程限定在海岸，因此 erosion 范围更宽。"},{"word":"erode","ipa":"/ɪˈrəʊd/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To wear something away; it names the action, while coastal erosion names the process as a noun.","definitionCN":"磨损某物；它指动作，而 coastal erosion 把这一过程作为名词来指称。"},{"word":"erosional","ipa":"/ɪˈrəʊʒənl/","tag":"adjective of result","definition":"Describing landforms created by erosion; it cannot replace the noun phrase that names the process.","definitionCN":"描述由侵蚀造成的地貌；它不能替代指称过程的名词短语。"},{"word":"coastal","ipa":"/ˈkəʊstl/","tag":"adjective, the locator","definition":"Relating to the coast; it only says where something happens, without naming the wearing away.","definitionCN":"与海岸有关的；它只说事情发生在哪里，并不指磨损本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"shoreline retreat","ipa":"/ˈʃɔːlaɪn rɪˈtriːt/","tag":"measured result","definition":"The landward movement of the waterline; it is the measurable outcome of coastal erosion, not the process.","definitionCN":"水线向陆地的移动；它是海岸侵蚀可测的结果，而不是过程本身。"},{"word":"sediment starvation","ipa":"/ˈsedɪmənt stɑːˈveɪʃn/","tag":"cause","definition":"A shortage of sand and silt reaching the shore; it is one driver of coastal erosion, not the loss itself.","definitionCN":"到达海岸的沙与粉砂不足；它是海岸侵蚀的驱动因素之一，而不是流失本身。"},{"word":"weathering","ipa":"/ˈweðərɪŋ/","tag":"breakdown in place","definition":"The breaking down of rock by weather and chemistry without removal; erosion carries the material away.","definitionCN":"岩石因天气与化学作用在原地破碎；侵蚀则把物质搬走。"},{"word":"deposition","ipa":"/dɪˈpɒzɪʃn/","tag":"the opposite balance","definition":"The laying down of sediment; it builds the shore up while coastal erosion takes it away.","definitionCN":"沉积物落下的过程；它把海岸堆高，而海岸侵蚀把海岸削去。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real Latin parts, real relatives and real field collocations, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的拉丁构件、真实的同族词与真实的野外搭配，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"Costa means rib, and the coast is the rib of the land.","cn":"costa 是肋骨，海岸就是大地的肋骨。"},{"en":"Rodere means to gnaw, so erosion is the sea gnawing the shore.","cn":"rodere 是啃，侵蚀就是海在啃岸。"},{"en":"The pair coastal erosion names both where it happens and what it does.","cn":"coastal erosion 同时说清发生地点与动作。"},{"en":"A sediment budget is the accounting side of the same loss.","cn":"沉积物收支是同一场流失的账目侧面。"},{"en":"Engineers distinguish slow retreat from storm-driven erosion.","cn":"工程师把缓慢后退与风暴突发侵蚀分开看。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a fist of water punching the same spot at the cliff foot until the rock gives way.","cn":"想象一只水做的拳头反复砸向崖脚同一点，直到岩石让开。"},{"en":"Picture a beach as a bank account that loses sand faster than rivers deposit it.","cn":"想象海滩是一本存沙的账，支出比河流存入更快。"},{"en":"Picture a coastline as a hem being slowly unstitched by the sea.","cn":"想象海岸线是一道被海水慢慢拆线的衣边。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Coastal erosion has removed half the dune in twenty years.","cn":"二十年间，海岸侵蚀削去了沙丘的一半。"},{"en":"Sea walls can slow coastal erosion but often shift it elsewhere.","cn":"海堤能减缓海岸侵蚀，却常把它转移到别处。"},{"en":"The report maps coastal erosion along the entire delta.","cn":"报告绘制了整个三角洲的海岸侵蚀分布。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「coastal（海岸的）+ erosion（侵蚀）」——海边被啃掉的过程 → 海岸侵蚀","word":"coastal erosion"},"root":"拉丁 costa「肋骨、侧边」→ 古法语 coste「岸」→ 英语 coast + -al → coastal；拉丁 e-「出」+ rodere「啃、啮」→ erodere「啃掉」→ erosio → 英语 erosion。costa 与 rodere 的更深来源均不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one wearing action: the general process, cliff retreat, beach loss, measured retreat, the sediment deficit, storm bursts, the hazard people suffer, and finally any slow attrition.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一「啃蚀」动作展开：总过程、崖壁后退、海滩流失、实测后退、沉积赤字、风暴突发、人们承受的灾害，最后引申为任何缓慢消磨。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: waves striking the same cliff foot over and over until the base is hollowed and the top collapses.","cn":"核心意象：波浪一遍遍撞向同一处崖脚，直到底部被掏空、顶部塌落。"},"chain":["GENERAL WEARING","CLIFF RETREAT","BEACH LOSS","SHORELINE SHIFT","SEDIMENT DEFICIT","STORM-DRIVEN LOSS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"PROCESS TO DAMAGE: a natural wearing becomes a category of risk once homes stand in its path.","cn":"从过程到灾害：一旦房屋挡在路上，自然磨损就变成风险类别。"},{"senses":"02 · 04","en":"VISIBLE TO MEASURED: the falling cliff is fixed on a baseline and becomes a rate of retreat.","cn":"从可见到可测：塌落的崖壁被固定在基线上，变成后退速率。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"SUPPLY AND LOSS: sand leaves faster than rivers and currents deliver it, so the beach narrows.","cn":"供给与流失：沙被带走快于河流与海流送来，海滩于是变窄。"},{"senses":"06","en":"EPISODIC DAMAGE: one storm can do the work of a decade.","cn":"突发损害：一场风暴能做十年的活。"},{"senses":"08","en":"ATTRITION METAPHOR: any edge can be worn away slowly, so the phrase lends itself to budgets and trust.","cn":"消磨比喻：任何边缘都能被慢慢磨掉，因此这个短语可借用于预算与信任。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Coastal erosion is built from two Latin-derived adjectives and nouns, so its morphology is unusually regular: locate with coastal, then name the action with erosion.","cn":"coastal erosion 由两个源自拉丁语的形容词与名词构成，形态异常规整：先用 coastal 定位，再用 erosion 命名动作。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Costa supplies coast and coastal; rodere supplies erode, erosion and erosive. The two Latin lines meet only in this modern phrase.","cn":"costa 提供 coast 与 coastal；rodere 提供 erode、erosion 与 erosive。两条拉丁线索只在这个近代短语里相遇。"},"items":[{"word":"coast","structure":"Latin costa via Old French coste","meaning":"the land beside the sea","meaningCN":"海旁的陆地","example":"The coast turns rocky north of the bay.","exampleCN":"海湾以北的海岸变得多岩。"},{"word":"-al","structure":"Latin -alis (adjective suffix)","meaning":"relating to","meaningCN":"与……有关的","example":"Coast plus -al gives coastal.","exampleCN":"coast 加 -al 得到 coastal。"},{"word":"coastal","structure":"coast + -al","meaning":"of or near the coast","meaningCN":"海岸的；沿海的","example":"Coastal roads flood at spring tides.","exampleCN":"沿海道路在大潮时被淹。"},{"word":"e-","structure":"Latin e- 'out' (variant of ex-)","meaning":"out, away","meaningCN":"向外；离开","example":"The prefix marks removal from the surface.","exampleCN":"这个前缀标记从表面移除。"},{"word":"rodere","structure":"Latin rodere 'to gnaw'","meaning":"to gnaw, eat into","meaningCN":"啃；啮入","example":"The root gives the image of biting.","exampleCN":"这个词根带来「咬」的意象。"},{"word":"erode","structure":"e- + rodere","meaning":"to wear away","meaningCN":"侵蚀；磨损","example":"Waves erode the softer beds first.","exampleCN":"波浪先侵蚀较软的岩层。"},{"word":"erosion","structure":"erodere + -ion (action noun)","meaning":"the act or result of wearing away","meaningCN":"侵蚀的动作或结果","example":"Erosion exposed the old foundation.","exampleCN":"侵蚀露出了旧地基。"},{"word":"erosive","structure":"erosion + -ive (tending to)","meaning":"having the power to wear away","meaningCN":"有侵蚀力的","example":"Fast water is highly erosive.","exampleCN":"急流具有很强的侵蚀力。"},{"word":"erosional","structure":"erosion + -al","meaning":"formed by erosion","meaningCN":"由侵蚀形成的","example":"An erosional notch marks the high-water line.","exampleCN":"一道侵蚀切口标出高水位线。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"costa","structure":"costa, costae (f., first declension)","meaning":"rib; side, flank","meaningCN":"肋骨；侧面"},{"word":"rodere","structure":"rodere, rosi, rosum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to gnaw, bite, eat into","meaningCN":"啃；咬；侵蚀"},{"word":"erosio","structure":"erosio, erosionis (f., third declension)","meaning":"a gnawing away, erosion","meaningCN":"啃蚀；侵蚀"}]}},{"word":"coastal zone","ipa_uk":"/ˌkəʊstl ˈzəʊn/","ipa_us":"/ˌkoʊstl ˈzoʊn/","definition_zh":"海岸带；沿海地带；潮间带及近岸水域；海岸开发区；海岸管理区","definition_en":"the belt of land and shallow sea where the coast meets the water, often defined for management","core_image":"一条从崖顶草坡延伸到浅海的窄带，滩面、盐沼与浅水并排铺开","scene":"规划员在潮间带的木桩上系了标记绳，把从最高潮线到浅海的带状区域量进图纸。The new rules protect the coastal zone from unchecked construction.","sceneCN":"这里指「陆地与海洋交界的带状区域」（第 1 个义项：从受潮汐与海浪影响的陆地一直延伸到近岸浅海的空间带）；句意是新规保护海岸带免受无序建设侵蚀。场景物件：木桩、标记绳、潮线、图纸。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"海岸带；沿海地带（可数；复数 coastal zones）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"coastal zone management","zh":"海岸带管理"},{"phrase":"integrated coastal zone management","zh":"海岸带综合管理"},{"phrase":"the coastal zone of a delta","zh":"三角洲的海岸带"},{"phrase":"coastal zone development","zh":"海岸带开发"},{"phrase":"coastal zone protection","zh":"海岸带保护"},{"phrase":"a coastal zone boundary","zh":"海岸带边界"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"coastal zones"},{"label":"定语形式（海岸带的）","form":"coastal-zone"},{"label":"相关名词（海岸）","form":"coast"},{"label":"相关形容词（海岸的）","form":"coastal"},{"label":"相关名词（地带）","form":"zone"},{"label":"相关名词（分区规划）","form":"zoning"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"coast","pos":"n./v.","zh":"海岸；沿海航行"},{"word":"coastal","pos":"adj.","zh":"海岸的；沿海的"},{"word":"zone","pos":"n./v.","zh":"地带；划分区域"},{"word":"zoning","pos":"n.","zh":"分区；分区规划"},{"word":"zonation","pos":"n.","zh":"成带分布；分带"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The land-sea strip","titleCN":"陆海交界的带状区域","definition":"the belt of land and shallow sea where the coast meets the water","definitionCN":"陆地与浅海相接、海岸临水的那条地带","example":"The new rules protect the coastal zone from unchecked construction.","exampleCN":"新规保护海岸带免受无序建设侵蚀。","why":"Zone names a belt with recognized limits, and coastal fixes one end at the water, so the phrase is the edge treated as an area rather than a line.","whyCN":"zone 指有可辨边界的地带，coastal 把一端固定在水中，因此这个短语把边缘当作一片区域而不是一条线。"},{"no":"02","title":"The tidal reach","titleCN":"受潮汐影响的岸段","definition":"the part of the coast reached by tides, from the high-water mark to the shallow nearshore","definitionCN":"从高潮线到近岸浅水、受潮汐作用的海岸部分","example":"Salt marshes and mudflats share the same coastal zone.","exampleCN":"盐沼与泥滩处在同一条海岸带上。","why":"Tides draw a natural boundary twice a day, so the phrase often narrows to the reach that water actually covers.","whyCN":"潮汐每天两次画出天然边界，因此这个短语常收窄到海水实际覆盖的那一段。"},{"no":"03","title":"An ecological ecotone","titleCN":"生态过渡带","definition":"the transition belt where marine, freshwater and terrestrial habitats overlap","definitionCN":"海洋、淡水与陆地生境相互重叠的过渡地带","example":"Migratory birds depend on the coastal zone as a staging ground.","exampleCN":"候鸟依赖海岸带作为中途停歇地。","why":"Ecologists saw that the strip is neither sea nor land but a meeting place, so the phrase became a name for an ecotone.","whyCN":"生态学家看出这条带既非海也非陆，而是交汇处，于是这个短语成了生态过渡带的名称。"},{"no":"04","title":"A legal management zone","titleCN":"法定管理区","definition":"an area defined by statute for permits, setbacks and coastal planning","definitionCN":"为许可、退让线与海岸规划而由法规划定的区域","example":"The coastal zone boundary lies fifty metres inland of the dune crest.","exampleCN":"海岸带边界位于沙丘脊线向内五十米处。","why":"Governments needed a mapped limit, so the ecological strip was given a legal boundary and became an administrative zone.","whyCN":"政府需要一条图上界线，于是生态地带被赋予法定边界，成为行政分区。"},{"no":"05","title":"A development corridor","titleCN":"沿海开发带","definition":"the settled and built-up strip used for ports, tourism and industry","definitionCN":"用于港口、旅游与产业的聚居与建设地带","example":"Hotels and marinas now line much of the coastal zone.","exampleCN":"旅馆与游艇码头如今排满了海岸带的大部分。","why":"Because people want to be near the water, the same belt became an economic corridor, and the phrase followed the money.","whyCN":"因为人们愿意靠近水，同一条带就成了经济走廊，短语也随之跟着资金走。"},{"no":"06","title":"The settled coastal belt","titleCN":"沿海聚居带","definition":"the densely populated strip in which most coastal towns and roads sit","definitionCN":"沿海城镇与道路密集分布的居住地带","example":"Most of the country's population lives in the coastal zone.","exampleCN":"该国大部分人口住在海岸带。","why":"Statistics treat the strip as a demographic unit, so the phrase can mean the belt where people actually live.","whyCN":"统计把这条带当作人口单元，因此这个短语也可指人们实际居住的地带。"},{"no":"07","title":"A geomorphic unit","titleCN":"地貌单元","definition":"a landform system of beach, dune, cliff, marsh and nearshore shelf","definitionCN":"由海滩、沙丘、崖壁、盐沼与近岸陆架构成的地貌系统","example":"Each coastal zone has its own balance of erosion and deposition.","exampleCN":"每个海岸带都有自己的侵蚀与沉积平衡。","why":"Geomorphologists group the features that share sediment, so the phrase names a process-linked landform unit.","whyCN":"地貌学家把共享沉积物的要素归在一起，因此这个短语指一个与过程相连的地貌单元。"},{"no":"08","title":"Figurative interface","titleCN":"比喻义：交界与接口","definition":"any boundary area where two systems meet and exchange","definitionCN":"任何两个系统相遇并交换物质的边界区域","example":"The workshop became a coastal zone between research and policy.","exampleCN":"这场研讨会成了研究与政策之间的「海岸带」。","why":"Once the strip is understood as an interface, it can describe any place where two worlds trade, not only land and sea.","whyCN":"一旦这条带被理解为接口，它就能描述任何两个世界互相交换的地方，而不只陆与海。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Coastal zone joins Latin costa 'rib, side' to Latin zona 'belt' from Greek zōnē. The compound is a twentieth-century planning term. Dates are approximate.","cn":"coastal zone 把拉丁 costa「肋骨、侧边」与拉丁 zona「带」并置，后者出自希腊 zōnē。这个复合词是二十世纪的规划术语。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK ZONE","en":"Greek zōnē meant a belt or girdle, and geographers used it for the climatic belts of the globe.","cn":"希腊 zōnē 指腰带或束带，地理学家用它指地球上的气候带。"},{"era":"LATIN ZONA","en":"Latin borrowed the Greek word as zona and kept both the belt sense and the geographic sense.","cn":"拉丁语借入希腊词作 zona，同时保留腰带义与地理带义。"},{"era":"LATIN COSTA","en":"Costa 'rib, side' gave Old French coste and English coast; the adjective coastal followed with the Latin suffix -alis.","cn":"costa「肋骨、侧边」形成古法语 coste 与英语 coast；形容词 coastal 随后加上拉丁后缀 -alis。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ZONE","en":"English zone first meant a belt on a map, then any area marked off for a purpose, such as a military or customs zone.","cn":"英语 zone 最初指地图上的一条带，随后指为某种目的划出的任何区域，如军事区或关税区。"},{"era":"THE PHRASE","en":"Coastal zone became common after mid-century coastal management laws, which required states to define the strip they would regulate.","cn":"二十世纪中叶海岸管理立法要求各州划定自己要监管的地带之后，coastal zone 开始通行。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin and first date): the pre-Latin source of costa is unknown, the pre-Greek source of zōnē is uncertain, and the first printed use of the English phrase is not precisely dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源与首见年代）：costa 在拉丁语之前的来源不明，zōnē 的前希腊语来源不确定，英语短语最早的印刷记录也没有确切年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds same-root belt and coast words that are easily swapped; group two holds other shore strips defined by different processes.","cn":"第一组是同根、容易被替换的「带」与「岸」相关词；第二组是按不同过程划分的其他岸边地带。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"coast","ipa":"/kəʊst/","tag":"the line or land edge","definition":"The land beside the sea, often thought of as a line; a coastal zone is the broader belt on both sides of that line.","definitionCN":"海旁的陆地，常被想成一条线；coastal zone 是这条线两侧更宽的地带。"},{"word":"coastal","ipa":"/ˈkəʊstl/","tag":"adjective only","definition":"Relating to the coast; it needs a noun such as zone or town and cannot stand for the area by itself.","definitionCN":"与海岸有关的形容词；它需要 zone、town 等名词，不能独自指那片区域。"},{"word":"zone","ipa":"/zəʊn/","tag":"general belt","definition":"Any area marked off for a purpose; coastal zone limits the purpose to the shore.","definitionCN":"为某种目的划出的任何区域；coastal zone 把目的限定到海岸。"},{"word":"zoning","ipa":"/ˈzəʊnɪŋ/","tag":"the regulation, not the area","definition":"The legal practice of dividing land into use districts; it acts on the coastal zone but is not the zone itself.","definitionCN":"把土地划为用途分区的法律实践；它作用于海岸带，却不是海岸带本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"shoreline","ipa":"/ˈʃɔːlaɪn/","tag":"the waterline","definition":"The line where water meets land; it is the inner edge of the coastal zone, not the whole belt.","definitionCN":"水与陆相接的线；它是海岸带的内缘，而不是整条带。"},{"word":"littoral","ipa":"/lɪˈtɒrəl/","tag":"the shallow-water shore","definition":"The zone between high and low water and the shallow sea beyond it; it is more strictly tidal than the planning term.","definitionCN":"高潮线与低潮线之间及以外浅海的区域；它比规划术语更严格地限于潮汐范围。"},{"word":"riparian zone","ipa":"/rɪˈpeəriən zəʊn/","tag":"river edge, different root","definition":"The belt along a river; it shares the belt idea but not the coastal setting, and its root is Latin ripa 'bank'.","definitionCN":"沿河的带状地带；它与「带」的观念相同，却不是海岸环境，词根是拉丁 ripa「河岸」。"},{"word":"exclusive economic zone","ipa":"/ɪkˈskluːsɪv ɪˌkɒnəmɪk zəʊn/","tag":"offshore legal waters","definition":"The sea area extending two hundred nautical miles from the coast; it is a maritime jurisdiction, not the land-sea strip.","definitionCN":"从海岸向外延伸二百海里的海域；它是海洋管辖范围，不是陆海交界带。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real Greek and Latin parts, real planning collocations and real relatives.","cn":"正常联想：真实的希腊与拉丁构件、真实规划搭配与真实同族词。"},"normal":[{"en":"Zone comes from Greek zōnē, a belt, and geographers still use it for belts of climate.","cn":"zone 出自希腊 zōnē「带」，地理学家至今用它指气候带。"},{"en":"Coastal says where; zone says it is a belt with limits.","cn":"coastal 说明在哪里，zone 说明它是一条有边界的带。"},{"en":"Coastal zone management is the standard policy phrase for the strip.","cn":"海岸带管理是这条带的标准政策说法。"},{"en":"The zone runs from the dune crest through the beach into the shallow sea.","cn":"这条带从沙丘脊线穿过海滩，一直伸进浅海。"},{"en":"The same belt is habitat, jurisdiction and building land at once.","cn":"同一条带同时是生境、管辖范围与建设用地。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a ribbon laid over the coast, one half on land and one half in water.","cn":"想象一条缎带铺在海岸上，一半在陆地，一半在水里。"},{"en":"Picture a meeting room where the sea and the land negotiate through tides.","cn":"想象一间会议室，海与陆通过潮汐谈判。"},{"en":"Picture a legal line drawn in the sand that the tide ignores twice a day.","cn":"想象沙上画出的法定界线，而潮汐每天两次无视它。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Integrated coastal zone management brings agencies to one table.","cn":"海岸带综合管理把各机构拉到同一张桌前。"},{"en":"The coastal zone supports both fisheries and tourism.","cn":"海岸带同时支撑渔业与旅游业。"},{"en":"Rising seas are squeezing the coastal zone from both sides.","cn":"上升的海面从两侧挤压海岸带。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「coastal（海岸的）+ zone（带）」——沿着海岸划出的一条带 → 海岸带","word":"coastal zone"},"root":"拉丁 costa「肋骨、侧边」→ 古法语 coste「岸」→ 英语 coast + -al → coastal；拉丁 zona「带」← 希腊 zōnē「腰带」。两词在二十世纪海岸管理立法中合为 coastal zone。costa 与 zōnē 的更深来源均不确定。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one belt: a physical strip, a tidal reach, an ecotone, a legal zone, a development corridor, a settled belt, a landform unit, and finally any interface between two systems.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一条「带」展开：物理地带、潮汐岸段、生态过渡带、法定管理区、开发走廊、聚居带、地貌单元，最后引申为任何两个系统之间的接口。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a narrow ribbon from the dune crest to the shallow sea, with beach, marsh and water laid side by side.","cn":"核心意象：一条从沙丘脊线延伸到浅海的窄带，海滩、盐沼与浅水并排铺开。"},"chain":["LAND-SEA STRIP","TIDAL REACH","ECOLOGICAL ECOTONE","LEGAL ZONE","DEVELOPMENT BELT","INTERFACE METAPHOR"],"branches":[{"senses":"02 · 03","en":"TIDE CREATES HABITAT: daily flooding mixes salt and fresh water and makes the strip an ecotone.","cn":"潮汐造出生境：每日淹水混合盐淡水，使这条带成为生态过渡带。"},{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"GEOMORPHOLOGY: beach, dune, cliff and marsh form one sediment-linked landform system.","cn":"地貌系统：海滩、沙丘、崖壁与盐沼组成一个共享沉积物的地貌体系。"},{"senses":"04 · 05","en":"LAW ENABLES DEVELOPMENT: a mapped boundary makes permits, setbacks and ports possible.","cn":"法律促成开发：画定的边界使许可、退让线与港口成为可能。"},{"senses":"06","en":"PEOPLE AND ECONOMY: the settled belt is a market in its own right.","cn":"人口与经济：这条聚居带本身就是一片市场。"},{"senses":"08","en":"INTERFACE METAPHOR: any meeting place of two systems can borrow the coastal image.","cn":"接口比喻：任何两个系统的交汇处都能借用海岸的意象。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Coastal zone is a two-part technical compound: an adjective of place plus a noun of bounded area. Both parts are borrowed, but both are fully productive in English.","cn":"coastal zone 是两部分构成的技术复合词：一个表示地点的形容词，加一个表示有界区域的名词。两部分都是借词，但在英语中都能产。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Costa gives coast and coastal; zona gives zone, zoning and zonation. The Greek belt word reached English through Latin, so the Latin layer carries it.","cn":"costa 提供 coast 与 coastal；zona 提供 zone、zoning 与 zonation。希腊的「带」词经拉丁进入英语，因此由拉丁层承载。"},"items":[{"word":"coast","structure":"Latin costa via Old French coste","meaning":"land beside the sea","meaningCN":"海旁的陆地","example":"The coast is low and sandy here.","exampleCN":"这里的海岸低平多沙。"},{"word":"coastal","structure":"coast + -al","meaning":"of the coast","meaningCN":"海岸的","example":"Coastal wetlands filter river water.","exampleCN":"沿海湿地过滤河水。"},{"word":"zone","structure":"Latin zona from Greek zōnē 'belt'","meaning":"a belt or bounded area","meaningCN":"带；有界区域","example":"The map marks a flood zone.","exampleCN":"地图标出一片洪泛区。"},{"word":"zoning","structure":"zone + -ing (action noun)","meaning":"division of land into use districts","meaningCN":"把土地划分为用途分区","example":"Zoning keeps industry off the dune.","exampleCN":"分区规划让工业远离沙丘。"},{"word":"zonation","structure":"zone + -ation (state or arrangement)","meaning":"arrangement in belts","meaningCN":"成带排列","example":"Zonation is clear on rocky shores.","exampleCN":"岩岸上的成带分布很清楚。"},{"word":"coastal zone","structure":"coastal + zone (compound noun)","meaning":"the land-sea belt","meaningCN":"陆海交界带","example":"The coastal zone is mapped every decade.","exampleCN":"海岸带每十年重绘一次。"},{"word":"coastal-zone","structure":"compound used attributively","meaning":"relating to the coastal belt","meaningCN":"海岸带的","example":"Coastal-zone rules limit new hotels.","exampleCN":"海岸带规定限制新建旅馆。"},{"word":"nearshore","structure":"near + shore (compound)","meaning":"the shallow water close to the shore","meaningCN":"近岸浅水","example":"Nearshore currents move the sand.","exampleCN":"近岸海流搬运沙粒。"},{"word":"setback","structure":"set + back (compound noun)","meaning":"a required distance from the water","meaningCN":"规定的退让距离","example":"A setback keeps houses off the active beach.","exampleCN":"退让线让房屋避开活动海滩。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"costa","structure":"costa, costae (f., first declension)","meaning":"rib; side, flank","meaningCN":"肋骨；侧面"},{"word":"zona","structure":"zona, zonae (f., first declension; from Greek zōnē)","meaning":"belt, girdle; climatic belt","meaningCN":"带；腰带；气候带"}]}},{"word":"salt marsh","ipa_uk":"/sælt mɑːʃ/","ipa_us":"/sælt mɑːrʃ/","definition_zh":"盐沼；盐沼湿地；沿海盐生草甸；潮间带盐沼生境；盐沼泥炭地","definition_en":"a low grassy coastal wetland flooded by salt water at high tide and drained by creeks at low tide","core_image":"一片被潮沟切成叶脉状的草地，草茎上结着白色盐霜","scene":"退潮后的滩面上，草茎被盐水染成灰绿，潮沟像叶脉一样分开草地。At high tide the salt marsh becomes a shallow sheet of silver water.","sceneCN":"这里指「受潮汐周期性淹没的盐生草甸」（第 1 个义项：生长耐盐草本植物、由潮沟切割的沿海低平地）；句意为涨潮时盐沼变成一片浅浅的银色水面。场景物件：草茎、潮沟、盐霜、浅水。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"盐沼；盐沼湿地（可数；复数 salt marshes）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a tidal salt marsh","zh":"潮汐盐沼"},{"phrase":"salt marsh vegetation","zh":"盐沼植被"},{"phrase":"salt marsh restoration","zh":"盐沼修复"},{"phrase":"salt marsh peat","zh":"盐沼泥炭"},{"phrase":"salt marsh cordgrass","zh":"盐沼米草"},{"phrase":"the salt marsh edge","zh":"盐沼边缘"},{"phrase":"salt marsh loss","zh":"盐沼丧失"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"salt marshes"},{"label":"拼写变体（合写形式）","form":"saltmarsh"},{"label":"定语形式（盐沼的）","form":"salt-marsh"},{"label":"相关名词（沼泽）","form":"marsh"},{"label":"相关名词（盐）","form":"salt"},{"label":"相关形容词（耐盐的）","form":"halophytic"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"salt","pos":"n./v./adj.","zh":"盐；加盐；咸的"},{"word":"marsh","pos":"n.","zh":"沼泽；湿地"},{"word":"marshy","pos":"adj.","zh":"沼泽的；湿软的"},{"word":"saltmarsh","pos":"n.","zh":"盐沼（合写形式）"},{"word":"halophyte","pos":"n.","zh":"耐盐植物"},{"word":"halophytic","pos":"adj.","zh":"耐盐的；盐生的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A tidal grassy wetland","titleCN":"潮汐盐生草甸","definition":"a low grassy coastal wetland flooded by salt water at high tide and drained by creeks at low tide","definitionCN":"高潮被咸水淹没、低潮由潮沟排干的沿海低平草地","example":"At high tide the salt marsh becomes a shallow sheet of silver water.","exampleCN":"涨潮时盐沼变成一片浅浅的银色水面。","why":"Salt names the water and marsh names the soft wet ground, so the compound is exactly the wet ground that salt water visits.","whyCN":"salt 指咸水，marsh 指湿软的地，复合词正是咸水会到访的那片湿地。"},{"no":"02","title":"The habitat of halophytes","titleCN":"耐盐植物的生境","definition":"the intertidal habitat in which salt-tolerant grasses and herbs dominate","definitionCN":"耐盐禾草与草本占优势的潮间带生境","example":"Only a few grasses can survive in the salt marsh.","exampleCN":"只有少数几种禾草能在盐沼里存活。","why":"Ecologists name habitats by their dominant life forms, so the phrase became a habitat type defined by salt-tolerant plants.","whyCN":"生态学家按优势生命形式命名生境，因此这个短语成了由耐盐植物定义的生境类型。"},{"no":"03","title":"The plant community","titleCN":"盐沼植物群落","definition":"the assemblage of cordgrass, sedges and succulents that covers the marsh surface","definitionCN":"覆盖沼面的米草、薹草与肉质植物组合","example":"The salt marsh is bright green in early summer.","exampleCN":"初夏时盐沼一片鲜绿。","why":"When the emphasis falls on the plants rather than the ground, the same phrase names the community standing on it.","whyCN":"当重点落在植物而不是地面时，同一个短语就指站在其上的群落。"},{"no":"04","title":"Salt marsh soil and peat","titleCN":"盐沼土壤与泥炭","definition":"the waterlogged, organic-rich soil or peat built up by marsh plants","definitionCN":"由盐沼植物积累起来的饱水、富含有机质的土壤或泥炭","example":"Cores show a metre of salt marsh peat below the sand.","exampleCN":"岩芯显示沙层之下有一米厚的盐沼泥炭。","why":"Because marsh plants leave layers behind, the phrase can name the ground substance they build, not just the surface.","whyCN":"因为盐沼植物会留下层积，这个短语也能指它们构建的地面物质，而不只是表面。"},{"no":"05","title":"A blue-carbon store","titleCN":"蓝碳储库","definition":"the carbon held in salt-marsh plants and peat, counted as a coastal carbon sink","definitionCN":"储存在盐沼植物与泥炭中的碳，被计为沿海碳汇","example":"Restoring the salt marsh would lock carbon into the ground.","exampleCN":"修复盐沼会把碳锁进地里。","why":"Climate policy needed a name for the carbon banked in coastal wetlands, and the habitat itself supplied it.","whyCN":"气候政策需要给沿海湿地存下的碳一个名称，这个生境本身就成了名称。"},{"no":"06","title":"A natural flood buffer","titleCN":"天然防洪缓冲带","definition":"the marsh surface and vegetation that absorb wave energy and reduce flooding","definitionCN":"吸收波浪能量、减轻洪水的沼面与植被","example":"The salt marsh shielded the village from the storm surge.","exampleCN":"盐沼挡住了风暴潮，护住了村庄。","why":"Engineers measured how much the marsh slows water, so the phrase also names a piece of natural defence.","whyCN":"工程师测量盐沼让水减速的程度，因此这个短语也指一道天然防线。"},{"no":"07","title":"Land fought over for reclamation","titleCN":"围垦争议中的土地","definition":"the marsh as a contested land bank that farmers and developers wish to drain","definitionCN":"作为被农民与开发商希望排干的有争议土地储备的盐沼","example":"Centuries of reclamation removed half of the salt marsh.","exampleCN":"数百年的围垦削去了盐沼的一半。","why":"Where land is scarce, the wet marsh is seen as wasted ground, so the phrase carries a land-use conflict.","whyCN":"在土地稀缺之处，湿润的盐沼被视为荒地，于是这个短语带上土地利用冲突。"},{"no":"08","title":"A classified wetland type","titleCN":"湿地分类术语","definition":"a formal category in wetland inventories and conservation law","definitionCN":"湿地名录与保护法规中的正式类别","example":"The site is listed as salt marsh in the national inventory.","exampleCN":"该地在国家名录中被列为盐沼。","why":"A management system needs stable categories, so the descriptive phrase became a legal wetland type.","whyCN":"管理系统需要稳定的类别，于是描述性短语成了法定湿地类型。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Salt marsh joins two native English words: salt from Old English sealt, and marsh from Old English merisc, a watery lowland. The compound is old in shape but technical in its modern use. Dates are approximate.","cn":"salt marsh 由两个英语本族词组成：salt 出自古英语 sealt，marsh 出自古英语 merisc「水浸低地」。这个复合形式很古老，现代用法却属技术术语。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH SEALT","en":"Sealt 'salt' descends from Germanic *saltaz, a reconstructed form related to Latin sal and Greek hals.","cn":"sealt「盐」出自日耳曼语 *saltaz，此为重构形式，与拉丁 sal、希腊 hals 同源。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH MERISC","en":"Merisc or mersc 'marsh' was built on mere 'sea, lake' plus a suffix -isc; it named wet, low, grassy ground.","cn":"merisc 或 mersc「沼泽」由 mere「海、湖」加后缀 -isc 构成，指湿软低平的草地。"},{"era":"GERMANIC AND LATIN KIN","en":"Mere belongs to the same old water-word family as Latin mare 'sea'; the two are distant cousins through a reconstructed root *mori-, not loanwords.","cn":"mere 与拉丁 mare「海」同属古老的「水」词族；两者通过重构词根 *mori- 成为远亲，并非借词关系。"},{"era":"MIDDLE ENGLISH","en":"Middle English kept both salt and mersh, and the collocation salt mersh named grassy ground reached by the tide.","cn":"中古英语同时保留 salt 与 mersh，salt mersh 这一搭配指受潮水到达的草地。"},{"era":"MODERN TECHNICAL USE","en":"In twentieth-century ecology the compound became a precise habitat class, distinguished from freshwater marsh and from mangrove swamp.","cn":"到二十世纪生态学，这个复合词成为精确的生境类别，与淡水沼泽及红树林沼泽区分开。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin): the pre-Germanic source of *saltaz is not settled, the reconstructed *mori- is a scholarly reconstruction, and the first technical use of the English compound is not exactly dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源）：*saltaz 在日耳曼语之前的来源无定论，*mori- 属学术重构，英语复合词最早的技术用法也没有确切年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds same-root or near-spelled marsh words; group two holds other coastal wetlands that differ by salinity, tide or vegetation.","cn":"第一组是同根或拼写相近的沼泽词；第二组是按盐度、潮汐或植被区分的其他沿海湿地。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"marsh","ipa":"/mɑːʃ/","tag":"the general wet ground","definition":"Any low wet grassy land; salt marsh specifies that the water is tidal and salty.","definitionCN":"任何低湿的草地；salt marsh 限定水是潮汐带来的咸水。"},{"word":"marshy","ipa":"/ˈmɑːʃi/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Describing ground that is soft and wet; it cannot name the coastal habitat as a category.","definitionCN":"描述地面湿软；它不能作为类别命名这种沿海生境。"},{"word":"saltmarsh","ipa":"/ˈsæltmɑːʃ/","tag":"spelling variant","definition":"The same habitat written as one word; the two-word form is the standard scientific spelling.","definitionCN":"同一生境的合写形式；分写形式是标准科学拼法。"},{"word":"saltwater","ipa":"/ˈsæltwɔːtə/","tag":"the water, not the land","definition":"Water containing salt, especially seawater; it describes the water that floods the marsh, not the marsh itself.","definitionCN":"含盐的水，尤指海水；它描述淹没盐沼的水，而不是盐沼本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"freshwater marsh","ipa":"/ˈfreʃwɔːtə mɑːʃ/","tag":"same form, different salinity","definition":"A marsh fed by rain and rivers rather than tides; it shares the marsh shape but lacks salt and tidal flushing.","definitionCN":"由雨水与河流而非潮汐补给的沼泽；形状相同，却没有盐分与潮汐冲刷。"},{"word":"mudflat","ipa":"/ˈmʌdflæt/","tag":"bare sediment, no grass","definition":"A bare tidal flat of mud; it often lies below the salt marsh and has little vegetation.","definitionCN":"裸露的潮汐泥滩；常位于盐沼下方，植被很少。"},{"word":"mangrove swamp","ipa":"/ˈmæŋɡrəʊv swɒmp/","tag":"tropical woody equivalent","definition":"A tidal wetland dominated by mangrove trees; salt marsh is its temperate grassy counterpart.","definitionCN":"以红树为主的潮汐湿地；盐沼是它在温带的草本对应物。"},{"word":"salt pan","ipa":"/sælt pæn/","tag":"dry salt crust","definition":"A shallow basin where water evaporates and leaves salt; it is too salty for marsh grasses.","definitionCN":"水蒸发后留下盐的浅盆；盐分过高，长不了盐沼草。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real Old English parts, real ecological collocations and real relatives.","cn":"正常联想：真实的古英语构件、真实生态搭配与真实同族词。"},"normal":[{"en":"Salt is sealt in Old English; marsh is merisc, a wet lowland.","cn":"salt 在古英语是 sealt；marsh 是 merisc，即湿低地。"},{"en":"Salt marsh is the grassy wetland the tide floods and drains.","cn":"盐沼就是潮水灌入又排干的草地湿地。"},{"en":"Cordgrass is the signature plant of many salt marshes.","cn":"米草是许多盐沼的标志植物。"},{"en":"The marsh builds peat, and the peat stores blue carbon.","cn":"盐沼积累泥炭，泥炭储存蓝碳。"},{"en":"Marsh and Latin mare are distant cousins, not borrowed twins.","cn":"marsh 与拉丁 mare 是远亲，不是借来的双胞胎。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a green carpet that the sea lifts and lowers twice a day.","cn":"想象一块绿毯，海每天把它托起又放下两次。"},{"en":"Picture a sponge of peat and grass holding carbon and softening waves.","cn":"想象一块泥炭与草构成的海绵，既存碳又软化波浪。"},{"en":"Picture white salt lines on green stems after the water pulls back.","cn":"想象水退后，绿色茎秆上留下的白色盐线。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The salt marsh absorbs the first metre of the storm surge.","cn":"盐沼吸收了风暴潮最初的一米水头。"},{"en":"A single salt marsh can store carbon for centuries.","cn":"一片盐沼能把碳储存数百年。"},{"en":"Draining the salt marsh destroyed the nursery for juvenile fish.","cn":"排干盐沼毁掉了幼鱼的育幼场。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「salt（盐）+ marsh（沼泽）」——被咸水淹的沼泽草地 → 盐沼","word":"salt marsh"},"root":"salt 出自古英语 sealt「盐」，属日耳曼语 *saltaz（重构形式），与拉丁 sal 同源；marsh 出自古英语 merisc「沼泽」，由 mere「海、湖」加 -isc 构成，mere 与拉丁 mare「海」经重构词根 *mori- 为远亲。英语复合词 salt marsh。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one wet meadow: a tidal grassy wetland, a halophyte habitat, a plant community, its peat, a carbon store, a flood buffer, a reclaimed land bank, and a legal wetland class.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一片湿草地展开：潮汐草甸、耐盐生境、植物群落、泥炭、碳库、防洪缓冲、围垦地储备，最后是法定湿地类别。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a flat meadow cut by tidal creeks, its stems whitened by salt after the water pulls back.","cn":"核心意象：一片被潮沟切开的平坦草甸，水退后草茎上泛着白色盐霜。"},"chain":["TIDAL GRASSY WETLAND","HALOPHYTE HABITAT","PLANT COMMUNITY","PEAT AND SOIL","BLUE-CARBON STORE","FLOOD BUFFER"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"SALT SELECTS PLANTS: only halophytes can live where every tide brings salt.","cn":"盐分筛选植物：只有耐盐植物能活在每次潮水都带盐的地方。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"PLANTS BUILD GROUND: stems die back each year and their remains become peat.","cn":"植物造地：茎秆每年枯落，残余物变成泥炭。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE CARBON STORE: waterlogged layers slow decay, so the marsh holds carbon.","cn":"碳储库：饱水层减慢分解，盐沼因此存住碳。"},{"senses":"06","en":"THE BUFFER: rough surface and dense stems take energy out of waves and surge.","cn":"缓冲带：粗糙的沼面与密集茎秆从波浪和风暴潮中抽走能量。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"CONFLICT TO CATEGORY: land hunger made the marsh contested, and law then fixed it as a protected class.","cn":"从争议到类别：对土地的渴求使盐沼成为争夺对象，法律随后把它定为受保护类别。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Salt marsh is a native English compound of two free words, so there is no hidden affix to decode; the interest lies in how two simple nouns make a precise habitat.","cn":"salt marsh 是由两个自由词构成的英语本族复合词，没有隐蔽的词缀可拆；值得注意的是两个简单名词如何构成一个精确的生境名。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin layer appears only through distant relatives such as mare 'sea' and sal 'salt'; neither word is borrowed from Latin.","cn":"拉丁层只通过 mare「海」与 sal「盐」这样的远亲出现；两个词都不是从拉丁语借入的。"},"items":[{"word":"salt","structure":"Old English sealt (noun and adjective)","meaning":"sodium chloride; salty","meaningCN":"盐；咸的","example":"Salt burns the edges of the leaves.","exampleCN":"盐烧焦叶缘。"},{"word":"marsh","structure":"Old English merisc 'wet lowland'","meaning":"low wet grassy ground","meaningCN":"低湿的草地","example":"The marsh holds water after rain.","exampleCN":"雨后沼泽存住水。"},{"word":"marshy","structure":"marsh + -y (adjective suffix)","meaning":"wet and soft like a marsh","meaningCN":"像沼泽一样湿软的","example":"The marshy field sank underfoot.","exampleCN":"湿软的地在脚下下陷。"},{"word":"salt marsh","structure":"salt + marsh (compound noun)","meaning":"tidal salt-water meadow","meaningCN":"受潮汐咸水淹没的草甸","example":"The salt marsh floods every spring tide.","exampleCN":"每次大潮盐沼都被淹。"},{"word":"salt-marsh","structure":"compound used attributively","meaning":"of the salt marsh","meaningCN":"盐沼的","example":"Salt-marsh peat is dark and fibrous.","exampleCN":"盐沼泥炭色深而多纤维。"},{"word":"saltmarsh","structure":"closed compound variant","meaning":"the same habitat","meaningCN":"同一生境","example":"The saltmarsh survey began at dawn.","exampleCN":"盐沼调查在黎明开始。"},{"word":"halophyte","structure":"Greek hals 'salt' + phyton 'plant'","meaning":"a salt-tolerant plant","meaningCN":"耐盐植物","example":"Halophytes regulate salt in their tissue.","exampleCN":"耐盐植物调节组织中的盐分。"},{"word":"cordgrass","structure":"cord + grass (compound)","meaning":"the dominant grass of many salt marshes","meaningCN":"许多盐沼的优势草种","example":"Cordgrass traps sediment and raises the marsh.","exampleCN":"米草截住沉积物，把盐沼抬高。"},{"word":"tidal creek","structure":"tidal + creek (compound)","meaning":"a channel drained by the tide","meaningCN":"由潮汐排水的潮沟","example":"A tidal creek cuts the marsh into islands.","exampleCN":"潮沟把盐沼切成小岛。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"mangrove","ipa_uk":"/ˈmæŋɡrəʊv/","ipa_us":"/ˈmæŋɡroʊv/","definition_zh":"红树；红树植物；红树类乔木或灌木；红树林群落中的单株","definition_en":"a tree or shrub that grows in tidal salt water and is supported by aerial roots","core_image":"一棵树站在浅滩上，支柱根像高跷一样插进泥里，枝头挂着长条形的胎生苗","scene":"护林员划着小船穿过露出水面的支柱根，苗圃里挂着尚未落下的长形胚轴。Each mangrove holds the mud in place with roots that reach the water like stilts.","sceneCN":"这里指「生长在潮间带咸水中的红树植株」（第 1 个义项：以支柱根或呼吸根立于泥滩、耐盐的乔木或灌木）；句意为每一株红树都用像高跷一样伸进水里的根把泥沙固定住。场景物件：支柱根、小船、泥滩、枝头的胎生苗。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"红树；红树植物（可数；复数 mangroves）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a mangrove tree","zh":"一株红树"},{"phrase":"mangrove roots","zh":"红树根系"},{"phrase":"mangrove species","zh":"红树物种"},{"phrase":"mangrove seedling","zh":"红树幼苗"},{"phrase":"mangrove swamp","zh":"红树沼泽"},{"phrase":"mangrove ecosystem","zh":"红树林生态系统"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"mangroves"},{"label":"定语形式（红树的）","form":"mangrove"},{"label":"集合名词（红树林片）","form":"mangrove stand"},{"label":"相关名词（红树林）","form":"mangrove forest"},{"label":"生态学术语（红树林群落）","form":"mangal"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"mangroves","pos":"n.","zh":"红树（复数）"},{"word":"mangrove forest","pos":"n.","zh":"红树林"},{"word":"mangrove swamp","pos":"n.","zh":"红树沼泽"},{"word":"mangal","pos":"n.","zh":"红树林群落"},{"word":"mangrove-dependent","pos":"adj.","zh":"依赖红树林的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The tree itself","titleCN":"红树植株","definition":"a tree or shrub that grows in tidal salt water and is supported by aerial roots","definitionCN":"生长在潮间带咸水中、由气生根支撑的乔木或灌木","example":"Each mangrove holds the mud in place with roots that reach the water like stilts.","exampleCN":"每一株红树都用像高跷一样伸进水里的根把泥沙固定住。","why":"The word names the plant first, not the forest; its identity is settled by where it stands and how it is rooted.","whyCN":"这个词首先命名植株而不是森林；它的身份由站立之处与扎根方式决定。"},{"no":"02","title":"A stand of mangroves","titleCN":"成片红树","definition":"a group of mangrove trees growing together on a tidal flat","definitionCN":"在潮滩上成片生长的红树植株","example":"A narrow mangrove fringes the channel at low tide.","exampleCN":"低潮时一条窄窄的红树带镶在水道边。","why":"Because the trees grow in dense stands, the plural and the collective use slide from individual plants to the group.","whyCN":"因为红树成片密生，复数与集合用法便从单株滑向整片。"},{"no":"03","title":"The taxonomic group","titleCN":"红树类群","definition":"the several unrelated plant families that have evolved the mangrove habit","definitionCN":"若干各自演化出红树习性的、并不近缘的植物科","example":"Botanists list dozens of mangrove species across several families.","exampleCN":"植物学家在数个科中列出数十种红树。","why":"The habitat keeps producing the same growth form in different lineages, so the word also names a functional group rather than one family.","whyCN":"同一生境在不同谱系里反复造出相同形态，因此这个词也指功能类群，而非单一科。"},{"no":"04","title":"Aerial roots and viviparous seed","titleCN":"气生根与胎生苗","definition":"the stilt roots, pneumatophores and live seedlings that let the plant breathe and settle in mud","definitionCN":"让植株在泥中呼吸与定植的支柱根、呼吸根与未落地即萌发的幼苗","example":"The mangrove seedling was still attached to the parent tree.","exampleCN":"红树幼苗仍挂在母树上。","why":"The word carries the image of a plant that solves two problems at once, breathing air and dropping a ready-made young, so it can stand for that adaptation.","whyCN":"这个词带有「同时解决两个难题」的意象：呼吸空气、直接落下已萌发的幼体，因此也能指这套适应。"},{"no":"05","title":"The tidal habitat","titleCN":"红树潮间带生境","definition":"the muddy intertidal zone dominated by mangrove vegetation","definitionCN":"由红树植被占优势的泥质潮间带","example":"Crabs move through the mangrove on the rising tide.","exampleCN":"涨潮时螃蟹在红树间穿行。","why":"Once ecologists mapped the zone by its dominant plants, the plant name became a habitat name.","whyCN":"当生态学家按优势植物来划分地带，植物名就成了生境名。"},{"no":"06","title":"Nursery and coastal defence","titleCN":"育幼场与海岸防护","definition":"the service mangroves provide as fish nurseries and as barriers against waves and surge","definitionCN":"红树作为鱼类育幼场以及抵御波浪与风暴潮的屏障所提供的服务","example":"The mangrove nursed the juvenile fish until they were large enough for the reef.","exampleCN":"红树抚育幼鱼，直到它们大到可以进入珊瑚礁。","why":"Once people valued the plant for what it does rather than what it is, the word absorbed the service it supplies.","whyCN":"当人们看重这株植物的作用而非其本身，这个词就吸收了它提供的服务。"},{"no":"07","title":"A blue-carbon store","titleCN":"蓝碳储库","definition":"the carbon held in mangrove wood, roots and waterlogged sediment","definitionCN":"储存在红树木材、根系与饱水沉积物中的碳","example":"Protecting the mangrove keeps centuries of carbon in the mud.","exampleCN":"保护红树把数百年的碳留在泥里。","why":"Climate accounting needed a unit for carbon banked by coastal plants, and the plant name was extended to the stock.","whyCN":"气候核算需要给沿海植物存下的碳一个单位，植物名便延伸指这份存量。"},{"no":"08","title":"A restoration unit","titleCN":"修复单元","definition":"the planting unit used in mangrove restoration and offset projects","definitionCN":"红树林修复与补偿项目中的种植单元","example":"The project planted ten thousand mangroves along the eroded bank.","exampleCN":"项目在受侵蚀的岸段种下一万株红树。","why":"Restoration works plant by plant, so the countable tree became the practical unit of a project.","whyCN":"修复工作按株种植，因此可数的植株成了项目的实用单位。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Mangrove entered English in the seventeenth century through Atlantic trade languages. Its origin is disputed: Portuguese mangue, a Tupi source, Malay manggi-manggi and a blend with English grove all have supporters. Dates are approximate.","cn":"mangrove 于十七世纪经大西洋贸易语言进入英语。它的来源有争议：葡萄牙语 mangue、图皮语来源、马来语 manggi-manggi，以及与英语 grove 混合的说法，各有支持者。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"PORTUGUESE MANGUE","en":"Portuguese mangue was used in Brazil for the tidal tree; it is often said to come from a Tupi word, but the exact Tupi form and meaning are not securely recorded.","cn":"葡萄牙语 mangue 在巴西用来指这种潮间带树木；常说它来自图皮语，但确切的图皮语形式与含义没有可靠记录。"},{"era":"MALAY HYPOTHESIS","en":"Another account connects the word with Malay manggi-manggi; this is a competing hypothesis, not a demonstrated derivation.","cn":"另一种说法把该词与马来语 manggi-manggi 联系起来；这是并列的假说，并非已证实的派生。"},{"era":"GROVE BLEND","en":"Some dictionaries suggest English grove influenced the final shape of mangrove; the resemblance is real, but influence is inferred rather than proven.","cn":"一些词典认为英语 grove 影响了 mangrove 的最终词形；相似确实存在，但影响是推断而非证明。"},{"era":"ENGLISH BORROWING","en":"English records mangrove from the early seventeenth century, first for trees of the tropical Atlantic and later for the whole growth form.","cn":"英语在十七世纪初记录 mangrove，最初指热带大西洋的树木，后指整个生长型。"},{"era":"ECOLOGICAL WIDENING","en":"In the twentieth century the word widened from one kind of tree to a worldwide tidal tree group and its habitat.","cn":"到二十世纪，这个词从一种树扩展到全球潮间带树类及其生境。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (word origin): no single origin is proven, the Tupi and Malay accounts are hypotheses, the grove influence is inferred, and the deeper source of Portuguese mangue is unknown.","cn":"来源不确定（词源本身）：没有任何单一来源得到证明，图皮语与马来语说法都是假说，grove 的影响属推断，葡萄牙语 mangue 的更深来源不明。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the plant and its collective forms; group two holds other tidal habitats and growth forms often confused with it.","cn":"第一组是植株及其集合形式；第二组是容易与它混淆的其他潮间带生境与生长型。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"mangrove forest","ipa":"/ˈmæŋɡrəʊv ˈfɒrɪst/","tag":"the stand, not the tree","definition":"The forest or stand as a whole; mangrove names the plant, so one is a tree and the other is the woodland it forms.","definitionCN":"指整片森林或林分；mangrove 指植株，因此一个是树，另一个是它形成的林地。"},{"word":"mangal","ipa":"/ˈmæŋɡəl/","tag":"ecological term","definition":"The ecological community of mangrove plants; it is the technical name for the assemblage, not for a single tree.","definitionCN":"红树植物的生态群落；这是群落的学术名称，不指单株。"},{"word":"mangrove swamp","ipa":"/ˈmæŋɡrəʊv swɒmp/","tag":"wetland wording","definition":"The waterlogged wetland dominated by mangroves; it emphasizes the wet ground rather than the trees.","definitionCN":"由红树占优势的饱水湿地；它强调湿地面而不是树木。"},{"word":"mangrove seedling","ipa":"/ˈmæŋɡrəʊv ˈsiːdlɪŋ/","tag":"the young plant","definition":"A young mangrove before it is established; it is one stage of the plant, not the mature tree.","definitionCN":"尚未定植的红树幼体；它是植株的一个阶段，不是成年树。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"salt marsh","ipa":"/sælt mɑːʃ/","tag":"temperate grassy counterpart","definition":"A tidal meadow of salt-tolerant grasses; it shares the salty tide but lacks woody trees and aerial roots.","definitionCN":"耐盐禾草组成的潮汐草甸；同样受咸潮影响，却没有木本树与气生根。"},{"word":"tidal forest","ipa":"/ˈtaɪdl ˈfɒrɪst/","tag":"broader category","definition":"Any woodland flooded by tides; mangrove forest is the tropical, salt-tolerant member of that wider class.","definitionCN":"任何受潮汐淹没的林地；红树林是这一更宽类别中热带、耐盐的成员。"},{"word":"seagrass","ipa":"/ˈsiːɡrɑːs/","tag":"submerged plant, different root","definition":"A flowering plant that grows fully submerged in shallow sea; it is not woody and has no aerial roots.","definitionCN":"完全沉在浅海中的开花植物；它没有木质结构，也没有气生根。"},{"word":"mudflat","ipa":"/ˈmʌdflæt/","tag":"bare sediment","definition":"A bare tidal mud surface without rooted trees; mangroves often colonize its upper edge.","definitionCN":"没有扎根树木的裸露潮泥面；红树常占据它的上缘。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real growth-form terms, real relatives and real habitat collocations, not invented rhymes.","cn":"正常联想：真实的生长型术语、真实同族词与真实生境搭配，而非编造的顺口溜。"},"normal":[{"en":"A mangrove stands on stilt roots in salty mud.","cn":"红树用支柱根立在咸泥上。"},{"en":"The seedling is viviparous, already growing while still on the parent tree.","cn":"红树幼苗是胎生的，还挂在母树上时就开始生长。"},{"en":"Mangrove is a growth form, not a single plant family.","cn":"红树是一种生长型，不是一个单一植物科。"},{"en":"Mangroves nurse fish and soften storm waves.","cn":"红树抚育鱼类，也削弱风暴波浪。"},{"en":"Mangrove mud stores blue carbon for centuries.","cn":"红树泥把蓝碳储存数百年。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a tree walking into the sea on many wooden stilts.","cn":"想象一棵树踩着许多木高跷走进海里。"},{"en":"Picture a nursery where the young are born already able to swim.","cn":"想象一座育幼所，幼体一出生就会游。"},{"en":"Picture a wall of roots that turns a storm into a whisper.","cn":"想象一道根墙，把风暴变成耳语。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A mangrove can tolerate being flooded twice a day.","cn":"一株红树能忍受每天两次淹水。"},{"en":"The mangrove roots trap plastic along with sediment.","cn":"红树根把塑料连同泥沙一起截住。"},{"en":"Restoration failed because the wrong mangrove was planted.","cn":"修复失败是因为种错了红树种类。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「mangrove」不作字面拆分；记住支柱根与胎生苗这两个画面 → 红树","word":"mangrove"},"root":"词源有争议：一说来自葡萄牙语 mangue（可能出自图皮语，确切形式不明），一说与马来语 manggi-manggi 有关，另有英语 grove 影响词形的推测；均为假说，无定论。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one salt-water tree: the plant, its stand, its taxonomic group, its roots and seedlings, its habitat, its nursery service, its carbon store and its restoration unit.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一株咸水树展开：植株、林片、类群、根与苗、生境、育幼服务、碳库与修复单元。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a tree standing on stilt roots in shallow tidal mud, a long seedling hanging from its crown.","cn":"核心意象：一棵树踩着支柱根立在浅浅的潮泥中，枝头挂着长条形的胎生苗。"},"chain":["THE TREE","A STAND OF TREES","TAXONOMIC GROUP","ROOT AND SEED ADAPTATION","TIDAL HABITAT","ECOSYSTEM SERVICE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 04","en":"ROOTS DEFINE THE TREE: stilt roots and breathing roots are what let it live where it does.","cn":"根定义树：支柱根与呼吸根正是它能在那里存活的原因。"},{"senses":"02 · 05","en":"A STAND BECOMES A HABITAT: dense trees change mud, water and light enough to house other life.","cn":"林片成为生境：密集的树改变泥、水与光，足以容纳其他生命。"},{"senses":"03","en":"THE GROUP: these trees form a taxonomic group of their own.","cn":"类群：这些树自成一个分类单元。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE CARBON STORE: waterlogged mud slows decay and holds carbon.","cn":"碳储库：树下饱水的泥减慢分解，把碳留住。"},{"senses":"06 · 08","en":"SERVICE JUSTIFIES RESTORATION: because the trees protect and nurse, projects plant them again.","cn":"服务支撑修复：正因为树能防护与育幼，项目才会重新种下它们。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Mangrove is not built from transparent English affixes; it is a borrowed name whose ending only resembles the native word grove. The useful units are the compounds it forms.","cn":"mangrove 不是由透明的英语词缀构成；它是一个借入名称，词尾只是碰巧像本族词 grove。真正有用的是它构成的复合词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"No Latin ancestor is established for mangrove; the name comes through Romance and possibly Tupi or Malay trade routes, so the Latin layer is left empty here.","cn":"mangrove 没有已确立的拉丁语祖先；这个名称经罗曼语、可能还经图皮语或马来语贸易路线传来，因此此处拉丁层留空。"},"items":[{"word":"mangrove","structure":"borrowed whole word (origin disputed)","meaning":"a tidal salt-water tree","meaningCN":"潮间带咸水树","example":"The mangrove grows where fresh and salt water meet.","exampleCN":"红树生长在淡水与咸水相遇之处。"},{"word":"mangroves","structure":"mangrove + plural -s","meaning":"several trees or a stand","meaningCN":"多株红树或一片林","example":"Mangroves lined both banks.","exampleCN":"两岸都排着红树。"},{"word":"mangrove forest","structure":"mangrove + forest (compound)","meaning":"a tidal woodland of mangroves","meaningCN":"红树构成的潮汐林地","example":"The mangrove forest floods at spring tide.","exampleCN":"大潮时红树林被淹。"},{"word":"mangrove swamp","structure":"mangrove + swamp (compound)","meaning":"the wet ground under a mangrove stand","meaningCN":"红树林下的湿泥地","example":"The mangrove swamp smells of sulphur.","exampleCN":"红树沼泽有硫磺味。"},{"word":"mangal","structure":"ecological term for the community","meaning":"a mangrove plant community","meaningCN":"红树植物群落","example":"The mangal supports crabs and snails.","exampleCN":"红树群落养着蟹与螺。"},{"word":"stilt root","structure":"stilt + root (compound)","meaning":"a root that props the trunk above the mud","meaningCN":"把树干撑在泥面上的根","example":"Stilt roots branch above the water line.","exampleCN":"支柱根在水线之上分叉。"},{"word":"pneumatophore","structure":"Greek pneuma 'air' + phoros 'bearing'","meaning":"a breathing root that reaches above the mud","meaningCN":"伸出泥面呼吸的根","example":"Pneumatophores stud the mud at low tide.","exampleCN":"低潮时呼吸根布满泥面。"},{"word":"vivipary","structure":"Latin vivus 'alive' + parere 'to bring forth'","meaning":"germination while the seed is still on the parent","meaningCN":"种子尚在母体上即萌发","example":"Vivipary gives the seedling a head start.","exampleCN":"胎生让幼苗先走一步。"},{"word":"propagule","structure":"Latin propagare 'to propagate' + -ule","meaning":"a detached young plant ready to root","meaningCN":"可脱落并扎根的幼体","example":"The propagule floated until it found mud.","exampleCN":"幼体漂浮着，直到遇见泥。"},{"word":"halophyte","structure":"Greek hals 'salt' + phyton 'plant'","meaning":"a salt-tolerant plant","meaningCN":"耐盐植物","example":"Mangroves are woody halophytes.","exampleCN":"红树是木本耐盐植物。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"mangrove forest","ipa_uk":"/ˈmæŋɡrəʊv ˈfɒrɪst/","ipa_us":"/ˈmæŋɡroʊv ˈfɔːrɪst/","definition_zh":"红树林；红树林森林；热带与亚热带潮间带林地；红树林生态系统","definition_en":"a tidal woodland of mangrove trees growing along tropical and subtropical shores","core_image":"一片密不透风的绿色树冠架在无数支柱根上，潮水在根间穿行","scene":"潮水漫进林下，密集的树冠把正午的光切成碎片，支柱根在浑水里交错。The mangrove forest shelters young fish among its tangled roots.","sceneCN":"这里指「由红树构成的潮间带林地」（第 1 个义项：热带或亚热带海岸上成片生长、受潮汐淹没的红树林）；句意为红树林在盘错的根系间庇护幼鱼。场景物件：树冠、支柱根、浑水、幼鱼。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"红树林；红树林森林（可数；复数 mangrove forests）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a dense mangrove forest","zh":"茂密的红树林"},{"phrase":"mangrove forest loss","zh":"红树林丧失"},{"phrase":"mangrove forest restoration","zh":"红树林修复"},{"phrase":"the canopy of a mangrove forest","zh":"红树林冠层"},{"phrase":"mangrove forest carbon","zh":"红树林碳"},{"phrase":"a mangrove forest reserve","zh":"红树林保护区"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"mangrove forests"},{"label":"定语形式（红树林的）","form":"mangrove-forest"},{"label":"相关名词（红树）","form":"mangrove"},{"label":"相关名词（森林）","form":"forest"},{"label":"生态学术语（红树林群落）","form":"mangal"},{"label":"同义说法（红树林地）","form":"mangrove woodland"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"mangrove","pos":"n.","zh":"红树"},{"word":"forest","pos":"n./v.","zh":"森林；造林"},{"word":"forested","pos":"adj.","zh":"覆盖森林的"},{"word":"forestry","pos":"n.","zh":"林业"},{"word":"mangal","pos":"n.","zh":"红树林群落"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A tidal woodland of mangroves","titleCN":"红树林林地","definition":"a tidal woodland of mangrove trees growing along tropical and subtropical shores","definitionCN":"热带与亚热带海岸上成片生长、受潮汐作用的红树构成的林地","example":"The mangrove forest shelters young fish among its tangled roots.","exampleCN":"红树林在盘错的根系间庇护幼鱼。","why":"Mangrove names the tree and forest names the woodland, so the compound names the stand as a vegetation type rather than a single plant.","whyCN":"mangrove 指树，forest 指林地，因此复合词命名的是一片植被类型，而不是单株。"},{"no":"02","title":"A tropical intertidal forest","titleCN":"热带潮间带森林","definition":"the forest formation found where tropical shores are flooded by tides","definitionCN":"热带海岸受潮汐淹没处形成的森林类型","example":"Mangrove forest replaces salt marsh where frost is absent.","exampleCN":"在没有霜冻的地方，红树林取代了盐沼。","why":"In global vegetation mapping the term marks a climatic zone as much as a plant, so it names a formation.","whyCN":"在全球植被制图中，这个术语既标记气候带也标记植物，因此它命名一种植被型。"},{"no":"03","title":"Canopy and root architecture","titleCN":"林冠与根系结构","definition":"the layered canopy, stilt roots and breathing roots that give the forest its physical structure","definitionCN":"层叠的林冠、支柱根与呼吸根所构成的森林物理结构","example":"The mangrove forest has a canopy closed enough to shade the mud.","exampleCN":"红树林的林冠密到能遮住泥面。","why":"Foresters describe a stand by its layers and roots, so the phrase can name the architecture rather than the species list.","whyCN":"林业人员按层次与根系描述林分，因此这个短语也能指结构本身，而非物种清单。"},{"no":"04","title":"A functioning ecosystem","titleCN":"运作中的生态系统","definition":"the community of trees, animals, microbes and sediment that functions as one system","definitionCN":"树木、动物、微生物与沉积物共同作为一个系统运作的群落","example":"The mangrove forest recycles nutrients within its own mud.","exampleCN":"红树林在自己的泥里循环养分。","why":"When the focus moves from trees to flows of energy and matter, the woodland becomes an ecosystem.","whyCN":"当重点从树转向能量与物质的流动，林地就变成了生态系统。"},{"no":"05","title":"A blue-carbon accounting unit","titleCN":"蓝碳核算单元","definition":"the forest and its sediment counted together as a carbon stock","definitionCN":"把森林与其沉积物合起来计算的碳储量","example":"The mangrove forest stores more carbon per hectare than the inland wood.","exampleCN":"每公顷红树林储存的碳多于内陆林地。","why":"Carbon markets need a boundary, so the stand plus its mud became one accounting unit.","whyCN":"碳市场需要边界，于是林分连同泥层成了一个核算单元。"},{"no":"06","title":"A coastal defence belt","titleCN":"海岸防护带","definition":"the belt of trees and roots that reduces wave height and storm surge","definitionCN":"降低波高与风暴潮的树木与根系带","example":"The mangrove forest broke the surge before it reached the seawall.","exampleCN":"红树林在风暴潮抵达海堤前把它打散。","why":"Coastal engineers measured the forest as a barrier, so the stand acquired a defence function.","whyCN":"海岸工程师把这片林当作屏障来测量，林分于是获得防护功能。"},{"no":"07","title":"A nursery ground","titleCN":"育幼场","definition":"the sheltered root maze where juvenile fish and crustaceans grow","definitionCN":"幼鱼与甲壳类在根系迷宫中生长的庇护所","example":"Shrimp leave the mangrove forest only when they are almost adult.","exampleCN":"虾几乎成年时才离开红树林。","why":"Fisheries science found that the forest is a nursery, so the place name became a function name.","whyCN":"渔业科学发现这片林是育幼场，地名于是变成功能名。"},{"no":"08","title":"A restoration and policy unit","titleCN":"修复与政策单元","definition":"a mapped forest area used in restoration targets, reserves and offsets","definitionCN":"用于修复目标、保护区与补偿项目的图定林地","example":"The province pledged to restore a thousand hectares of mangrove forest.","exampleCN":"该省承诺修复一千公顷红树林。","why":"Policy needs hectares and boundaries, so the vegetation type became a unit of planning.","whyCN":"政策需要公顷与边界，于是植被类型成了规划单元。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Mangrove forest joins a borrowed tropical tree name of disputed origin to forest, a word from medieval Latin forestis 'outside place'. The compound is modern ecology. Dates are approximate.","cn":"mangrove forest 把一个来源有争议的借入树名与 forest 组合起来，后者出自中世纪拉丁 forestis「外围之地」。这个复合词属现代生态学。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"MANGROVE, DISPUTED","en":"Mangrove came to English through Portuguese or Spanish trade forms; Tupi, Malay and English grove have all been proposed as influences, and none is proven.","cn":"mangrove 经葡萄牙语或西班牙语贸易词形进入英语；图皮语、马来语与英语 grove 都被提出过影响，但都未获证明。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN FORESTIS","en":"Forestis meant 'outside place' or 'wooded land outside the settlement'; it gave Old French forest and English forest.","cn":"forestis 意为「外围之地」或「聚落之外的林地」，形成古法语 forest 与英语 forest。"},{"era":"FOREIGN AND NATIVE","en":"The compound pairs a borrowed tropical name with a native-feeling but ultimately Latin-derived word, a common pattern in scientific English.","cn":"这个复合词把一个借入的热带名称与一个感觉像本族词、实则源自拉丁的 forest 配在一起，这是科技术语的常见模式。"},{"era":"NINETEENTH-CENTURY USE","en":"Travelers and colonial surveyors wrote of mangrove forests before ecologists had a formal category for them.","cn":"在生态学家建立正式类别之前，旅行者与殖民地测量员已在使用红树林这一说法。"},{"era":"MODERN ECOLOGY","en":"Twentieth-century ecology fixed the phrase as the name of a tropical intertidal formation, distinct from salt marsh and swamp forest.","cn":"二十世纪生态学把这个短语定为热带潮间带植被型的名称，与盐沼及沼泽林区分。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (word origin and first date): the origin of mangrove remains disputed, and the first printed use of the full compound is not precisely dated.","cn":"来源不确定（词源与首见年代）：mangrove 的来源仍有争议，完整复合词最早的印刷记录没有确切年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the tree, stand and ecological names that overlap; group two holds other wooded or tidal systems often mistaken for this forest.","cn":"第一组是相互重叠的树、林分与生态名称；第二组是常被误认作红树林的其他林地或潮汐系统。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"mangrove","ipa":"/ˈmæŋɡrəʊv/","tag":"the tree","definition":"A single tree or the plant kind; mangrove forest is the woodland made of many such trees.","definitionCN":"单株树或这一类植物；mangrove forest 是由许多这样的树构成的林地。"},{"word":"mangal","ipa":"/ˈmæŋɡəl/","tag":"community term","definition":"The ecological community of mangroves; it overlaps with the forest but stresses the living assemblage rather than the woodland.","definitionCN":"红树的生态群落；它与红树林重叠，但强调活的组合而不是林地本身。"},{"word":"mangrove swamp","ipa":"/ˈmæŋɡrəʊv swɒmp/","tag":"wet ground emphasis","definition":"The waterlogged ground under the trees; the forest names the trees, the swamp names the wet substrate.","definitionCN":"树下的饱水地面；森林指树，沼泽指湿基底。"},{"word":"forest","ipa":"/ˈfɒrɪst/","tag":"general woodland","definition":"Any large wooded area; mangrove forest restricts the woodland to tidal salt water and tropical shores.","definitionCN":"任何大片林地；mangrove forest 把林地限定到潮汐咸水与热带海岸。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"salt marsh","ipa":"/sælt mɑːʃ/","tag":"grassy not woody","definition":"A tidal meadow of salt-tolerant grasses; it occupies a similar zone but has no tree canopy.","definitionCN":"耐盐禾草组成的潮汐草甸；它占据相似地带，却没有树冠。"},{"word":"swamp forest","ipa":"/swɒmp ˈfɒrɪst/","tag":"freshwater woodland","definition":"A forest on waterlogged freshwater ground; it is flooded but not tidal and not salty.","definitionCN":"建在饱水淡水地面上的森林；它被水淹，但不受潮汐作用，也不咸。"},{"word":"tidal wetland","ipa":"/ˈtaɪdl ˈwetlənd/","tag":"broader class","definition":"Any wetland shaped by tides; mangrove forest is one woody member of this wider class.","definitionCN":"任何受潮汐塑造的湿地；红树林是这一更宽类别中的木本成员。"},{"word":"coastal woodland","ipa":"/ˈkəʊstl ˈwʊdlənd/","tag":"dry-land forest","definition":"Woodland near the coast but above the tide; it lacks salt flooding and aerial roots.","definitionCN":"靠近海岸但位于潮线以上的林地；它没有咸水淹浸与气生根。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real compounds, real ecological categories and real conservation collocations.","cn":"正常联想：真实复合词、真实生态类别与真实保护搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"Mangrove names the tree; forest names the woodland.","cn":"mangrove 指树；forest 指林地。"},{"en":"The forest forms where tropical shores are flooded by tides.","cn":"这片林形成于受潮汐淹没的热带海岸。"},{"en":"Its canopy, stilt roots and breathing roots are its architecture.","cn":"林冠、支柱根与呼吸根是它的建筑结构。"},{"en":"Mangrove forest is a nursery, a carbon store and a storm barrier.","cn":"红树林是育幼场、碳库与风暴屏障。"},{"en":"Restoration targets are counted in hectares of mangrove forest.","cn":"修复目标按红树林公顷数计算。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a green roof held above the water by thousands of wooden legs.","cn":"想象一片绿色屋顶，被成千上万条木腿撑在水面之上。"},{"en":"Picture a city where the streets are roots and the citizens are fish.","cn":"想象一座城，街道是根，居民是鱼。"},{"en":"Picture a forest that files carbon into the mud like documents into a vault.","cn":"想象一片森林，把碳像档案一样存进泥的保险库。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The mangrove forest was cleared for shrimp ponds.","cn":"红树林被清掉，改成了养虾池。"},{"en":"A healthy mangrove forest can raise the shore as sea level rises.","cn":"健康的红树林能在海面上升时把岸面抬高。"},{"en":"The map shows mangrove forest retreating along the delta.","cn":"地图显示红树林沿三角洲后退。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「mangrove（红树）+ forest（森林）」——红树构成的潮间带森林 → 红树林","word":"mangrove forest"},"root":"mangrove 来源有争议：或出自葡萄牙语 mangue（可能来自图皮语），或与马来语 manggi-manggi 有关，另有英语 grove 影响词形的推测；forest 出自中世纪拉丁 forestis「外围之地」→ 古法语 forest。复合词为现代生态学术语。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one woodland: a vegetation type, a tropical formation, a canopy architecture, an ecosystem, a carbon unit, a defence belt, a nursery and a policy unit.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一片林地展开：植被类型、热带植被型、林冠结构、生态系统、碳单元、防护带、育幼场与政策单元。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a dense green canopy held above muddy tidal water by countless stilt roots.","cn":"核心意象：一片浓密绿冠由无数支柱根撑在浑黄的潮水之上。"},"chain":["TIDAL WOODLAND","TROPICAL FORMATION","CANOPY ARCHITECTURE","ECOSYSTEM","BLUE CARBON","COASTAL DEFENCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"TREE TO FORMATION: a stand of one kind of tree becomes a mapped vegetation type across a climate zone.","cn":"从树到植被型：一片同种树林变成跨越气候带的图定植被类型。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"STRUCTURE MAKES FUNCTION: canopy and roots create the shade, shelter and sediment traps that the ecosystem runs on.","cn":"结构产生功能：林冠与根系造出荫蔽、庇护与截沙，生态系统靠此运转。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE CARBON STOCK: the wet, slow-decay system is measured as stored carbon.","cn":"碳储量：这套湿而慢分解的系统被计为储碳。"},{"senses":"06","en":"THE BREAKWATER: the stand takes energy out of waves before they reach the shore.","cn":"防波带：实体林分在波浪抵达岸前抽走能量。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"NURSERY TO POLICY: a function valued by fisheries becomes a hectare target in restoration policy.","cn":"从育幼到政策：渔业看重的功能变成修复政策中的公顷目标。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Mangrove forest is a compound of a borrowed tree name and a Latin-derived woodland word; both parts are free morphemes, and the phrase is best read as a label for a formation.","cn":"mangrove forest 是一个由借入树名与拉丁来源林地词构成的复合词；两部分都是自由语素，最好把它读作一种植被型的标签。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Only forest has a Latin line, through medieval forestis; mangrove has no established Latin ancestor, so the Latin layer is partial.","cn":"只有 forest 有拉丁线索，经由中世纪 forestis；mangrove 没有已确立的拉丁祖先，因此拉丁层只是部分的。"},"items":[{"word":"mangrove","structure":"borrowed tropical tree name (origin disputed)","meaning":"a tidal salt-water tree","meaningCN":"潮间带咸水树","example":"The mangrove roots trap sediment.","exampleCN":"红树根截住沉积物。"},{"word":"forest","structure":"medieval Latin forestis via Old French","meaning":"a large wooded area","meaningCN":"大片林地","example":"The forest begins above the tide line.","exampleCN":"森林从潮线以上开始。"},{"word":"forestis","structure":"forestis (adjective and noun, medieval Latin)","meaning":"outside; wooded land outside settlement","meaningCN":"外围的；聚落之外的林地","example":"The medieval term marked land beyond the village.","exampleCN":"这个中世纪词标记村庄之外的土地。"},{"word":"forested","structure":"forest + -ed (having)","meaning":"covered with trees","meaningCN":"覆盖树木的","example":"The delta is densely forested.","exampleCN":"三角洲林木茂密。"},{"word":"forestry","structure":"forest + -ry (practice or place)","meaning":"the management of forests","meaningCN":"林业；森林管理","example":"Forestry maps the stand by canopy height.","exampleCN":"林业按林冠高度绘制林分。"},{"word":"mangrove forest","structure":"mangrove + forest (compound noun)","meaning":"a tidal woodland of mangroves","meaningCN":"红树构成的潮汐林地","example":"The mangrove forest floods twice a day.","exampleCN":"红树林每天被淹两次。"},{"word":"mangrove-forest","structure":"compound used attributively","meaning":"of the mangrove woodland","meaningCN":"红树林的","example":"Mangrove-forest loss slows after protection.","exampleCN":"保护之后红树林丧失减慢。"},{"word":"canopy","structure":"Greek kanōpeion 'mosquito net' via Latin canopeum","meaning":"the upper layer of trees","meaningCN":"树木的上层","example":"The canopy closes over the creek.","exampleCN":"林冠在潮沟上方合拢。"},{"word":"mangal","structure":"ecological term for the community","meaning":"a mangrove assemblage","meaningCN":"红树群落","example":"The mangal is rich in molluscs.","exampleCN":"红树群落软体动物丰富。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"forestis","structure":"forestis (adjective/noun, medieval Latin)","meaning":"outside; wooded land outside a settlement","meaningCN":"外围的；聚落之外的林地"},{"word":"canopeum","structure":"canopeum, canopeī (n., second declension; from Greek)","meaning":"a mosquito net; later a canopy","meaningCN":"蚊帐；后指华盖、林冠"}]}},{"word":"marine biodiversity","ipa_uk":"/məˈriːn ˌbaɪəʊdaɪˈvɜːsəti/","ipa_us":"/məˈriːn ˌbaɪoʊdaɪˈvɜːrsəti/","definition_zh":"海洋生物多样性；海洋物种多样性；海洋遗传多样性；海洋生态系统多样性","definition_en":"the variety of life in the sea, from genes and species to habitats and ecosystems","core_image":"珊瑚礁、深海平原与海草床在同一片蓝色里并存，每一处都挤满不同的生物","scene":"潜水员在珊瑚礁上记录鱼群，每一种新出现的颜色都被写进水下记录板。Coral reefs hold a large share of marine biodiversity despite covering a tiny part of the sea floor.","sceneCN":"这里指「海洋中生命形式的整体多样性」（第 1 个义项：从基因、物种到生境与生态系统的海洋生命差异总量）；句意为珊瑚礁虽然只覆盖海底极小一部分，却拥有很大比例的海洋生物多样性。场景物件：珊瑚、鱼群、水下记录板、海草。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"海洋生物多样性（不可数；指多套系统时偶用复数 marine biodiversities）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"marine biodiversity loss","zh":"海洋生物多样性丧失"},{"phrase":"a hotspot of marine biodiversity","zh":"海洋生物多样性热点"},{"phrase":"protect marine biodiversity","zh":"保护海洋生物多样性"},{"phrase":"marine biodiversity conservation","zh":"海洋生物多样性保护"},{"phrase":"the measurement of marine biodiversity","zh":"海洋生物多样性的测量"},{"phrase":"marine biodiversity under climate change","zh":"气候变化下的海洋生物多样性"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（少见）","form":"marine biodiversities"},{"label":"相关名词（生物多样性）","form":"biodiversity"},{"label":"相关形容词（海洋的）","form":"marine"},{"label":"相关形容词（生物多样的）","form":"biodiverse"},{"label":"同义学术说法（海洋生物多样性）","form":"marine biological diversity"},{"label":"定语形式（海洋生物多样性的）","form":"marine-biodiversity"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"biodiversity","pos":"n.","zh":"生物多样性"},{"word":"marine","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"海洋的；海军陆战队员"},{"word":"biological","pos":"adj.","zh":"生物的；生物学的"},{"word":"diversity","pos":"n.","zh":"多样性"},{"word":"biodiverse","pos":"adj.","zh":"生物多样的"},{"word":"biodiversity loss","pos":"n.","zh":"生物多样性丧失"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The total variety of sea life","titleCN":"海洋生命的总多样性","definition":"the variety of life in the sea, from genes and species to habitats and ecosystems","definitionCN":"海洋中从基因、物种到生境与生态系统的生命差异总量","example":"Coral reefs hold a large share of marine biodiversity despite covering a tiny part of the sea floor.","exampleCN":"珊瑚礁虽然只覆盖海底极小一部分，却拥有很大比例的海洋生物多样性。","why":"Marine locates the variety in salt water and biodiversity names variety itself, so the phrase is the whole range of sea life taken as one quantity.","whyCN":"marine 把多样性定位到咸水，biodiversity 指多样性本身，因此这个短语是把全部海洋生命当作一个总量。"},{"no":"02","title":"Species richness","titleCN":"海洋物种丰富度","definition":"the number of marine species present in a place or in the ocean as a whole","definitionCN":"某一海域或整个海洋中出现的海洋物种数量","example":"The survey found unexpectedly high marine biodiversity on the slope.","exampleCN":"调查在陆坡发现了异常高的海洋生物多样性。","why":"Counting species is the oldest way to measure variety, so the phrase often narrows to species richness.","whyCN":"统计物种是衡量多样性最古老的方法，因此这个短语常收窄到物种丰富度。"},{"no":"03","title":"Genetic variation in the sea","titleCN":"海洋遗传多样性","definition":"the genetic differences among individuals and populations of marine organisms","definitionCN":"海洋生物个体与种群之间的遗传差异","example":"Marine biodiversity below the species level buffers populations against warming.","exampleCN":"物种层面以下的海洋生物多样性为种群抵御变暖提供缓冲。","why":"Variety exists inside a species too, and molecular tools made that layer visible, so the phrase extends downward to genes.","whyCN":"多样性也存在于物种内部，分子工具让这一层可见，于是这个短语向下延伸到基因。"},{"no":"04","title":"Habitat and ecosystem diversity","titleCN":"海洋生境与生态系统多样性","definition":"the range of marine habitat types, such as reefs, seagrass beds, vents and abyssal plains","definitionCN":"海洋生境类型的范围，如珊瑚礁、海草床、热液喷口与深海平原","example":"Marine biodiversity depends on having many kinds of habitat.","exampleCN":"海洋生物多样性依赖于拥有多种生境。","why":"Ecologists count variety at the scale of ecosystems as well, so the phrase can mean the diversity of habitats rather than of species.","whyCN":"生态学家也在生态系统尺度上统计多样性，因此这个短语也可指生境多样性而非物种多样性。"},{"no":"05","title":"Concentration in hotspots","titleCN":"热点区的集中分布","definition":"the unusually dense variety found in coral reefs, estuaries and deep-sea vents","definitionCN":"珊瑚礁、河口与深海热液喷口等处异常密集的多样性","example":"The reef is a hotspot of marine biodiversity in an otherwise empty sea.","exampleCN":"这片礁在原本空阔的海中是一处海洋生物多样性热点。","why":"Conservation needs priorities, so the phrase came to name places where variety is concentrated rather than evenly spread.","whyCN":"保护工作需要优先级，因此这个短语开始指多样性集中而非均匀分布的地方。"},{"no":"06","title":"The resource base of fisheries","titleCN":"渔业资源基础","definition":"the variety of marine life on which capture fisheries and aquaculture depend","definitionCN":"捕捞渔业与水产养殖所依赖的海洋生命多样性","example":"Declining marine biodiversity makes catches less stable.","exampleCN":"海洋生物多样性下降使渔获更不稳定。","why":"Fisheries see variety as portfolio insurance, so the phrase acquired an economic reading alongside the ecological one.","whyCN":"渔业把多样性看作组合保险，因此这个短语在生态读法之外多了经济读法。"},{"no":"07","title":"A conservation policy target","titleCN":"保护政策目标","definition":"the stated goal of protecting a share of marine variety in treaties and national plans","definitionCN":"条约与国家规划中保护一定比例海洋多样性的既定目标","example":"The agreement sets a marine biodiversity target for protected areas.","exampleCN":"该协议为保护区设定了海洋生物多样性目标。","why":"Once governments promised to protect variety, the phrase became a measurable policy target.","whyCN":"当政府承诺保护多样性，这个短语就成了可测量的政策目标。"},{"no":"08","title":"A measured index","titleCN":"可测指数","definition":"a numeric score, such as a diversity index, used to compare marine sites","definitionCN":"用于比较不同海域的数值评分，如多样性指数","example":"The team calculated marine biodiversity for each station.","exampleCN":"团队为每个站点计算了海洋生物多样性。","why":"Management requires numbers, so the concept was operationalized into indices and scores.","whyCN":"管理需要数字，于是这个概念被操作化为指数与评分。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Marine biodiversity joins Latin marinus 'of the sea' to a twentieth-century coinage that combines Greek bios 'life' with Latin diversus 'turned different ways'. Dates are approximate.","cn":"marine biodiversity 把拉丁 marinus「海的」与一个二十世纪新造词并置，后者把希腊 bios「生命」与拉丁 diversus「转向不同方向」组合起来。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MARE","en":"Mare 'sea' gave the adjective marinus 'of the sea', which English borrowed as marine; the deeper origin of mare is uncertain.","cn":"mare「海」形成形容词 marinus「海的」，英语借入为 marine；mare 的更深来源不确定。"},{"era":"GREEK BIOS","en":"Greek bios meant 'life, way of life' and entered modern science through the combining form bio-.","cn":"希腊 bios 意为「生命、生活方式」，经组合形式 bio- 进入现代科学。"},{"era":"LATIN DIVERSUS","en":"Diversus, the past participle of divertere 'to turn in different directions', gave English diverse and diversity.","cn":"diversus 是 divertere「转向不同方向」的过去分词，衍生英语 diverse 与 diversity。"},{"era":"COINAGE","en":"Biodiversity is generally dated to the mid 1980s and widely attributed to Walter G. Rosen; it spread after a 1988 symposium volume edited by E. O. Wilson.","cn":"biodiversity 一般认为是二十世纪八十年代中期所造，广泛归功于 Walter G. Rosen；它在 1988 年由 E. O. Wilson 主编的会议文集后流行。"},{"era":"MARINE EXTENSION","en":"Marine was attached to the new noun once ocean scientists needed to separate sea variety from the general term.","cn":"当海洋科学家需要把海洋多样性从通用词中分出，marine 便被加到这个新名词前。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin and first date): the pre-Latin source of mare is unknown, the pre-Greek source of bios is uncertain, and the first use of the exact English phrase is not recorded.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源与首见年代）：mare 在拉丁语之前的来源不明，bios 的前希腊语来源不确定，确切英语短语的最早使用没有记录。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the words built on the same bio- and diversity stock; group two holds neighbouring marine variety concepts and measures.","cn":"第一组是同出 bio- 与 diversity 词干的词；第二组是邻近的海洋多样性概念与测量词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"biodiversity","ipa":"/ˌbaɪəʊdaɪˈvɜːsəti/","tag":"the general term","definition":"The variety of life on land or in water; marine biodiversity restricts it to the sea.","definitionCN":"陆地或水中生命的多样性；marine biodiversity 把它限定到海洋。"},{"word":"marine","ipa":"/məˈriːn/","tag":"adjective, the locator","definition":"Relating to the sea; it only says where the variety is found, not that variety exists.","definitionCN":"与海有关的；它只说多样性在哪里，并不表示多样性本身。"},{"word":"biodiverse","ipa":"/ˌbaɪəʊdaɪˈvɜːs/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Describing a place rich in variety; it cannot serve as the name of the measured concept.","definitionCN":"描述某地多样性丰富；它不能作为被测量概念的名称。"},{"word":"marine biology","ipa":"/məˈriːn baɪˈɒlədʒi/","tag":"the discipline, not the variety","definition":"The science of marine organisms; marine biodiversity is what that science studies.","definitionCN":"研究海洋生物的科学；海洋生物多样性是它研究的对象。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"species richness","ipa":"/ˈspiːʃiːz ˈrɪtʃnəs/","tag":"one component","definition":"The count of species in a place; it is one measurable part of marine biodiversity, not the whole concept.","definitionCN":"某地物种的数量；它是海洋生物多样性可测的一部分，而不是整个概念。"},{"word":"ecosystem diversity","ipa":"/ˈiːkəsɪstəm daɪˈvɜːsəti/","tag":"habitat scale","definition":"The variety of ecosystem types; in the sea it is the habitat layer of marine biodiversity.","definitionCN":"生态系统类型的多样性；在海洋中它是海洋生物多样性的生境层。"},{"word":"genetic diversity","ipa":"/dʒəˈnetɪk daɪˈvɜːsəti/","tag":"within-species layer","definition":"Variation among genes and populations; it is the layer below species in marine biodiversity.","definitionCN":"基因与种群之间的变异；它是海洋生物多样性中物种以下的一层。"},{"word":"biological diversity","ipa":"/ˌbaɪəˈlɒdʒɪkl daɪˈvɜːsəti/","tag":"older synonym","definition":"The longer wording for the same idea; marine biological diversity is the formal variant of this phrase.","definitionCN":"同一概念的较长说法；海洋生物多样性是这一短语的正式变体。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real Greek and Latin parts, real ecological layers and real policy collocations.","cn":"正常联想：真实的希腊与拉丁构件、真实生态层次与真实政策搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"Bio- is life, diversity is difference, so biodiversity is life's difference.","cn":"bio- 是生命，diversity 是差异，生物多样性就是生命的差异。"},{"en":"Marine comes from Latin mare, the sea.","cn":"marine 出自拉丁 mare，即海。"},{"en":"The concept has three layers: genes, species and ecosystems.","cn":"这个概念有三层：基因、物种与生态系统。"},{"en":"Coral reefs are hotspots out of all proportion to their area.","cn":"珊瑚礁的面积很小，却是极不成比例的热点。"},{"en":"Fisheries treat variety as a portfolio that spreads risk.","cn":"渔业把多样性看作分散风险的组合。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a blue library whose books are genes, species and habitats.","cn":"想象一座蓝色图书馆，书是基因、物种与生境。"},{"en":"Picture a reef as a crowded city and the open sea as empty countryside.","cn":"想象珊瑚礁是拥挤的城市，外海是空旷的乡野。"},{"en":"Picture a net made of many species; lose strands and the whole net weakens.","cn":"想象一张由许多物种编成的网，抽掉几股，整张网就变弱。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Marine biodiversity is highest where habitats overlap.","cn":"海洋生物多样性在生境交叠处最高。"},{"en":"The treaty asks nations to report on marine biodiversity.","cn":"该条约要求各国报告海洋生物多样性状况。"},{"en":"Deep-sea mining could reduce marine biodiversity before it is even described.","cn":"深海采矿可能在海洋生物多样性尚未被描述之前就把它削减。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「marine（海洋的）+ biodiversity（生物多样性）」——海里的生命差异总量 → 海洋生物多样性","word":"marine biodiversity"},"root":"拉丁 mare「海」（更深来源不确定）→ marinus「海的」→ 英语 marine；希腊 bios「生命」+ 拉丁 diversus「转向不同方向」→ diversity；biodiversity 为二十世纪八十年代新造词，一般归功于 Walter G. Rosen。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one range of sea life: total variety, species count, genetic variation, habitat range, hotspots, fisheries base, policy target and measured index.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一片海洋生命范围展开：总多样性、物种数、遗传变异、生境范围、热点、渔业基础、政策目标与测量指数。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: reef, seagrass bed and open blue water side by side, each crowded with different forms of life.","cn":"核心意象：珊瑚礁、海草床与开阔蓝水并排，每一处都挤满不同的生命形态。"},"chain":["TOTAL MARINE VARIETY","SPECIES RICHNESS","GENETIC VARIATION","HABITAT DIVERSITY","HOTSPOTS","POLICY TARGET"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 08","en":"CONCEPT TO NUMBER: a broad idea becomes a diversity index that can be compared across stations.","cn":"从概念到数字：宽泛的观念变成可在站点间比较的多样性指数。"},{"senses":"02 · 06","en":"SPECIES TO FISHERIES: the number of species underpins the stability of catches.","cn":"从物种到渔业：物种数量支撑渔获的稳定。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"GENES AND HABITATS: variation inside species and between habitats both supply resilience.","cn":"基因与生境：种内变异与生境差异都提供韧性。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE HOTSPOTS: variety concentrates in a few places that stand out.","cn":"热点区：多样性集中在格外突出的少数海域。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE TARGET: what fisheries depend on becomes what governments promise to protect.","cn":"政策目标：渔业赖以生存的东西，成为政府承诺保护的对象。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Marine biodiversity is a hybrid compound: a Latin adjective plus a modern noun made of a Greek prefix and a Latin root. Both halves are transparent.","cn":"marine biodiversity 是混合复合词：一个拉丁形容词，加一个由希腊前缀与拉丁词根构成的现代名词。两半都透明。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Mare supplies marine; diversus supplies diversity; Greek bios supplies the bio- element. The phrase mixes both classical layers.","cn":"mare 提供 marine；diversus 提供 diversity；希腊 bios 提供 bio- 成分。这个短语混合了两个古典层。"},"items":[{"word":"marine","structure":"Latin marinus 'of the sea' from mare","meaning":"relating to the sea","meaningCN":"海的；海洋的","example":"Marine animals range from plankton to whales.","exampleCN":"海洋动物从浮游生物到鲸都有。"},{"word":"bio-","structure":"Greek bios 'life' (combining form)","meaning":"life","meaningCN":"生命","example":"Bio- appears in biology and biosphere.","exampleCN":"bio- 出现在生物学与生物圈等词中。"},{"word":"diversity","structure":"Latin diversus 'turned different ways' + -ity","meaning":"variety, difference","meaningCN":"多样性；差异","example":"Diversity rises toward the tropics.","exampleCN":"多样性向热带升高。"},{"word":"biodiversity","structure":"bio- + diversity (modern coinage)","meaning":"the variety of life","meaningCN":"生命多样性","example":"Biodiversity is measured at three levels.","exampleCN":"生物多样性在三个层面测量。"},{"word":"marine biodiversity","structure":"marine + biodiversity (compound noun)","meaning":"the variety of sea life","meaningCN":"海洋生命的多样性","example":"Marine biodiversity is unevenly distributed.","exampleCN":"海洋生物多样性分布不均。"},{"word":"biodiverse","structure":"bio- + diverse (adjective)","meaning":"rich in life forms","meaningCN":"生命形式丰富的","example":"The reef is extremely biodiverse.","exampleCN":"这片礁的生命形式极为丰富。"},{"word":"richness","structure":"rich + -ness (abstract noun)","meaning":"the count or abundance of a category","meaningCN":"某一类别的数量或丰富程度","example":"Species richness is one metric.","exampleCN":"物种丰富度是一项指标。"},{"word":"hotspot","structure":"hot + spot (compound)","meaning":"a place of concentrated activity or variety","meaningCN":"活动或多样性集中的地点","example":"The reef is a biodiversity hotspot.","exampleCN":"这片礁是生物多样性热点。"},{"word":"endemism","structure":"Greek endēmos 'local' + -ism","meaning":"the state of being found only in one place","meaningCN":"只产于一地的状态","example":"High endemism raises the value of the hotspot.","exampleCN":"高度的特有性提高了热点价值。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"mare","structure":"mare, maris (n., third declension)","meaning":"sea","meaningCN":"海"},{"word":"marinus","structure":"marinus, marina, marinum (adjective)","meaning":"of the sea","meaningCN":"海的"},{"word":"diversus","structure":"diversus, diversa, diversum (adjective; participle of divertere)","meaning":"turned different ways; various","meaningCN":"转向不同方向的；多样的"}]}},{"word":"ocean acidification","ipa_uk":"/ˌəʊʃən ˌæsɪdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌoʊʃən ˌæsɪdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","definition_zh":"海洋酸化；海水酸度上升；海洋碳酸盐化学改变；人为二氧化碳吸收导致的pH下降","definition_en":"the ongoing decrease in the pH of seawater caused mainly by its absorption of carbon dioxide from the atmosphere","core_image":"海水里溶进二氧化碳，贝壳与珊瑚的钙质骨架在酸性水中慢慢变薄","scene":"实验舱里，海水被通入二氧化碳，贝壳表面的钙质开始变薄。Scientists measure ocean acidification by tracking the falling pH of surface water.","sceneCN":"这里指「海水pH持续下降的过程」（第 1 个义项：海洋吸收大气二氧化碳后酸度上升、碱度下降的整体变化）；句意为科学家通过追踪表层海水pH的下降来测量海洋酸化。场景物件：实验舱、气泡、贝壳、pH计。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"海洋酸化（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"ocean acidification research","zh":"海洋酸化研究"},{"phrase":"the impacts of ocean acidification","zh":"海洋酸化的影响"},{"phrase":"ocean acidification and warming","zh":"海洋酸化与变暖"},{"phrase":"monitor ocean acidification","zh":"监测海洋酸化"},{"phrase":"ocean acidification thresholds","zh":"海洋酸化阈值"},{"phrase":"a driver of ocean acidification","zh":"海洋酸化的驱动因素"}],"forms":[{"label":"相关动词（使酸化）","form":"acidify"},{"label":"相关形容词（已酸化的）","form":"acidified"},{"label":"相关名词（酸化）","form":"acidification"},{"label":"相关名词（酸）","form":"acid"},{"label":"相关形容词（酸性的）","form":"acidic"},{"label":"定语形式（海洋酸化的）","form":"ocean-acidification"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"ocean","pos":"n.","zh":"海洋"},{"word":"acid","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"酸；酸性的"},{"word":"acidic","pos":"adj.","zh":"酸性的"},{"word":"acidify","pos":"v.","zh":"使酸化"},{"word":"acidification","pos":"n.","zh":"酸化"},{"word":"acidified","pos":"adj.","zh":"已酸化的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The fall in seawater pH","titleCN":"海水pH下降","definition":"the ongoing decrease in the pH of seawater caused mainly by its absorption of carbon dioxide","definitionCN":"主要由海水吸收二氧化碳引起的pH持续下降","example":"Scientists measure ocean acidification by tracking the falling pH of surface water.","exampleCN":"科学家通过追踪表层海水pH的下降来测量海洋酸化。","why":"Acidification names the process of becoming more acid, and ocean fixes the setting, so the phrase is simply that process at sea.","whyCN":"acidification 指变酸的过程，ocean 固定场景，因此这个短语就是发生在海里的这一过程。"},{"no":"02","title":"A shift in carbonate chemistry","titleCN":"碳酸盐化学的改变","definition":"the change in dissolved carbonate and bicarbonate that lowers the saturation state of calcium carbonate","definitionCN":"溶解碳酸盐与碳酸氢盐的变化，使碳酸钙饱和度下降","example":"Ocean acidification makes it harder for shells to build their calcium carbonate.","exampleCN":"海洋酸化使贝壳更难构建碳酸钙。","why":"The pH number is only the visible tip; the real change is the shift in the carbonate system that builders depend on.","whyCN":"pH 数字只是露出的尖端；真正的变化是建造者所依赖的碳酸盐体系的移动。"},{"no":"03","title":"Anthropogenic carbon uptake","titleCN":"人为碳吸收","definition":"the process by which the ocean absorbs carbon dioxide released by burning fossil fuels and land use","definitionCN":"海洋吸收化石燃料燃烧与土地利用所释放的二氧化碳的过程","example":"Ocean acidification is driven by carbon dioxide that human activity adds to the air.","exampleCN":"海洋酸化由人类活动排入空气的二氧化碳驱动。","why":"The chemistry would be harmless if the carbon came slowly, so the modern sense stresses the human source and its speed.","whyCN":"如果碳来得缓慢，这套化学本无大碍，因此现代义强调人为来源及其速度。"},{"no":"04","title":"Stress on calcifiers","titleCN":"对钙化生物的压力","definition":"the reduced ability of corals, molluscs and other calcifiers to form and keep skeletons","definitionCN":"珊瑚、软体动物等钙化生物形成与保持骨骼的能力下降","example":"Ocean acidification slows the growth of coral skeletons.","exampleCN":"海洋酸化减慢珊瑚骨骼的生长。","why":"Biologists care about the organisms that build with carbonate, so the phrase came to name the stress on them.","whyCN":"生物学家关心用碳酸盐建造身体的生物，因此这个短语开始指它们承受的压力。"},{"no":"05","title":"Effects on larvae and plankton","titleCN":"对幼体与浮游生物的影响","definition":"the harm to early life stages and small drifting organisms that are sensitive to pH","definitionCN":"对pH敏感的早期生命阶段与小型漂流生物所受的损害","example":"Ocean acidification can damage the larvae of oysters before they settle.","exampleCN":"海洋酸化可能在牡蛎幼体附着前就伤害它们。","why":"Early stages are often the most fragile, so the phrase extends from adult shells to larvae and plankton.","whyCN":"早期阶段往往最脆弱，因此这个短语从成体贝壳延伸到幼体与浮游生物。"},{"no":"06","title":"Food-web and fishery consequences","titleCN":"食物网与渔业后果","definition":"the indirect effects on food webs, fish stocks and the people who depend on them","definitionCN":"对食物网、鱼类资源及依赖它们的人所产生的间接影响","example":"Ocean acidification may reshape the food web from the smallest shells upward.","exampleCN":"海洋酸化可能从最小的贝壳开始重塑食物网。","why":"Once effects move from one shell to the species that eat it, the phrase becomes shorthand for a chain of consequences.","whyCN":"当影响从一个贝壳移到吃它的物种，这个短语就成了连锁后果的简称。"},{"no":"07","title":"A monitoring problem","titleCN":"监测问题","definition":"the technical challenge of measuring pH, alkalinity and saturation over time and space","definitionCN":"在时间与空间上测量pH、碱度与饱和度的技术难题","example":"Ocean acidification monitoring now uses autonomous sensors on buoys.","exampleCN":"海洋酸化监测如今使用浮标上的自动传感器。","why":"The change is slow and uneven, so the phrase also names the observational program needed to see it.","whyCN":"变化缓慢且不均，因此这个短语也指看见它所需的观测计划。"},{"no":"08","title":"A climate policy issue","titleCN":"气候政策议题","definition":"the topic as framed in climate negotiations, emissions targets and marine protection plans","definitionCN":"气候谈判、排放目标与海洋保护规划中设定的议题","example":"Ocean acidification is now written into the climate convention's marine work.","exampleCN":"海洋酸化如今被写入气候公约的海洋工作。","why":"Because the cause is global emissions, the phrase moved from chemistry to the agenda of diplomacy.","whyCN":"因为成因是全球排放，这个短语从化学移到了外交议程。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Ocean acidification joins Greek ōkeanos, the world-encircling stream, to a Latin-derived noun built from acidus 'sour' and facere 'to make'. The phrase is late twentieth-century. Dates are approximate.","cn":"ocean acidification 把希腊 ōkeanos「环绕世界的大河」与一个拉丁来源名词并置，后者由 acidus「酸的」与 facere「做」构成。这个短语属二十世纪后期。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK OKEANOS","en":"Ōkeanos named the great river around the world; Latin took it as oceanus, and English ocean followed through French. Its pre-Greek source is unknown.","cn":"ōkeanos 指环绕世界的大河；拉丁作 oceanus，英语 ocean 经法语而来。其前希腊语来源不明。"},{"era":"LATIN ACIDUS","en":"Acidus 'sour, sharp' came from acere 'to be sour or sharp'; a link with a reconstructed root *ak- 'sharp' is often proposed but remains a reconstruction.","cn":"acidus「酸的、尖的」出自 acere「发酸、发尖」；常被联系到重构词根 *ak-「尖锐」，但那只是重构。"},{"era":"FACERE","en":"Latin facere 'to make' supplies the -fy of acidify and the -fication of acidification, literally 'making sour'.","cn":"拉丁 facere「做」提供 acidify 的 -fy 与 acidification 的 -fication，字面即「使变酸」。"},{"era":"ACIDIFICATION","en":"The noun acidification was formed in modern scientific English from acidify plus -ation, naming the process rather than the state.","cn":"名词 acidification 由现代科技英语以 acidify 加 -ation 构成，命名过程而非状态。"},{"era":"THE MARINE PHRASE","en":"Ocean acidification became a standard term in the 2000s, as long time series showed a steady fall in surface pH.","cn":"长期观测显示表层pH稳步下降之后，ocean acidification 在二十世纪第一个十年成为标准术语。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin and first date): the pre-Greek source of ōkeanos is unknown, the *ak- root is a reconstruction, and the first printed use of the full phrase is not precisely dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源与首见年代）：ōkeanos 的前希腊语来源不明，*ak- 词根属重构，完整短语最早的印刷记录没有确切年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds same-root acid and ocean forms that are easily confused; group two holds related climate and chemical changes of the sea.","cn":"第一组是同根、容易混淆的酸与海洋形式；第二组是相关的海洋气候与化学变化。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"acidification","ipa":"/ˌæsɪdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"the general process","definition":"Becoming more acid in any setting; ocean acidification is the marine case of that wider process.","definitionCN":"在任何环境中变得更酸；海洋酸化是这一更宽过程的海水情形。"},{"word":"acidify","ipa":"/əˈsɪdɪfaɪ/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To make something acid; it names the action, while the phrase names the resulting trend.","definitionCN":"使某物变酸；它指动作，而短语指由此形成的趋势。"},{"word":"acidic","ipa":"/əˈsɪdɪk/","tag":"adjective of state","definition":"Having a low pH; it describes the water at a moment, not the process by which it got there.","definitionCN":"pH 低的；它描述某一刻的水，而不是水变酸的过程。"},{"word":"ocean warming","ipa":"/ˈəʊʃən ˈwɔːmɪŋ/","tag":"parallel symptom, different chemistry","definition":"The rise in seawater temperature from the same carbon emissions; it is a twin impact, not acidification.","definitionCN":"同样由碳排放引起的海水升温；它是并列影响，不是酸化。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"pH decline","ipa":"/piː eɪtʃ dɪˈklaɪn/","tag":"the measured signal","definition":"The drop in the pH number itself; it is the indicator of ocean acidification, not its full chemistry.","definitionCN":"pH 数值本身的下降；它是海洋酸化的指示，而不是全部化学。"},{"word":"carbonate undersaturation","ipa":"/ˈkɑːbəneɪt ˌʌndəsætʃəˈreɪʃn/","tag":"mechanism","definition":"The state in which seawater holds too little carbonate for shells to form easily; it is a consequence of acidification.","definitionCN":"海水碳酸盐不足、贝壳难以形成的状态；它是酸化的后果。"},{"word":"eutrophication","ipa":"/ˌjuːtrəfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"different cause of low oxygen","definition":"Nutrient overload that fuels algal blooms and low oxygen; it can also shift pH but is not the carbon-driven process.","definitionCN":"营养盐过量引发藻华与低氧；它也能改变pH，但不是碳驱动的过程。"},{"word":"acid rain","ipa":"/ˈæsɪd reɪn/","tag":"atmospheric, not marine","definition":"Rain made acid by sulphur and nitrogen emissions; it affects lakes and soils, not the open ocean's carbon chemistry.","definitionCN":"由硫与氮排放变酸的雨；它影响湖泊与土壤，而不是外海的碳化学。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real Latin parts, real chemical measurements and real policy collocations.","cn":"正常联想：真实的拉丁构件、真实化学测量与真实政策搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"Acid plus facere means making sour, so acidification is the process of becoming more acid.","cn":"acid 加 facere 意为使变酸，因此酸化就是变酸的过程。"},{"en":"The ocean absorbs carbon dioxide, and the pH falls.","cn":"海洋吸收二氧化碳，pH 随之下降。"},{"en":"Lower pH means less carbonate for shells and reefs.","cn":"pH 更低意味着贝壳与礁石可用的碳酸盐更少。"},{"en":"Ocean acidification is measured with pH, alkalinity and saturation.","cn":"海洋酸化用pH、碱度与饱和度来测量。"},{"en":"The same emissions cause both warming and acidification.","cn":"同一批排放同时造成变暖与酸化。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a shell dissolving edge first in invisible sour water.","cn":"想象一只贝壳在看不见的酸水里先从边缘溶解。"},{"en":"Picture the sea drinking carbon dioxide and quietly turning its chemistry.","cn":"想象海喝下二氧化碳，悄悄改变自己的化学。"},{"en":"Picture a thermometer and a pH meter rising and falling together.","cn":"想象温度计与pH计一起升落。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Ocean acidification threatens reefs more slowly than bleaching but just as surely.","cn":"海洋酸化对礁石的威胁比白化更慢，却同样确定。"},{"en":"The bay shows ocean acidification earlier than the open sea.","cn":"这片海湾比外海更早显现海洋酸化。"},{"en":"Models project ocean acidification to continue even if emissions fall.","cn":"模型预测即使排放下降，海洋酸化仍会继续。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「ocean（海洋）+ acidification（酸化）」——海水变酸的过程 → 海洋酸化","word":"ocean acidification"},"root":"希腊 ōkeanos「环绕世界的大河」（前希腊语来源不明）→ 拉丁 oceanus → 英语 ocean；拉丁 acidus「酸的」← acere「发酸」+ facere「做」→ 现代 acidify / acidification。复合词为二十世纪后期术语。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one chemical drift: falling pH, carbonate change, human carbon uptake, stress on calcifiers, larval harm, food-web effects, monitoring, and climate policy.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一场化学漂移展开：pH下降、碳酸盐改变、人为碳吸收、钙化生物受压、幼体受损、食物网影响、监测与气候政策。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: carbon dioxide dissolving into seawater while the calcium skeleton of a shell thins at its edge.","cn":"核心意象：二氧化碳溶进海水，贝壳的钙质骨架在边缘一点点变薄。"},"chain":["FALLING PH","CARBONATE CHEMISTRY","HUMAN CARBON UPTAKE","CALCIFIER STRESS","LARVAL HARM","FOOD-WEB EFFECT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 07","en":"SIGNAL AND SENSOR: a slow pH trend can only be seen with long, calibrated measurements.","cn":"信号与传感器：缓慢的pH趋势只有靠长期校准的测量才看得见。"},{"senses":"02 · 04","en":"CHEMISTRY TO SKELETON: carbonate saturation decides whether a shell can be built.","cn":"从化学到骨架：碳酸盐饱和度决定贝壳能否被建造。"},{"senses":"03 · 08","en":"CAUSE TO POLICY: because the carbon is human, the chemistry becomes a negotiation topic.","cn":"从成因到政策：因为碳来自人类，化学就成了谈判议题。"},{"senses":"06","en":"THE FOOD WEB: damage to shells travels up through the species that eat them.","cn":"食物网：对贝壳的伤害会沿着吃它的物种向上传递。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE LARVAE: trouble starts at the larval stage.","cn":"幼体：问题从幼体阶段开始。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Ocean acidification is a transparent compound: a Greek-derived sea word plus a Latin-derived process noun. The second word can be split into acid, -ify and -ation.","cn":"ocean acidification 是透明复合词：希腊来源的海词，加拉丁来源的过程名词。第二个词可拆为 acid、-ify 与 -ation。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Acidus gives acid and acidic; facere gives the -fy and -fication that turn a quality into a process. Ocean adds the Greek layer.","cn":"acidus 提供 acid 与 acidic；facere 提供把性质变成过程的 -fy 与 -fication。ocean 加入希腊层。"},"items":[{"word":"ocean","structure":"Greek ōkeanos via Latin oceanus","meaning":"the great body of sea water","meaningCN":"巨大的海水体","example":"The ocean absorbs a quarter of our carbon emissions.","exampleCN":"海洋吸收我们碳排放的四分之一。"},{"word":"acid","structure":"Latin acidus 'sour'","meaning":"a sour substance; sour","meaningCN":"酸；酸的","example":"The acid dissolves the shell.","exampleCN":"酸溶解贝壳。"},{"word":"-ic","structure":"Latin -icus (adjective suffix)","meaning":"having the quality of","meaningCN":"具有……性质的","example":"Acid plus -ic gives acidic.","exampleCN":"acid 加 -ic 得到 acidic。"},{"word":"-ify","structure":"Latin facere 'to make' via French -ifier","meaning":"to make or become","meaningCN":"使成为；变得","example":"Acidify means to make acid.","exampleCN":"acidify 意为使变酸。"},{"word":"acidify","structure":"acid + -ify","meaning":"to make or become acid","meaningCN":"使变酸；变酸","example":"Carbon dioxide acidifies the water.","exampleCN":"二氧化碳使水变酸。"},{"word":"-ation","structure":"Latin -atio (action or result noun)","meaning":"the process or result of","meaningCN":"……的过程或结果","example":"Acidify plus -ation gives acidification.","exampleCN":"acidify 加 -ation 得到 acidification。"},{"word":"acidification","structure":"acidify + -ation","meaning":"the process of becoming acid","meaningCN":"变酸的过程","example":"Acidification changes the water chemistry.","exampleCN":"酸化改变水的化学。"},{"word":"acidified","structure":"acidify + -ed (past participle)","meaning":"made acid","meaningCN":"已变酸的","example":"Acidified water holds less carbonate.","exampleCN":"酸化的水持有更少的碳酸盐。"},{"word":"alkalinity","structure":"alkali + -ity (abstract noun)","meaning":"the water's capacity to buffer acid","meaningCN":"水缓冲酸的能力","example":"Alkalinity slows the pH change.","exampleCN":"碱度减缓pH变化。"},{"word":"calcifier","structure":"calx 'lime' + -ify + -er (one that does)","meaning":"an organism that builds calcium carbonate","meaningCN":"构建碳酸钙的生物","example":"Corals are major calcifiers.","exampleCN":"珊瑚是主要的钙化生物。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"acidus","structure":"acidus, acida, acidum (adjective)","meaning":"sour, sharp, acid","meaningCN":"酸的；尖锐的"},{"word":"facere","structure":"facere, feci, factum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to make, do","meaningCN":"做；使成为"},{"word":"oceanus","structure":"oceanus, oceanī (m., second declension; from Greek)","meaning":"the outer sea, ocean","meaningCN":"外海；大洋"}]}},{"word":"acidification","ipa_uk":"/ˌæsɪdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","ipa_us":"/ˌæsɪdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","definition_zh":"酸化；使变酸的过程；土壤酸化；水体酸化；食品酸化；生理性酸化","definition_en":"the process of making something acid or of becoming more acid","core_image":"一滴酸落进清水，试纸由绿转红，酸度一点点升高","scene":"实验室里，技术员把二氧化碳通入海水样品，指示剂的颜色慢慢转向红色。The team studied acidification in both seawater and soil to compare how each system buffered the change.","sceneCN":"这里指「使物质变酸或自身变酸的过程」（第 1 个义项：酸度升高、pH 下降的一般过程）；句意为团队同时研究海水与土壤的酸化，比较两个系统如何缓冲这一变化。场景物件：样品瓶、通气管、指示剂、比色卡。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"酸化（可数或不可数；复数 acidifications）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"ocean acidification","zh":"海洋酸化"},{"phrase":"soil acidification","zh":"土壤酸化"},{"phrase":"the acidification of lakes","zh":"湖泊酸化"},{"phrase":"acidification rate","zh":"酸化速率"},{"phrase":"induced acidification","zh":"诱发酸化"},{"phrase":"acidification threshold","zh":"酸化阈值"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"acidifications"},{"label":"相关动词（使酸化）","form":"acidify"},{"label":"相关形容词（已酸化的）","form":"acidified"},{"label":"相关形容词（正在酸化的）","form":"acidifying"},{"label":"相关名词（酸）","form":"acid"},{"label":"相关名词（酸度）","form":"acidity"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"acid","pos":"n./adj.","zh":"酸；酸的"},{"word":"acidic","pos":"adj.","zh":"酸性的"},{"word":"acidify","pos":"v.","zh":"使酸化；变酸"},{"word":"acidified","pos":"adj.","zh":"已酸化的"},{"word":"acidity","pos":"n.","zh":"酸度"},{"word":"acidulant","pos":"n.","zh":"酸化剂"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The general process of becoming acid","titleCN":"变酸的一般过程","definition":"the process of making something acid or of becoming more acid","definitionCN":"使某物变酸或自身变得更酸的过程","example":"The team studied acidification in both seawater and soil.","exampleCN":"团队同时研究了海水与土壤的酸化。","why":"Acid plus the making suffix -ify plus the process suffix -ation names becoming acid in the abstract, before any setting is chosen.","whyCN":"acid 加上「使成为」的 -ify 与「过程」的 -ation，先抽象地命名「变酸」，尚未限定场景。"},{"no":"02","title":"The ocean case","titleCN":"海洋酸化","definition":"the fall in seawater pH caused by absorption of carbon dioxide","definitionCN":"海水吸收二氧化碳所引起的pH下降","example":"Acidification of the surface ocean has accelerated since the industrial era.","exampleCN":"工业时代以来，表层海洋的酸化已经加速。","why":"The ocean is the largest sink for our carbon, so the general process acquired a dominant marine reading.","whyCN":"海洋是我们碳的最大汇，因此这个一般过程获得了主导性的海洋读法。"},{"no":"03","title":"The soil case","titleCN":"土壤酸化","definition":"the loss of base cations and the rise in exchangeable aluminium that make soil more acid","definitionCN":"盐基离子流失、可交换铝升高而使土壤变酸","example":"Acidification reduced the soil's ability to hold nutrients.","exampleCN":"酸化降低了土壤保持养分的能力。","why":"Farming and acid deposition remove the bases that buffer soil, so the process became a standard agricultural term.","whyCN":"耕作与酸性沉降带走缓冲土壤的盐基，这一过程于是成为标准农业术语。"},{"no":"04","title":"The freshwater case","titleCN":"淡水水体酸化","definition":"the fall in pH of lakes and streams, often with loss of fish and invertebrates","definitionCN":"湖泊与溪流pH下降，常伴随鱼类与无脊椎动物减少","example":"Acidification emptied the lake of its native fish.","exampleCN":"酸化使湖里的本地鱼消失。","why":"When acid deposition outstripped the water's buffering, the process became visible as dead lakes.","whyCN":"当酸性沉降超过水体的缓冲能力，这一过程就以「死湖」的形式显现。"},{"no":"05","title":"Acid rain and deposition","titleCN":"酸雨与酸性沉降","definition":"the delivery of acid-forming sulphur and nitrogen compounds from the atmosphere","definitionCN":"大气中成酸硫、氮化合物沉降到地表","example":"Acidification began downwind of the smelters.","exampleCN":"酸化从冶炼厂下风向开始。","why":"The cause can be named by its delivery route, so acidification often means the deposition step that starts the change.","whyCN":"成因可以按输送路径命名，因此酸化也常指启动变化的那一步沉降。"},{"no":"06","title":"An industrial chemical step","titleCN":"工业化学步骤","definition":"a deliberate acidification step in mining, food processing or chemical manufacture","definitionCN":"采矿、食品加工或化工生产中刻意使物料变酸的步骤","example":"Acidification of the slurry released the metal for extraction.","exampleCN":"矿浆酸化释放出金属以便提取。","why":"Industry uses the same word for a controlled operation, so the process can be a deliberate act rather than a harm.","whyCN":"工业用同一个词指受控操作，因此这个流程可以是有意为之，而不是损害。"},{"no":"07","title":"Food acidification","titleCN":"食品酸化","definition":"the lowering of pH in food by fermentation or added acids to preserve and flavour it","definitionCN":"通过发酵或加酸降低食品pH，以保鲜与调味","example":"Acidification gives yogurt its tang and keeps it safe.","exampleCN":"酸化给酸奶酸味，也让它更安全。","why":"Preservation depends on making the food hostile to microbes, so the same process became a kitchen and factory term.","whyCN":"保鲜依赖让食物对微生物不友好，同一过程于是成了厨房与工厂的术语。"},{"no":"08","title":"Physiological acidification","titleCN":"生理性酸化","definition":"the normal or abnormal lowering of pH in a body fluid or organ","definitionCN":"体液或器官中正常或异常的pH下降","example":"Acidification of the stomach is part of digestion.","exampleCN":"胃的酸化是消化的一部分。","why":"Bodies also run acid-making steps, so the term extends from the environment into physiology.","whyCN":"身体也进行成酸步骤，因此这个词从环境延伸到生理学。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Acidification is a modern Latin-derived noun: acidus 'sour' plus facere 'to make', with the action suffix -ation. It names a process, not a substance. Dates are approximate.","cn":"acidification 是近代拉丁来源名词：acidus「酸的」加 facere「做」，再加动作后缀 -ation。它命名过程，而非物质。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN ACIDUS","en":"Acidus 'sour, sharp' came from acere 'to be sour'; a link with a reconstructed root *ak- 'sharp' is often suggested but remains a reconstruction.","cn":"acidus「酸的、尖的」出自 acere「发酸」；常被联系到重构词根 *ak-「尖锐」，但那只是重构。"},{"era":"ENGLISH ACID","en":"English borrowed acid from Latin or French and used it both for the substance and for the quality.","cn":"英语从拉丁语或法语借入 acid，既指物质，也指性质。"},{"era":"-IFY","en":"The suffix -ify came through French from Latin facere 'to make', so acidify literally means to make acid.","cn":"后缀 -ify 经法语来自拉丁 facere「做」，因此 acidify 字面即「使变酸」。"},{"era":"-ATION","en":"Latin -atio supplied the action noun ending -ation, turning the verb into the name of a process.","cn":"拉丁 -atio 提供动作名词词尾 -ation，把动词变成过程之名。"},{"era":"MODERN WORD","en":"Acidification is recorded in English scientific writing from the nineteenth century, first for chemical operations and later for environmental change.","cn":"acidification 自十九世纪英语科学写作起有记录，最初指化学操作，后指环境变化。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin): the pre-Latin source of acidus is unknown, and the *ak- root is a reconstruction rather than a demonstrated derivation.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源）：acidus 在拉丁语之前的来源不明，*ak- 词根属重构，不是已证实的派生。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the same-root acid family with different grammatical jobs; group two holds other environmental changes that are often called acidification by mistake.","cn":"第一组是同根 acid 词族的不同语法角色；第二组是常被误称为酸化的其他环境变化。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"acidify","ipa":"/əˈsɪdɪfaɪ/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To make or become acid; it names the action, while acidification names the process as a whole.","definitionCN":"使变酸或变酸；它指动作，而 acidification 指整个过程。"},{"word":"acid","ipa":"/ˈæsɪd/","tag":"the substance","definition":"A substance that gives up protons; it is the agent, not the change it causes.","definitionCN":"能给出质子的物质；它是作用者，而不是它引起的变化。"},{"word":"acidic","ipa":"/əˈsɪdɪk/","tag":"the state","definition":"Having a low pH; it describes a condition at one moment, not a trend over time.","definitionCN":"pH 低的；它描述某一刻的状态，而不是一段时间内的趋势。"},{"word":"acidity","ipa":"/əˈsɪdəti/","tag":"the degree","definition":"The measured strength of acid in a substance; it is a quantity, while acidification is a process.","definitionCN":"物质中酸的实测强度；它是数量，而 acidification 是过程。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"ocean acidification","ipa":"/ˌəʊʃən ˌæsɪdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"one setting","definition":"The marine case of the general process; acidification alone can mean soil, lakes or food as well.","definitionCN":"一般过程在海洋中的情形；单说 acidification 也可能指土壤、湖泊或食品。"},{"word":"soil acidification","ipa":"/sɔɪl ˌæsɪdɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"one setting","definition":"The terrestrial case driven by base loss; it is not interchangeable with the marine process.","definitionCN":"由盐基流失驱动的陆地情形；不能与海洋过程互换。"},{"word":"acid rain","ipa":"/ˈæsɪd reɪn/","tag":"the delivery route","definition":"Rain made acid by air pollution; it is one cause of acidification, not the resulting change in soil or water.","definitionCN":"空气污染造成的酸性降雨；它是酸化的成因之一，而不是土壤或水中的结果变化。"},{"word":"alkalinization","ipa":"/ˌælkəlaɪnaɪˈzeɪʃn/","tag":"the opposite direction","definition":"The process of becoming more alkaline; it moves pH the other way and is not a form of acidification.","definitionCN":"变得更碱的过程；它把pH推向相反方向，不是酸化的一种。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real suffixes, real chemical terms and real environmental collocations.","cn":"正常联想：真实后缀、真实化学术语与真实环境搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"Acid plus -ify plus -ation means the process of making acid.","cn":"acid 加 -ify 加 -ation，就是使变酸的过程。"},{"en":"The word can take a setting: ocean, soil, lake or food.","cn":"这个词可以带场景：海洋、土壤、湖泊或食品。"},{"en":"Acidification is a process, acidity is a measured degree.","cn":"酸化是过程，酸度是可测的程度。"},{"en":"Acid rain is one delivery route for the same change.","cn":"酸雨是同一变化的输送路径之一。"},{"en":"The opposite trend is alkalinization.","cn":"相反的趋势是碱化。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a colour strip sliding from green to red as the water turns.","cn":"想象一条色带随着水的变化从绿滑向红。"},{"en":"Picture a soil losing its buffer one rain at a time.","cn":"想象土壤在一场场雨中失去缓冲。"},{"en":"Picture a yogurt pot turning sour on purpose, the same word as a damaged lake.","cn":"想象一盒酸奶被有意变酸，用的却是与受损湖泊同一个词。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Acidification of the lake killed the fish within a decade.","cn":"湖泊酸化在十年内杀死了鱼群。"},{"en":"Farmers limed the field to slow acidification.","cn":"农民给田里施石灰，以减缓酸化。"},{"en":"Acidification is measured as a fall in pH, not as a rise in acid content.","cn":"酸化按pH下降来衡量，而不是按酸含量上升来衡量。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「acid（酸）+ -ify（使成为）+ -ation（过程）」——使变酸的过程 → 酸化","word":"acidification"},"root":"拉丁 acidus「酸的」← acere「发酸」；拉丁 facere「做」提供 -ify 与 -fication；再加 -ation 构成动作名词。acidus 的更深来源不确定，*ak- 词根为重构。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one souring process: the general change, the ocean case, the soil case, the freshwater case, acid deposition, industry, food and the body.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一「变酸」过程展开：一般变化、海洋情形、土壤情形、淡水情形、酸性沉降、工业、食品与身体。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a drop of acid entering clear water while a test strip shifts from green to red.","cn":"核心意象：一滴酸落进清水，试纸从绿转向红。"},"chain":["MAKING SOUR","OCEAN CASE","SOIL CASE","FRESHWATER CASE","INDUSTRIAL STEP","FOOD PROCESS"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 08","en":"GENERAL TO BODY: the abstract process also names the normal souring inside a stomach.","cn":"从一般到身体：抽象过程也指胃里正常的变酸。"},{"senses":"02 · 06","en":"SEA AND INDUSTRY: the same chemistry can be an unintended global trend or a deliberate extraction step.","cn":"海与工业：同一套化学既可能是无意的全球趋势，也可能是有意的提取步骤。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"SOIL AND DEPOSITION: acid arriving from the air strips the soil of its buffering bases.","cn":"土壤与沉降：从空气来的酸剥去土壤的缓冲盐基。"},{"senses":"04","en":"THE LAKES: freshwater is often the visible end of the same deposition.","cn":"湖泊：淡水水体常是同一沉降最可见的去处。"},{"senses":"07","en":"FOOD BY DESIGN: controlled souring preserves and flavours food rather than damaging it.","cn":"有意的食品酸化：受控变酸用于保鲜调味，而非造成损害。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Acidification is a textbook suffix chain: a root, a verb-forming suffix and a noun-forming suffix. Each step changes the grammatical job without changing the core idea of sourness.","cn":"acidification 是教科书式的后缀链：词根、动词后缀、名词后缀。每一步改变语法角色，却不改变「酸」这一核心观念。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Acidus supplies the root, facere supplies -ify and -fication, and -atio supplies the noun ending. The whole word is Latin in its parts.","cn":"acidus 提供词根，facere 提供 -ify 与 -fication，-atio 提供名词词尾。整个词的各部分都属拉丁。"},"items":[{"word":"acid","structure":"Latin acidus 'sour'","meaning":"a sour substance","meaningCN":"酸；酸性物质","example":"Acid turns the indicator red.","exampleCN":"酸使指示剂变红。"},{"word":"-ic","structure":"Latin -icus (adjective suffix)","meaning":"having the quality of","meaningCN":"具有……性质的","example":"Acidic soils lose nutrients.","exampleCN":"酸性土壤流失养分。"},{"word":"-ify","structure":"Latin facere via French -ifier","meaning":"to make or become","meaningCN":"使成为；变得","example":"The process acidifies the water.","exampleCN":"这一过程使水变酸。"},{"word":"acidify","structure":"acid + -ify","meaning":"to make acid","meaningCN":"使酸化","example":"Carbon dioxide acidifies seawater.","exampleCN":"二氧化碳使海水酸化。"},{"word":"-ation","structure":"Latin -atio (action noun)","meaning":"the process or result","meaningCN":"过程或结果","example":"The suffix turns the verb into a process name.","exampleCN":"这个后缀把动词变成过程名。"},{"word":"acidification","structure":"acidify + -ation","meaning":"the process of becoming acid","meaningCN":"变酸的过程","example":"Acidification changes the whole system.","exampleCN":"酸化改变整个系统。"},{"word":"acidified","structure":"acidify + -ed","meaning":"made acid","meaningCN":"已酸化的","example":"Acidified water holds less carbonate.","exampleCN":"酸化的水含有更少碳酸盐。"},{"word":"acidity","structure":"acid + -ity (abstract noun)","meaning":"the degree of being acid","meaningCN":"酸的程度","example":"Acidity is measured by titration.","exampleCN":"酸度用滴定法测量。"},{"word":"acidulant","structure":"acid + -ulant (agent noun)","meaning":"a substance added to make food acid","meaningCN":"加入食品使其变酸的物质","example":"Citric acid is a common acidulant.","exampleCN":"柠檬酸是常用的酸化剂。"},{"word":"alkalinization","structure":"alkaline + -ization (process noun)","meaning":"the process of becoming alkaline","meaningCN":"变碱的过程","example":"Alkalinization reverses the pH trend.","exampleCN":"碱化逆转pH趋势。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"acidus","structure":"acidus, acida, acidum (adjective)","meaning":"sour, sharp, acid","meaningCN":"酸的；尖锐的"},{"word":"acere","structure":"acere (verb, second conjugation; stative)","meaning":"to be sour, be sharp","meaningCN":"发酸；发尖"},{"word":"facere","structure":"facere, feci, factum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to make, do","meaningCN":"做；使成为"}]}},{"word":"marine pollution","ipa_uk":"/məˈriːn pəˈluːʃn/","ipa_us":"/məˈriːn pəˈluːʃn/","definition_zh":"海洋污染；海洋污染物输入；陆源污染；油污；塑料污染；营养盐污染；海洋噪声污染","definition_en":"the introduction into the sea of substances, energy or organisms that harm marine life, ecosystems or human uses","core_image":"河口外的海面浮着一层油膜，塑料碎片与泡沫混在浪花里","scene":"志愿者在河口外的沙滩上捡起缠着海草的塑料瓶，远处的海面泛着一层油光。Marine pollution reaches even the deepest trenches through currents and sinking particles.","sceneCN":"这里指「进入海洋并造成危害的物质或能量」（第 1 个义项：人类活动把污染物排入海中、损害生命与生态系统的总过程）；句意为海洋污染经由洋流与下沉颗粒，连最深的海沟也能到达。场景物件：塑料瓶、海草、油膜、浪花。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"海洋污染（不可数）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"marine pollution control","zh":"海洋污染控制"},{"phrase":"land-based marine pollution","zh":"陆源海洋污染"},{"phrase":"marine pollution monitoring","zh":"海洋污染监测"},{"phrase":"a source of marine pollution","zh":"海洋污染源"},{"phrase":"marine pollution from plastics","zh":"塑料造成的海洋污染"},{"phrase":"the law of marine pollution","zh":"海洋污染法"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（少见）","form":"marine pollutions"},{"label":"相关动词（污染）","form":"pollute"},{"label":"相关名词（污染物）","form":"pollutant"},{"label":"相关形容词（受污染的）","form":"polluted"},{"label":"相关形容词（造成污染的）","form":"polluting"},{"label":"定语形式（海洋污染的）","form":"marine-pollution"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"pollution","pos":"n.","zh":"污染"},{"word":"pollute","pos":"v.","zh":"污染"},{"word":"pollutant","pos":"n.","zh":"污染物"},{"word":"polluter","pos":"n.","zh":"污染者"},{"word":"polluted","pos":"adj.","zh":"受污染的"},{"word":"marine","pos":"adj.","zh":"海洋的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Contamination of the sea","titleCN":"海洋污染总称","definition":"the introduction into the sea of substances, energy or organisms that harm marine life, ecosystems or human uses","definitionCN":"人类把物质、能量或生物引入海中，损害海洋生命、生态系统或人类用途","example":"Marine pollution reaches even the deepest trenches through currents and sinking particles.","exampleCN":"海洋污染经由洋流与下沉颗粒，连最深的海沟也能到达。","why":"Marine fixes the setting and pollution names the making-impure, so the phrase is the whole range of harmful inputs to the sea.","whyCN":"marine 固定场景，pollution 指使变脏，因此这个短语是进入海洋的全部有害输入。"},{"no":"02","title":"Land-based runoff","titleCN":"陆源输入","definition":"pollution carried from land by rivers, drains and groundwater","definitionCN":"经河流、排水管与地下水从陆地带来的污染","example":"Most marine pollution begins on land, far from the beach.","exampleCN":"大部分海洋污染始于陆地，离海滩很远。","why":"Because most inputs come downhill from cities and farms, the phrase often means the land-based share.","whyCN":"因为大部分输入从城市与农场顺流而下，这个短语常指陆源那一部分。"},{"no":"03","title":"Oil spills","titleCN":"溢油与油污","definition":"crude oil or fuel released from tankers, pipelines or wells into the sea","definitionCN":"油轮、管道或油井把原油或燃料泄入海中","example":"Marine pollution from the spill coated the birds for months.","exampleCN":"溢油造成的海洋污染给鸟身上裹了好几个月的油。","why":"Oil is the most visible input, so the phrase became a familiar label for tanker and rig disasters.","whyCN":"石油是最显眼的输入，因此这个短语成了油轮与钻井事故的常用标签。"},{"no":"04","title":"Plastics and microplastics","titleCN":"塑料与微塑料","definition":"plastic debris, pellets and fragments that persist and accumulate in the sea","definitionCN":"在海中持久存在并累积的塑料垃圾、颗粒与碎片","example":"Marine pollution is now dominated by plastic by count.","exampleCN":"按数量计，海洋污染如今以塑料为主。","why":"As plastic production grew, the phrase shifted toward the most numerous and durable debris.","whyCN":"随着塑料产量增长，这个短语转向数量最多、最持久的垃圾。"},{"no":"05","title":"Nutrient overload","titleCN":"营养盐过量","definition":"excess nitrogen and phosphorus that fuel algal blooms and low-oxygen dead zones","definitionCN":"过量氮磷引发藻华与低氧死区","example":"Marine pollution from fertilizer created a dead zone at the river mouth.","exampleCN":"化肥造成的海洋污染在河口造出一片死区。","why":"The harm here is too much food rather than poison, so the phrase includes enrichment as a form of pollution.","whyCN":"这里的危害是「食物太多」而非毒物，因此这个短语把富营养化也算作污染。"},{"no":"06","title":"Chemical contaminants","titleCN":"化学污染物","definition":"heavy metals, persistent organic pollutants and industrial chemicals that accumulate in tissue","definitionCN":"在组织中累积的重金属、持久性有机污染物与工业化学品","example":"Marine pollution shows up as mercury in top predators.","exampleCN":"海洋污染在顶级捕食者体内表现为汞。","why":"When contaminants travel through food chains and concentrate, the phrase names that chemical load.","whyCN":"当污染物沿食物链传递并富集，这个短语就指这份化学负荷。"},{"no":"07","title":"Underwater noise","titleCN":"水下噪声","definition":"sound from ships, sonar and construction that disrupts marine animals","definitionCN":"船只、声呐与施工产生的、干扰海洋动物的声音","example":"Marine pollution now includes noise that drowns out whale calls.","exampleCN":"海洋污染如今也包括淹没鲸歌的噪声。","why":"Modern law treats energy as a pollutant, so the phrase extends from matter to sound.","whyCN":"现代法律把能量也视为污染物，因此这个短语从物质延伸到声音。"},{"no":"08","title":"A legal definition","titleCN":"法律定义","definition":"the treaty definition of harmful input that states must prevent and control","definitionCN":"条约中对各国有义务预防与控制的有害输入所作的定义","example":"The convention defines marine pollution by its effects, not by its source.","exampleCN":"该公约按影响而非来源定义海洋污染。","why":"Once treaties needed a shared test, the phrase became a term of law with a precise scope.","whyCN":"当条约需要共同的判定标准，这个短语就成了范围精确的法律术语。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Marine pollution joins Latin marinus 'of the sea' with Latin polluere 'to defile', whose deeper history is not fully settled. The phrase is a modern legal and scientific collocation. Dates are approximate.","cn":"marine pollution 把拉丁 marinus「海的」与拉丁 polluere「弄脏、亵渎」并置，后者更深的历史并无定论。这个短语是近代法律与科学搭配。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN MARE","en":"Mare 'sea' gave marinus 'of the sea', borrowed into English as marine; the deeper origin of mare is uncertain.","cn":"mare「海」形成 marinus「海的」，借入英语作 marine；mare 的更深来源不确定。"},{"era":"LATIN POLLUERE","en":"Polluere meant 'to defile, contaminate'; it is often analysed as a prefix plus a washing root, but the details are disputed.","cn":"polluere 意为「弄脏、污染」；常被分析为前缀加「洗」的词根，但具体细节有争议。"},{"era":"POLLUTION IN ENGLISH","en":"English pollution first meant moral defilement before it came to mean physical contamination.","cn":"英语 pollution 最初指道德上的玷污，后来才指物理污染。"},{"era":"MARINE EXTENSION","en":"Marine was attached once pollution law needed to separate the sea from rivers and air.","cn":"当污染法需要把海洋与河流、空气分开，marine 便被加在前面。"},{"era":"TWENTIETH-CENTURY LAW","en":"Mid-century oil-spill treaties made marine pollution a standard legal term with duties to prevent and control.","cn":"二十世纪中叶的溢油条约使 marine pollution 成为带有预防与控制义务的标准法律术语。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin): the pre-Latin source of mare is unknown, the internal history of polluere is disputed, and the first use of the exact phrase is not precisely dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源）：mare 在拉丁语之前的来源不明，polluere 的内部历史有争议，确切短语最早的用法没有精确年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the same-root pollution family; group two holds specific marine impacts often used as if they were synonyms.","cn":"第一组是同根 pollution 词族；第二组是常被当作同义词使用的具体海洋影响。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"pollution","ipa":"/pəˈluːʃn/","tag":"the general term","definition":"Contamination of any environment; marine pollution restricts it to the sea.","definitionCN":"任何环境的污染；marine pollution 把它限定到海洋。"},{"word":"pollute","ipa":"/pəˈluːt/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To make something impure; it names the act, while marine pollution names the resulting condition.","definitionCN":"使某物变脏；它指行为，而 marine pollution 指由此形成的状态。"},{"word":"pollutant","ipa":"/pəˈluːtənt/","tag":"the substance","definition":"A specific contaminating substance; marine pollution is the whole input and its effects, not one substance.","definitionCN":"具体的污染物质；marine pollution 指整体输入及其影响，不是某一种物质。"},{"word":"marine","ipa":"/məˈriːn/","tag":"adjective, the locator","definition":"Relating to the sea; it only says where the pollution occurs, not that pollution exists.","definitionCN":"与海有关的；它只说污染发生在哪里，并不表示污染本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"contamination","ipa":"/kənˌtæmɪˈneɪʃn/","tag":"presence of a harmful agent","definition":"The presence of a harmful agent in a place or organism; it is narrower than the whole pollution process.","definitionCN":"有害因子出现在某处或某生物体内；它比整个污染过程窄。"},{"word":"eutrophication","ipa":"/ˌjuːtrəfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"nutrient-driven","definition":"Enrichment by nutrients that causes blooms and low oxygen; it is one major form of marine pollution.","definitionCN":"营养盐富集造成藻华与低氧；它是海洋污染的一种主要形式。"},{"word":"oil spill","ipa":"/ɔɪl spɪl/","tag":"one event","definition":"A single release of oil; marine pollution covers spills along with chronic inputs from many sources.","definitionCN":"一次石油泄漏；海洋污染还涵盖许多来源的长期输入。"},{"word":"marine debris","ipa":"/məˈriːn dɪˈbriː/","tag":"solid waste","definition":"Solid manufactured waste in the sea; it is the visible part of marine pollution, not the whole.","definitionCN":"海中的固体人造垃圾；它是海洋污染可见的一部分，而非全部。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real Latin parts, real treaty terms and real source categories.","cn":"正常联想：真实的拉丁构件、真实条约术语与真实来源类别。"},"normal":[{"en":"Marine means of the sea; pollution means making impure.","cn":"marine 是海的；pollution 是使变脏。"},{"en":"Most marine pollution starts on land and travels downhill.","cn":"大部分海洋污染从陆地开始，顺流而下。"},{"en":"Oil, plastic, nutrients, chemicals and noise are the main families.","cn":"油、塑料、营养盐、化学品与噪声是主要类别。"},{"en":"The law defines pollution by harm, not by the pipe it came from.","cn":"法律按危害而非管道来源来定义污染。"},{"en":"A dead zone is nutrient pollution seen from space.","cn":"死区是从太空看得见的营养盐污染。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a river carrying a city's hidden waste into a blue bowl.","cn":"想象一条河把城市隐形的废物带进一只蓝色的大碗。"},{"en":"Picture plastic breaking into pieces smaller than the plankton that eat them.","cn":"想象塑料裂成比吃它的浮游生物还小的碎片。"},{"en":"Picture a whale trying to sing through a wall of ship noise.","cn":"想象一头鲸试图穿过一堵船噪声的墙来歌唱。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Marine pollution from the river closed the shellfish beds.","cn":"来自河流的海洋污染使贝类养殖区关闭。"},{"en":"The treaty targets marine pollution from ships first.","cn":"该条约首先针对来自船舶的海洋污染。"},{"en":"Marine pollution knows no border, so states must act together.","cn":"海洋污染不分国界，因此各国必须共同行动。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「marine（海洋的）+ pollution（污染）」——进入海洋并造成危害的污染 → 海洋污染","word":"marine pollution"},"root":"拉丁 mare「海」（更深来源不确定）→ marinus「海的」→ 英语 marine；拉丁 polluere「弄脏、污染」→ pollu- + -tion → pollution。polluere 的内部历史有争议，短语为近代法律与科学搭配。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one harmful input: total contamination, land runoff, oil, plastic, nutrients, chemicals, noise and the legal definition.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一种有害输入展开：总污染、陆源径流、石油、塑料、营养盐、化学品、噪声与法律定义。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: an oil film on the water outside an estuary, with plastic fragments and foam mixed into the waves.","cn":"核心意象：河口外的水面浮着油膜，塑料碎片与泡沫混进浪花。"},"chain":["TOTAL CONTAMINATION","LAND-BASED INPUTS","OIL SPILLS","PLASTICS","NUTRIENT OVERLOAD","LEGAL DEFINITION"],"branches":[{"senses":"02 · 05","en":"LAND TO SEA: fertilizer and sewage enter by rivers and become nutrient overload offshore.","cn":"从陆到海：化肥与污水经河流进入，在近海变成营养盐过量。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"VISIBLE AND INVISIBLE: a spill is seen at once, while chemical loads accumulate quietly in tissue.","cn":"可见与不可见：溢油立刻被看见，化学负荷却在组织里悄悄累积。"},{"senses":"04","en":"THE DEBRIS: plastic is an input the law must treat as pollution.","cn":"垃圾：塑料是法律必须视为污染的输入。"},{"senses":"01 · 08","en":"CONDITION TO LAW: a described harm becomes a treaty term with duties attached.","cn":"从状态到法律：被描述的危害变成附有义务的条约术语。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE NOISE: sound itself counts as pollution.","cn":"噪声：声音本身也算作污染。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Marine pollution is a two-word Latin-derived phrase; the second word has a verb, a noun and an agent form, so the family is easy to read.","cn":"marine pollution 是由两个拉丁来源词构成的短语；第二个词有动词、名词与施事形式，词族容易读出。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Mare gives marine; polluere gives pollute, pollution and pollutant. The two Latin lines meet in this modern compound.","cn":"mare 提供 marine；polluere 提供 pollute、pollution 与 pollutant。两条拉丁线索在这个近代复合词中相遇。"},"items":[{"word":"marine","structure":"Latin marinus 'of the sea'","meaning":"relating to the sea","meaningCN":"海的；海洋的","example":"Marine life suffers first at the surface.","exampleCN":"海洋生命最先在表层受害。"},{"word":"pollute","structure":"Latin polluere 'to defile'","meaning":"to make impure","meaningCN":"使变脏；污染","example":"The factory polluted the bay.","exampleCN":"工厂污染了海湾。"},{"word":"pollution","structure":"pollu- + -tion (action or state)","meaning":"the state of being contaminated","meaningCN":"受污染的状态","example":"Pollution closed the beach.","exampleCN":"污染使海滩关闭。"},{"word":"pollutant","structure":"pollute + -ant (agent noun)","meaning":"a contaminating substance","meaningCN":"污染物质","example":"The pollutant persists for decades.","exampleCN":"这种污染物会存留数十年。"},{"word":"polluter","structure":"pollute + -er (one who)","meaning":"a person or body that pollutes","meaningCN":"造成污染者","example":"The polluter pays under the treaty.","exampleCN":"根据条约，污染者付费。"},{"word":"polluted","structure":"pollute + -ed","meaning":"contaminated","meaningCN":"受污染的","example":"Polluted sediment harms bottom feeders.","exampleCN":"受污染沉积物伤害底栖摄食者。"},{"word":"marine pollution","structure":"marine + pollution (compound noun)","meaning":"harmful input to the sea","meaningCN":"进入海洋的有害输入","example":"Marine pollution crosses national borders.","exampleCN":"海洋污染跨越国界。"},{"word":"marine-pollution","structure":"compound used attributively","meaning":"of marine pollution","meaningCN":"海洋污染的","example":"Marine-pollution rules cover plastics.","exampleCN":"海洋污染规定涵盖塑料。"},{"word":"eutrophication","structure":"Greek eu- 'good' + trophe 'food' + -ation","meaning":"nutrient enrichment of water","meaningCN":"水体营养盐富集","example":"Eutrophication follows nutrient pollution.","exampleCN":"富营养化紧随营养盐污染。"},{"word":"debris","structure":"French débris 'rubble'","meaning":"scattered fragments, especially waste","meaningCN":"散落的碎片，尤指垃圾","example":"Marine debris gathers on the tide line.","exampleCN":"海洋垃圾聚集在潮线。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"mare","structure":"mare, maris (n., third declension)","meaning":"sea","meaningCN":"海"},{"word":"marinus","structure":"marinus, marina, marinum (adjective)","meaning":"of the sea","meaningCN":"海的"},{"word":"polluere","structure":"polluere, pollui, pollutum (verb, third conjugation)","meaning":"to defile, contaminate","meaningCN":"弄脏；污染"}]}},{"word":"overfishing","ipa_uk":"/ˌəʊvəˈfɪʃɪŋ/","ipa_us":"/ˌoʊvərˈfɪʃɪŋ/","definition_zh":"过度捕捞；捕捞超过可持续产量；生长型过度捕捞；补充型过度捕捞；经济型过度捕捞；生态系统型过度捕捞","definition_en":"fishing at a rate that removes fish faster than the population can replace them","core_image":"渔网从海里拉起，网眼里的鱼越来越小、越来越少","scene":"清晨的码头上，渔民把一网小鱼倒进筐里，最大的也不过手掌长。Biologists warn that overfishing has emptied the grounds their grandparents knew.","sceneCN":"这里指「捕捞速度超过鱼类自我补充能力」（第 1 个义项：从种群中取走的鱼多于其繁殖补充的总过程）；句意为生物学家警告，过度捕捞已经掏空了祖辈熟悉的老渔场。场景物件：渔网、小鱼、鱼筐、码头。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"过度捕捞（不可数；作动名词用）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"overfishing of a stock","zh":"对某一种群的过度捕捞"},{"phrase":"global overfishing","zh":"全球过度捕捞"},{"phrase":"overfishing and bycatch","zh":"过度捕捞与兼捕"},{"phrase":"end overfishing","zh":"终止过度捕捞"},{"phrase":"overfishing driven by subsidies","zh":"补贴驱动的过度捕捞"},{"phrase":"the science of overfishing","zh":"过度捕捞科学"}],"forms":[{"label":"相关动词（过度捕捞）","form":"overfish"},{"label":"相关形容词（已被过度捕捞的）","form":"overfished"},{"label":"动名词（过度捕捞）","form":"overfishing"},{"label":"相关名词（鱼）","form":"fish"},{"label":"相关名词（渔场；渔业）","form":"fishery"},{"label":"相关名词（渔业；渔场，复数）","form":"fisheries"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"overfish","pos":"v.","zh":"过度捕捞"},{"word":"overfished","pos":"adj.","zh":"已被过度捕捞的"},{"word":"fish","pos":"n./v.","zh":"鱼；捕鱼"},{"word":"fishery","pos":"n.","zh":"渔场；渔业"},{"word":"fisheries","pos":"n.","zh":"渔业；渔场（复数）"},{"word":"fishing","pos":"n.","zh":"捕鱼；渔业"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Fishing beyond replacement","titleCN":"超过补充能力的捕捞","definition":"fishing at a rate that removes fish faster than the population can replace them","definitionCN":"捕走鱼的速度快于种群繁殖补充的速度","example":"Biologists warn that overfishing has emptied the grounds their grandparents knew.","exampleCN":"生物学家警告，过度捕捞已经掏空了祖辈熟悉的老渔场。","why":"Over- marks excess and fishing marks the taking, so the word is the simple idea of taking more than the stock can give back.","whyCN":"over- 标记过量，fishing 标记捕取，因此这个词就是「取得比资源能还回来的更多」这一简单观念。"},{"no":"02","title":"Growth overfishing","titleCN":"生长型过度捕捞","definition":"taking fish so young that the stock loses the yield it would have gained if they had grown","definitionCN":"捕走太幼小的鱼，使资源失去它们长大本可带来的产量","example":"Growth overfishing shows up as smaller fish in every catch.","exampleCN":"生长型过度捕捞表现为每网鱼都更小。","why":"Fisheries science splits the problem by mechanism, and this first type is about individual growth rather than births.","whyCN":"渔业科学按机制拆分问题，这第一种关于个体生长，而不是出生。"},{"no":"03","title":"Recruitment overfishing","titleCN":"补充型过度捕捞","definition":"taking so many adults that too few remain to produce the next generation","definitionCN":"捕走太多成鱼，剩下的个体不足以繁殖下一代","example":"Recruitment overfishing leaves too few spawners for a good year class.","exampleCN":"补充型过度捕捞留下的产卵鱼太少，难以形成好年级群。","why":"The second type attacks the birth side of the equation, so the stock loses its capacity to recruit new fish.","whyCN":"第二种类型打击等式出生的一端，资源因此失去补充新鱼的能力。"},{"no":"04","title":"Economic overfishing","titleCN":"经济型过度捕捞","definition":"keeping more fishing capacity than the stock can support profitably","definitionCN":"保有的捕捞能力超过资源能有利可图支撑的水平","example":"Economic overfishing persists even when catch limits are set.","exampleCN":"即使设定了捕捞上限，经济型过度捕捞仍然存在。","why":"Boats can chase too few fish because subsidies and competition keep them at sea, so the problem is economic as well as biological.","whyCN":"补贴与竞争让船继续出海，去追已经太少的鱼，因此问题既是生物性的，也是经济性的。"},{"no":"05","title":"Ecosystem overfishing","titleCN":"生态系统型过度捕捞","definition":"fishing that alters the balance of species and food webs, not just the target stock","definitionCN":"改变物种平衡与食物网、而不只影响目标种群的捕捞","example":"Ecosystem overfishing removed the large predators first.","exampleCN":"生态系统型过度捕捞先移除了大型捕食者。","why":"When the catch reshapes the whole community, the word widens from one stock to the system.","whyCN":"当捕捞重塑整个群落，这个词就从单一资源扩展到整个系统。"},{"no":"06","title":"Stock collapse","titleCN":"资源崩溃","definition":"the end state in which a stock falls so low that the fishery can no longer operate","definitionCN":"资源低到渔业无法再运作的终局状态","example":"Overfishing brought the cod stock to collapse.","exampleCN":"过度捕捞把鳕鱼资源推向崩溃。","why":"Because the process has a visible endpoint, the word often stands for the collapse it causes.","whyCN":"因为这一过程有可见的终点，这个词常直接指它造成的崩溃。"},{"no":"07","title":"A policy target","titleCN":"政策治理对象","definition":"the problem that catch limits, subsidies reform and closed seasons are meant to solve","definitionCN":"捕捞上限、补贴改革与禁渔期旨在解决的问题","example":"The plan aims to end overfishing by a fixed date.","exampleCN":"该计划目标是在既定日期前终止过度捕捞。","why":"Once the process was measured, it became something governments could legislate against.","whyCN":"一旦这个过程可测量，它就变成政府可以立法应对的对象。"},{"no":"08","title":"Figurative over-extraction","titleCN":"比喻义：过度索取","definition":"taking more from any limited resource than it can renew","definitionCN":"从任何有限资源中取走超过其再生能力的东西","example":"The startup suffered overfishing of its best engineers.","exampleCN":"这家初创公司对最优秀工程师的「过度捕捞」使其受损。","why":"The fishing image is easy to borrow for any finite pool of talent or attention, so the word can leave the sea.","whyCN":"捕鱼的意象很容易借给任何有限的人才或注意力池，因此这个词可以离开海洋。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Overfishing joins the native prefix over- 'too much' to fishing, whose root fish descends from Old English fisc and Germanic *fiskaz. The compound is modern resource science. Dates are approximate.","cn":"overfishing 把本族前缀 over-「过多」与 fishing 组合，后者的词根 fish 出自古英语 fisc 与日耳曼语 *fiskaz。这个复合词属现代资源科学。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH OFER","en":"Ofer 'over, beyond' is the native source of over-, marking excess or going beyond a limit.","cn":"ofer「在上、超过」是 over- 的本族来源，标记过量或越界。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH FISC","en":"Fisc 'fish' descends from Germanic *fiskaz, a reconstructed form related to Latin piscis.","cn":"fisc「鱼」出自日耳曼语 *fiskaz，此为重构形式，与拉丁 piscis 同源。"},{"era":"FISHING","en":"The gerund fishing names the activity of catching fish; it is formed from the verb fish plus -ing.","cn":"动名词 fishing 指捕鱼活动，由动词 fish 加 -ing 构成。"},{"era":"MODERN RESOURCE TERM","en":"Overfishing became a technical term in twentieth-century fisheries science, once catch statistics could be compared with stock growth.","cn":"二十世纪渔业科学能把渔获统计与资源生长相比较之后，overfishing 成为技术术语。"},{"era":"SUBTYPES","en":"Later work split the idea into growth, recruitment, economic and ecosystem overfishing, each naming a different failure.","cn":"后来的研究把它拆成生长型、补充型、经济型与生态系统型，每种各指一种不同的失灵。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin): the pre-Germanic source of *fiskaz is not settled, and the first use of overfishing in its modern technical sense is not precisely dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源）：*fiskaz 在日耳曼语之前的来源无定论，overfishing 现代技术义的最早使用没有精确年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds same-root fish and fishery forms; group two holds related catch and depletion terms that are not synonyms.","cn":"第一组是同根 fish 与 fishery 形式；第二组是相关但并非同义的捕捞与枯竭术语。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"overfish","ipa":"/ˌəʊvəˈfɪʃ/","tag":"the verb","definition":"To fish a stock too hard; the verb names the act, while overfishing names the process and its state.","definitionCN":"把资源捕得太狠；动词指行为，overfishing 指过程与状态。"},{"word":"overfished","ipa":"/ˌəʊvəˈfɪʃt/","tag":"the resulting state","definition":"Describing a stock already reduced below safe limits; it is the condition, not the activity.","definitionCN":"描述资源已被压到安全线以下；它是状态，不是活动。"},{"word":"fishing","ipa":"/ˈfɪʃɪŋ/","tag":"the neutral activity","definition":"Catching fish in general; overfishing adds that the rate is beyond replacement.","definitionCN":"泛指捕鱼；overfishing 追加了「超过补充速度」这一层。"},{"word":"fishery","ipa":"/ˈfɪʃəri/","tag":"the unit, not the problem","definition":"A stock, ground or industry; it is what overfishing damages, not the damage itself.","definitionCN":"资源、渔场或产业；它是过度捕捞损害的对象，而不是损害本身。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"overharvesting","ipa":"/ˌəʊvəˈhɑːvɪstɪŋ/","tag":"broader taking","definition":"Taking any wild resource beyond renewal; it can apply to forests and plants, while overfishing is marine and fish-specific.","definitionCN":"取走任何野生资源超过其再生；可用于森林与植物，而过度捕捞专指鱼类与海洋。"},{"word":"bycatch","ipa":"/ˈbaɪkætʃ/","tag":"unintended catch","definition":"Non-target animals caught accidentally; it is a separate harm that often accompanies overfishing.","definitionCN":"意外捕到的非目标动物；它是常与过度捕捞并行的另一种危害。"},{"word":"stock depletion","ipa":"/stɒk dɪˈpliːʃn/","tag":"the result","definition":"The reduction of a fish stock; it is the outcome that overfishing produces.","definitionCN":"鱼类资源的减少；它是过度捕捞造成的结果。"},{"word":"sustainable yield","ipa":"/səˈsteɪnəbl jiːld/","tag":"the limit","definition":"The catch a stock can give year after year; overfishing is fishing above that limit.","definitionCN":"资源年复一年能提供的渔获；过度捕捞就是超过这一上限。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real native parts, real fisheries categories and real management collocations.","cn":"正常联想：真实本族构件、真实渔业类别与真实管理搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"Over- means too much; fishing means taking fish.","cn":"over- 是太多，fishing 是捕鱼。"},{"en":"The four subtypes are growth, recruitment, economic and ecosystem.","cn":"四个子类是生长型、补充型、经济型与生态系统型。"},{"en":"Fish is fisc in Old English, related to Latin piscis.","cn":"fish 在古英语是 fisc，与拉丁 piscis 同源。"},{"en":"Bycatch is a separate problem that often travels with overfishing.","cn":"兼捕是与过度捕捞常同行的另一个问题。"},{"en":"The fix is a catch limit set below sustainable yield.","cn":"解决办法是把捕捞上限设在可持续产量之下。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a net coming up with smaller and smaller fish each season.","cn":"想象每一季拉上来的网里，鱼越来越小。"},{"en":"Picture a bank account emptied faster than interest can refill it.","cn":"想象一本账户，取钱快过利息回填。"},{"en":"Picture a food web losing its top strand first.","cn":"想象一张食物网先失去最上面那股线。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Overfishing removed the oldest and largest fish first.","cn":"过度捕捞先移走最老最大的鱼。"},{"en":"Subsidies can keep overfishing profitable for a while.","cn":"补贴能让过度捕捞在一段时间内仍有利可图。"},{"en":"The stock recovered only after overfishing was ended.","cn":"资源只有在过度捕捞终止后才恢复。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「over（过度）+ fishing（捕鱼）」——捕得比鱼能补回来的更多 → 过度捕捞","word":"overfishing"},"root":"over- 出自古英语 ofer「在上、超过」；fish 出自古英语 fisc，属日耳曼语 *fiskaz（重构形式），与拉丁 piscis 同源；加 -ing 构成动名词。现代技术义形成于二十世纪渔业科学。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one excess: taking beyond replacement, the growth type, the recruitment type, the economic type, the ecosystem type, collapse, policy, and any over-extraction.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一种「过量」展开：超过补充、生长型、补充型、经济型、生态系统型、崩溃、政策，以及任何过度索取。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a net hauled up full of small fish that never had time to grow.","cn":"核心意象：拉上来的网里全是还没来得及长大的小鱼。"},"chain":["EXCEEDING YIELD","GROWTH OVERFISHING","RECRUITMENT OVERFISHING","ECONOMIC OVERFISHING","ECOSYSTEM OVERFISHING","STOCK COLLAPSE"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"RATE TO SIZE: taking too many small fish is the first way the rate shows up.","cn":"从速度到体型：捕走太多小鱼，是这一速度最先显现的方式。"},{"senses":"03 · 06","en":"BIRTH TO COLLAPSE: too few spawners is how a stock loses its next generation and then its fishery.","cn":"从出生到崩溃：产卵鱼太少，资源先失去下一代，再失去渔业。"},{"senses":"04 · 07","en":"PROFIT TO POLICY: subsidies keep excess capacity alive, so reform must change the economics.","cn":"从利润到政策：补贴让过剩产能存活，改革必须改变经济账。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE ECOSYSTEM: catch the whole food web and collapse becomes hard to reverse.","cn":"生态系统：捕空整张食物网，崩溃就更难逆转。"},{"senses":"08","en":"OVER-EXTRACTION METAPHOR: any finite pool can be fished too hard, including talent.","cn":"过度索取比喻：任何有限的池子都可能被捕得太狠，包括人才。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Overfishing is a native prefix plus a gerund; there is no borrowed affix, and the meaning is the sum of its two visible parts.","cn":"overfishing 由本族前缀加动名词构成；没有借来词缀，意义就是两个可见部分之和。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin layer appears only through the distant relative piscis 'fish'; the word itself is native English and Germanic.","cn":"拉丁层只通过远亲 piscis「鱼」出现；这个词本身属英语本族与日耳曼语。"},"items":[{"word":"over-","structure":"Old English ofer 'over, beyond'","meaning":"too much; beyond a limit","meaningCN":"过多；越过界限","example":"Over- turns a normal action into an excess.","exampleCN":"over- 把正常动作变成过量。"},{"word":"fish","structure":"Old English fisc, Germanic *fiskaz","meaning":"a fish; to catch fish","meaningCN":"鱼；捕鱼","example":"They fish the same bank every spring.","exampleCN":"他们每年春天在同一片滩捕鱼。"},{"word":"fishing","structure":"fish + -ing (gerund)","meaning":"the activity of catching fish","meaningCN":"捕鱼活动","example":"Fishing supports the whole port.","exampleCN":"捕鱼支撑着整个港口。"},{"word":"overfish","structure":"over- + fish (verb)","meaning":"to fish too hard","meaningCN":"过度捕捞","example":"Fleets overfish the shared stock.","exampleCN":"船队过度捕捞共享资源。"},{"word":"overfished","structure":"overfish + -ed","meaning":"already fished below safe limits","meaningCN":"已被捕到安全线以下的","example":"The overfished bank closed for a year.","exampleCN":"过度捕捞的渔场关闭了一年。"},{"word":"overfishing","structure":"overfish + -ing (gerund)","meaning":"the process of fishing beyond replacement","meaningCN":"超过补充速度的捕捞过程","example":"Overfishing is the main cause of collapse.","exampleCN":"过度捕捞是资源崩溃的主要原因。"},{"word":"fishery","structure":"fish + -ery (place or practice)","meaning":"a fishing ground or industry","meaningCN":"渔场或渔业","example":"The fishery employs three hundred people.","exampleCN":"该渔业雇了三百人。"},{"word":"fisheries","structure":"fishery + plural -ies","meaning":"several fisheries","meaningCN":"多个渔业或渔场","example":"Fisheries share the same limit.","exampleCN":"各渔业共享同一上限。"},{"word":"bycatch","structure":"by- 'aside' + catch","meaning":"unintended catch of non-target animals","meaningCN":"意外捕到的非目标动物","example":"Bycatch includes turtles and young fish.","exampleCN":"兼捕包括海龟与幼鱼。"},{"word":"sustainable yield","structure":"sustainable + yield (compound)","meaning":"the catch that can be taken year after year","meaningCN":"年复一年可取的渔获","example":"The limit is set below sustainable yield.","exampleCN":"上限设在可持续产量之下。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"piscis","structure":"piscis, piscis (m., third declension)","meaning":"fish","meaningCN":"鱼"}]}},{"word":"fisheries","ipa_uk":"/ˈfɪʃəriz/","ipa_us":"/ˈfɪʃəriz/","definition_zh":"渔业；渔场；渔业资源；捕捞与养殖产业；内陆渔业；渔业管理","definition_en":"the industries and systems that catch, manage and sometimes farm fish and other aquatic organisms","core_image":"港口里渔船并排靠岸，冰面上摊着不同大小的鱼，拍卖牌不停翻动","scene":"天还没亮，港口已经挤满渔船，拍卖员举着牌子喊出第一筐鱼的价格。Fisheries across the region agreed to a shared catch limit.","sceneCN":"这里指「捕捞与管理水产品的产业体系」（第 1 个义项：以捕获、养殖与经营鱼类及其他水生物为业的行业整体）；句意为本区域各渔业同意接受一个共享的捕捞上限。场景物件：渔船、鱼筐、冰面、拍卖牌。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"渔业；渔场（fishery 的复数，常作集合名词）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"marine fisheries","zh":"海洋渔业"},{"phrase":"inland fisheries","zh":"内陆渔业"},{"phrase":"fisheries management","zh":"渔业管理"},{"phrase":"fisheries science","zh":"渔业科学"},{"phrase":"small-scale fisheries","zh":"小规模渔业"},{"phrase":"shared fisheries","zh":"共享渔业"},{"phrase":"fisheries subsidies","zh":"渔业补贴"}],"forms":[{"label":"单数（渔业；渔场）","form":"fishery"},{"label":"复数","form":"fisheries"},{"label":"相关动词（捕鱼）","form":"fish"},{"label":"相关名词（渔民；渔船）","form":"fisher"},{"label":"相关名词（捕鱼活动）","form":"fishing"},{"label":"定语形式（渔业的）","form":"fishery"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"fishery","pos":"n.","zh":"渔业；渔场"},{"word":"fish","pos":"n./v.","zh":"鱼；捕鱼"},{"word":"fisher","pos":"n.","zh":"渔民；渔船"},{"word":"fishing","pos":"n.","zh":"捕鱼；渔业"},{"word":"fisherman","pos":"n.","zh":"渔民"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The industry as a whole","titleCN":"渔业产业","definition":"the industries and systems that catch, manage and sometimes farm fish and other aquatic organisms","definitionCN":"以捕获、管理并有时养殖鱼类及其他水生物为业的产业与体系","example":"Fisheries across the region agreed to a shared catch limit.","exampleCN":"本区域各渔业同意接受一个共享的捕捞上限。","why":"The plural of fishery can name the whole sector, not just several fishing grounds, because the industry is made of many units.","whyCN":"fishery 的复数可指整个行业，而不只是几处渔场，因为产业由许多单元组成。"},{"no":"02","title":"Fishing grounds","titleCN":"渔场","definition":"the places where commercial fishing takes place","definitionCN":"商业捕捞实际进行的海域或水域","example":"The northern fisheries closed after the stock fell.","exampleCN":"资源下降后，北方各渔场关闭了。","why":"A fishery is first a place on the water, so the plural can simply mean several grounds.","whyCN":"fishery 首先是水面上的一个地点，因此复数可以只指几处渔场。"},{"no":"03","title":"Fleets and operations","titleCN":"船队与作业单位","definition":"the boats, gear and crews that work a stock","definitionCN":"作业于某一资源的船只、渔具与船员","example":"Artisanal fisheries use smaller boats than industrial ones.","exampleCN":"手工渔业使用的船比工业渔业小。","why":"Management counts capacity, so the word can mean the operating units rather than the fish or the place.","whyCN":"管理要统计产能，因此这个词也可指作业单元，而不是鱼或地点。"},{"no":"04","title":"Fish stocks","titleCN":"渔业资源","definition":"the populations of fish that a fishery harvests","definitionCN":"渔业所收获的鱼类种群","example":"Shared fisheries require joint stock assessments.","exampleCN":"共享渔业需要联合的资源评估。","why":"A fishery is also shorthand for the stock it depends on, because management is written about the two together.","whyCN":"fishery 也常简称它所依赖的资源，因为管理文本把两者写在一起。"},{"no":"05","title":"The sector including aquaculture","titleCN":"含养殖的行业口径","definition":"the wider food sector that includes capture fisheries and fish farming","definitionCN":"包含捕捞渔业与鱼类养殖的更宽食品行业","example":"Global fisheries now produce more farmed than wild fish.","exampleCN":"全球渔业如今生产的养殖鱼多于野生鱼。","why":"Statistical agencies group capture and culture under one heading, so the plural widened to cover both.","whyCN":"统计机构把捕捞与养殖归在同一标题下，因此复数扩展到两者。"},{"no":"06","title":"Inland fisheries","titleCN":"内陆渔业","definition":"fisheries in rivers, lakes and reservoirs rather than the sea","definitionCN":"河流、湖泊与水库而非海中的渔业","example":"Inland fisheries feed millions of people.","exampleCN":"内陆渔业养活了数百万人。","why":"The same activity happens in fresh water, so the plural needed a modifier rather than a new word.","whyCN":"同一活动也发生在淡水中，因此复数只需加修饰语，而不必另造新词。"},{"no":"07","title":"Management and science","titleCN":"管理与科学","definition":"the agencies, rules and assessments that regulate fishing","definitionCN":"规范捕捞的机构、规则与评估","example":"Fisheries science sets the limit, and fisheries policy enforces it.","exampleCN":"渔业科学设定上限，渔业政策负责执行。","why":"Because the word appears constantly in regulation, it can stand for the management system itself.","whyCN":"因为这个词不断出现在法规中，它可以指管理体系本身。"},{"no":"08","title":"Access rights and jurisdiction","titleCN":"渔业权与管辖","definition":"the legal rights to fish a stock or in a zone","definitionCN":"在某资源或某区域捕鱼的法定权利","example":"The two states share fisheries in the strait.","exampleCN":"两国共享海峡内的渔业权。","why":"Law treats the right to fish as a kind of property, so the plural can name those rights.","whyCN":"法律把捕鱼权当作一种财产，因此复数可以指这些权利。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Fisheries is the plural of fishery, formed from native fish plus the place-and-practice suffix -ery, which came through French from Latin -aria. Dates are approximate.","cn":"fisheries 是 fishery 的复数，由本族词 fish 加表示地点与行业的后缀 -ery 构成，后者经法语来自拉丁 -aria。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"OLD ENGLISH FISC","en":"Fisc 'fish' descends from Germanic *fiskaz, a reconstructed form related to Latin piscis.","cn":"fisc「鱼」出自日耳曼语 *fiskaz，此为重构形式，与拉丁 piscis 同源。"},{"era":"SUFFIX -ERY","en":"The suffix -ery came through Old French -erie from Latin -aria, naming a place where something is done or a collective practice.","cn":"后缀 -ery 经古法语 -erie 来自拉丁 -aria，命名做事的地点或集合性的行业。"},{"era":"FISHERY","en":"Fishery first named a place for catching fish, then the business carried on there.","cn":"fishery 最初指捕鱼的地点，随后指在那里进行的生意。"},{"era":"PLURAL WIDENING","en":"The plural fisheries widened from several grounds to the whole industry and its management systems.","cn":"复数 fisheries 从几处渔场扩展到整个产业及其管理体系。"},{"era":"MODERN SCOPE","en":"Twentieth-century statistics extended fisheries to include aquaculture and inland capture, making it a sector term.","cn":"二十世纪统计把水产养殖与内陆捕捞纳入 fisheries，使其成为行业术语。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin): the pre-Germanic source of *fiskaz is not settled, and the first use of fisheries as a sector term is not precisely dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源）：*fiskaz 在日耳曼语之前的来源无定论，fisheries 作为行业术语的最早使用没有精确年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds singular, plural and personal forms of the same fish family; group two holds neighbouring food-sector and management terms.","cn":"第一组是同一 fish 词族的单数、复数与人物形式；第二组是邻近的食品行业与管理术语。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"fishery","ipa":"/ˈfɪʃəri/","tag":"singular","definition":"One ground, stock or business; fisheries can mean several of them or the whole sector.","definitionCN":"一处渔场、一份资源或一家企业；fisheries 可指数个，也可指整个行业。"},{"word":"fisher","ipa":"/ˈfɪʃə/","tag":"person or boat","definition":"A person who fishes or a fishing vessel; it is an agent, not the industry.","definitionCN":"捕鱼的人或渔船；它是施事者，不是行业。"},{"word":"fishing","ipa":"/ˈfɪʃɪŋ/","tag":"the activity","definition":"The act or sport of catching fish; fisheries is the organized industry and its management.","definitionCN":"捕鱼的行为或运动；fisheries 是有组织的产业及其管理。"},{"word":"fish","ipa":"/fɪʃ/","tag":"the animal","definition":"The animal itself; the plural fisheries names the human system built around catching it.","definitionCN":"动物本身；fisheries 指围绕捕捉它建立的人类体系。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"aquaculture","ipa":"/ˈækwəkʌltʃə/","tag":"farming, not capture","definition":"The farming of aquatic organisms; it is included in the broad sector but is not capture fishing.","definitionCN":"水生物的养殖；它被纳入宽口径行业，但不是捕捞。"},{"word":"fish stock","ipa":"/fɪʃ stɒk/","tag":"the resource","definition":"A population of fish treated as a harvestable unit; fisheries depend on stocks but are not the stocks.","definitionCN":"被当作可收获取单元的鱼类种群；渔业依赖资源，但不等同于资源。"},{"word":"catch","ipa":"/kætʃ/","tag":"the landed amount","definition":"The fish actually taken; it is the output of a fishery, not the system.","definitionCN":"实际捕到的鱼；它是渔业的产出，不是体系本身。"},{"word":"fisheries management","ipa":"/ˈfɪʃəriz ˈmænɪdʒmənt/","tag":"the control system","definition":"The rules and assessments that regulate fishing; it is one part of fisheries, not the whole sector.","definitionCN":"规范捕捞的规则与评估；它是渔业的一部分，不是整个行业。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real suffix history, real sector categories and real management collocations.","cn":"正常联想：真实后缀历史、真实行业类别与真实管理搭配。"},"normal":[{"en":"Fish plus -ery makes fishery, a place and practice of catching fish.","cn":"fish 加 -ery 构成 fishery，即捕鱼的地点与行业。"},{"en":"Fisheries is simply the plural, but it often names the whole sector.","cn":"fisheries 只是复数，却常指整个行业。"},{"en":"Marine and inland are the two great divisions.","cn":"海洋与内陆是两大分区。"},{"en":"Fisheries science sets limits; fisheries policy enforces them.","cn":"渔业科学设上限，渔业政策执行上限。"},{"en":"The broad sector now includes aquaculture as well as capture.","cn":"宽口径行业如今既含捕捞也含养殖。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a harbour before dawn, every boat carrying a share of one shared stock.","cn":"想象黎明前的港口，每条船都载着同一份共享资源的一部分。"},{"en":"Picture a ledger where catches, limits and licenses are written on the same page.","cn":"想象一本账，渔获、上限与许可证写在同一页。"},{"en":"Picture a single fish counted by a scientist, a boat and a treaty at once.","cn":"想象同一条鱼同时被科学家、渔船与条约计算。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Small-scale fisheries employ most of the region's coastal workers.","cn":"小规模渔业雇用了该区域大部分沿海劳动者。"},{"en":"Fisheries and conservation groups negotiated the closed season.","cn":"渔业与保护团体谈判确定了禁渔期。"},{"en":"Inland fisheries collapsed after the dam blocked the migration.","cn":"水坝阻断洄游后，内陆渔业崩溃。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「fish（鱼）+ -ery（行业/场所）+ 复数」——捕鱼的行业与渔场 → 渔业","word":"fisheries"},"root":"fish 出自古英语 fisc，属日耳曼语 *fiskaz（重构形式），与拉丁 piscis 同源；后缀 -ery 经古法语 -erie 来自拉丁 -aria，表示地点或行业；fishery 加复数 -ies 成 fisheries，现代常指整个渔业部门。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one industry: the sector, the grounds, the fleets, the stocks, the wider scope, inland fisheries, management and access rights.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一行业展开：产业、渔场、船队、资源、宽口径、内陆渔业、管理与渔业权。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a harbour at dawn, boats side by side, iced fish on the quay and an auction board turning.","cn":"核心意象：黎明时的港口，渔船并排，码头冰面上摊着鱼，拍卖牌不停翻动。"},"chain":["INDUSTRY","FISHING GROUNDS","FLEETS","FISH STOCKS","SECTOR SCOPE","MANAGEMENT"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"SECTOR TO PLACE: an industry is also a set of named grounds on the water.","cn":"从行业到地点：一个产业同时也是一片片具名水域。"},{"senses":"03 · 04","en":"GEAR TO RESOURCE: boats and gear exist only because there is a stock to harvest.","cn":"从渔具到资源：船与网存在，只因为有可收获取的资源。"},{"senses":"06","en":"THE INLAND WATERS: the same harvest logic applies in rivers and lakes.","cn":"内陆水域：同一套收获逻辑也适用于河流与湖泊。"},{"senses":"05","en":"THE WIDER SECTOR: once aquaculture is counted, one word covers both.","cn":"行业口径：一旦算入养殖，一个词就覆盖两者。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"MANAGEMENT TO RIGHTS: rules decide who may fish, and those permissions become property.","cn":"从管理到权利：规则决定谁能捕鱼，这些许可随后成为财产。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Fisheries is a plural noun whose base fishery is a transparent native root plus a borrowed suffix; the plural adds no new meaning beyond number.","cn":"fisheries 是复数名词，其基础 fishery 由本族词根加借入后缀透明构成；复数除数量外不添加新义。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The suffix -ery reaches Latin -aria through French, while fish itself is Germanic; only piscis is a distant Latin relative.","cn":"后缀 -ery 经法语上溯拉丁 -aria，而 fish 本身属日耳曼语；只有 piscis 是拉丁远亲。"},"items":[{"word":"fish","structure":"Old English fisc, Germanic *fiskaz","meaning":"fish; to catch fish","meaningCN":"鱼；捕鱼","example":"The fish return to the river each year.","exampleCN":"鱼每年回到这条河。"},{"word":"-ery","structure":"Old French -erie from Latin -aria","meaning":"place or practice of","meaningCN":"……的地点或行业","example":"The suffix builds words like bakery and fishery.","exampleCN":"这个后缀构成 bakery 与 fishery 一类词。"},{"word":"fishery","structure":"fish + -ery","meaning":"a fishing ground or business","meaningCN":"渔场或渔业企业","example":"The fishery reopened after recovery.","exampleCN":"资源恢复后渔场重新开放。"},{"word":"fisheries","structure":"fishery + plural -ies","meaning":"several fisheries; the sector","meaningCN":"多处渔业；整个行业","example":"Fisheries depend on healthy stocks.","exampleCN":"渔业依赖健康的资源。"},{"word":"fisher","structure":"fish + -er (agent)","meaning":"a person who fishes","meaningCN":"捕鱼的人","example":"The fisher mended the net at dawn.","exampleCN":"渔民在黎明修补渔网。"},{"word":"fisherman","structure":"fisher + man","meaning":"a person who catches fish","meaningCN":"渔民","example":"The fisherman knew the tide by memory.","exampleCN":"这位渔民凭记忆就知道潮汐。"},{"word":"fishing","structure":"fish + -ing (gerund)","meaning":"the activity of catching fish","meaningCN":"捕鱼活动","example":"Fishing is restricted in spring.","exampleCN":"春季捕鱼受限。"},{"word":"fisheries management","structure":"fisheries + management (compound)","meaning":"the regulation of fishing","meaningCN":"渔业管理","example":"Fisheries management uses stock assessments.","exampleCN":"渔业管理使用资源评估。"},{"word":"aquaculture","structure":"Latin aqua 'water' + cultura 'cultivation'","meaning":"the farming of aquatic organisms","meaningCN":"水生物养殖","example":"Aquaculture now exceeds capture in some markets.","exampleCN":"在某些市场，养殖已超过捕捞。"},{"word":"stock assessment","structure":"stock + assessment (compound)","meaning":"the scientific estimate of a fish population","meaningCN":"鱼类种群的科学评估","example":"The stock assessment set the catch limit.","exampleCN":"资源评估设定了捕捞上限。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"piscis","structure":"piscis, piscis (m., third declension)","meaning":"fish","meaningCN":"鱼"},{"word":"-aria","structure":"-aria (neuter plural suffix; place or business)","meaning":"place or business of","meaningCN":"……的地点或行业"},{"word":"aqua","structure":"aqua, aquae (f., first declension)","meaning":"water","meaningCN":"水"}]}},{"word":"hydrology","ipa_uk":"/haɪˈdrɒlədʒi/","ipa_us":"/haɪˈdrɑːlədʒi/","definition_zh":"水文学；水文循环研究；水文状况；水文过程；水资源评估；工程水文学；生态水文学；行星水文学","definition_en":"the science of water on Earth: its movement, distribution, storage and interaction with land, air and life","core_image":"一条河从山地降水到平原径流，再蒸发成云，水在图上画出一个闭环","scene":"水文学家在河谷布设水位尺，把降雨、径流与蒸发画进同一张循环图。Hydrology explains why the river rises days after the rain has stopped.","sceneCN":"这里指「研究地球上水的分布与运动的学科」（第 1 个义项：以水文循环、径流、蒸发与储水为对象的科学）；句意为水文学解释了为什么雨停数日之后河水才上涨。场景物件：水位尺、河谷、循环图、雨量筒。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"水文学；水文状况（不可数；指多个分支时偶用复数 hydrologies）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"engineering hydrology","zh":"工程水文学"},{"phrase":"the hydrology of a catchment","zh":"某流域的水文状况"},{"phrase":"hydrology and water resources","zh":"水文学与水资源"},{"phrase":"isotope hydrology","zh":"同位素水文学"},{"phrase":"a hydrology model","zh":"水文模型"},{"phrase":"the hydrology of a wetland","zh":"湿地的水文情势"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（指多个分支或区域体系）","form":"hydrologies"},{"label":"相关形容词（英式）（水文的）","form":"hydrological"},{"label":"相关形容词（美式变体）（水文的）","form":"hydrologic"},{"label":"相关名词（水文学家）","form":"hydrologist"},{"label":"相关副词（从水文角度）","form":"hydrologically"},{"label":"相关前缀形式（水的前缀）","form":"hydro-"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"hydrological","pos":"adj.","zh":"水文的；水文学的"},{"word":"hydrologic","pos":"adj.","zh":"水文的（美式变体）"},{"word":"hydrologist","pos":"n.","zh":"水文学家"},{"word":"hydro-","pos":"prefix","zh":"水；水文的"},{"word":"hydrograph","pos":"n.","zh":"水位过程线；流量过程线"},{"word":"hydrosphere","pos":"n.","zh":"水圈"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The scientific discipline","titleCN":"水文学学科","definition":"the science of water on Earth: its movement, distribution, storage and interaction with land, air and life","definitionCN":"研究地球上水的运动、分布、储存及与陆地、空气和生命相互作用的科学","example":"Hydrology explains why the river rises days after the rain has stopped.","exampleCN":"水文学解释了为什么雨停数日之后河水才上涨。","why":"Hydro- is water and -logy is reasoned study, so the word names the disciplined study of water rather than water itself.","whyCN":"hydro- 是水，-logy 是系统的研究，因此这个词命名的是对水的学科研究，而非水本身。"},{"no":"02","title":"The study of the water cycle","titleCN":"水文循环研究","definition":"the branch that tracks evaporation, precipitation, runoff and storage as one cycle","definitionCN":"把蒸发、降水、径流与储水作为同一循环追踪的分支","example":"Hydrology treats the catchment as one connected cycle.","exampleCN":"水文学把流域看作一个相连的循环。","why":"The discipline's central object is the cycle, so the word often means the study of that loop rather than all water science.","whyCN":"这门学科的核心对象是循环，因此这个词常指对这一闭环的研究，而非全部水科学。"},{"no":"03","title":"A regional water regime","titleCN":"区域水文情势","definition":"the actual pattern of water in a place: when it arrives, where it goes and how it varies","definitionCN":"某地水的实际格局：何时到来、流向何处、如何变化","example":"The hydrology of the delta changed after the dam was built.","exampleCN":"大坝建成后，三角洲的水文情势改变了。","why":"Scientists say the hydrology of a place when they mean its measured regime, not the abstract discipline.","whyCN":"科学家说某地的 hydrology，指的是实测的水文情势，而不是抽象学科。"},{"no":"04","title":"Hydrological processes","titleCN":"水文过程","definition":"the physical processes of infiltration, runoff, evaporation and groundwater flow","definitionCN":"下渗、径流、蒸发与地下水流动等物理过程","example":"Hydrology studies how water moves through soil and rock.","exampleCN":"水文学研究水如何穿过土壤与岩石。","why":"The discipline is often reduced to its processes, so the word can name the mechanisms rather than the whole field.","whyCN":"这门学科常被化约为它的过程，因此这个词可指机制本身，而非整个领域。"},{"no":"05","title":"Water-resource assessment","titleCN":"水资源评估","definition":"the applied work of estimating supply, recharge and safe yield","definitionCN":"估算供水、补给与安全开采量的应用工作","example":"Hydrology sets how much groundwater can be pumped each year.","exampleCN":"水文学决定每年可抽取多少地下水。","why":"Society needs numbers for supply, so the science acquired an applied assessment sense.","whyCN":"社会需要供水的数字，因此这门科学获得了应用评估义。"},{"no":"06","title":"Engineering hydrology","titleCN":"工程水文学","definition":"the branch that supplies design floods, spillways and drainage capacity","definitionCN":"为设计洪水、溢洪道与排水能力提供依据的分支","example":"Engineering hydrology fixed the spillway width.","exampleCN":"工程水文学确定了溢洪道宽度。","why":"Builders need extreme values, so a distinct applied branch took the name of the parent science.","whyCN":"建造者需要极值，于是出现了一个以母学科命名的应用分支。"},{"no":"07","title":"Ecohydrology","titleCN":"生态水文学","definition":"the study of how water and living communities shape each other","definitionCN":"研究水与生命群落如何相互塑造的学问","example":"Hydrology and ecology meet in the study of wetland plants.","exampleCN":"水文学与生态学在湿地植物研究中相遇。","why":"When water is studied through its effects on organisms, the field gains an ecological face.","whyCN":"当水通过其对生物的影响被研究，这门学问就多了一张生态面孔。"},{"no":"08","title":"Planetary hydrology","titleCN":"行星水文学","definition":"the study of water and water-like fluids on other planets and moons","definitionCN":"研究其他行星与卫星上的水及类水液体的学问","example":"Planetary hydrology compares Earth's rivers with channels on Mars.","exampleCN":"行星水文学把地球的河流与火星的河道相比较。","why":"The methods travel beyond Earth, so the word now covers water systems on other worlds.","whyCN":"方法可以离开地球，因此这个词如今涵盖其他世界的水系统。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Hydrology joins Greek hydōr 'water' to -logia 'study, reasoned account'. The English word is recorded from the eighteenth century. Dates are approximate.","cn":"hydrology 把希腊 hydōr「水」与 -logia「研究、系统论述」组合起来。英语词自十八世纪有记录。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK HYDOR","en":"Hydōr meant 'water'; its deeper origin is often connected with a reconstructed Indo-European root *wed- 'water', but that root is a reconstruction, not a demonstrated form.","cn":"hydōr 意为「水」；其更深来源常被联系到重构的印欧词根 *wed-「水」，但那只是重构，不是已证实的形式。"},{"era":"GREEK LOGOS","en":"Logos meant 'word, reason, account', and -logia named a field of reasoned study; legein 'to gather, say' is its verb.","cn":"logos 意为「言词、理性、论述」，-logia 命名一个系统研究的领域；其动词是 legein「聚集、言说」。"},{"era":"SCIENTIFIC LATIN","en":"Modern Latin used hydrologia for the study of water, and English borrowed the pattern in the eighteenth century.","cn":"近代拉丁用 hydrologia 指对水的研究，英语在十八世纪借用了这一构词模式。"},{"era":"EARLY SCOPE","en":"Early hydrology was mostly descriptive and engineering-oriented, concerned with springs, rivers and water supply.","cn":"早期水文学多为描述性与工程导向，关心泉、河流与供水。"},{"era":"MODERN SCIENCE","en":"In the twentieth century hydrology became a quantitative science of the whole cycle, using gauges, tracers and models.","cn":"到二十世纪，水文学成为研究整个循环的定量科学，使用水位计、示踪剂与模型。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin and first date): the pre-Greek source of hydōr is uncertain, *wed- is a reconstruction, and the first English use of hydrology is not exactly dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源与首见年代）：hydōr 的前希腊语来源不确定，*wed- 属重构，hydrology 最早的英语使用没有精确年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the same hydr- stock with different grammatical jobs; group two holds neighbouring water sciences that are often confused with hydrology.","cn":"第一组是同出 hydr- 词干、语法角色不同的词；第二组是常与水文学混淆的邻近水科学。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"hydrological","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","tag":"adjective","definition":"Relating to hydrology; it modifies a noun and cannot stand alone as the name of the science.","definitionCN":"与水文学有关的；它修饰名词，不能独自作为学科名。"},{"word":"hydrologist","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒlədʒɪst/","tag":"person","definition":"A person who practises hydrology; it is the agent, not the field.","definitionCN":"从事水文学的人；它是施事者，不是领域。"},{"word":"hydrologic","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəˈlɒdʒɪk/","tag":"US adjective variant","definition":"The shorter American adjective for the same idea; it differs in spelling, not in meaning.","definitionCN":"同一概念的较短美式形容词；差别在拼写，不在意义。"},{"word":"hydro-","ipa":"/ˈhaɪdrəʊ/","tag":"combining form","definition":"A prefix meaning water; it builds words such as hydrosphere and hydroelectric but is not a word by itself.","definitionCN":"表示水的构词成分；它构成 hydrosphere、hydroelectric 等词，但本身不是独立词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"hydrography","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒɡrəfi/","tag":"mapping, not theory","definition":"The measurement and mapping of water bodies for navigation; it describes where water is, not how it moves.","definitionCN":"为航行测量并绘制水体；它描述水在哪里，而不是水如何运动。"},{"word":"hydraulics","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒlɪks/","tag":"fluid mechanics","definition":"The mechanics of fluids in motion and under pressure; it is the physics used by hydrology, not the whole science.","definitionCN":"研究流体运动与受压的力学；它是水文学使用的物理，而不是整个科学。"},{"word":"hydrogeology","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəʊdʒiˈɒlədʒi/","tag":"groundwater branch","definition":"The geology of groundwater; it is a subfield of hydrology focused on rock and aquifers.","definitionCN":"研究地下水的地质学；它是水文学中聚焦岩石与含水层的子领域。"},{"word":"hydrometeorology","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəʊˌmiːtiəˈrɒlədʒi/","tag":"atmosphere interface","definition":"The study of water in the atmosphere and its transfer to the ground; it is the weather side of the cycle.","definitionCN":"研究大气中的水及其向地面输送；它是循环中天气的一侧。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real Greek parts, real subfields and real measurement terms.","cn":"正常联想：真实希腊构件、真实子领域与真实测量术语。"},"normal":[{"en":"Hydro- is water; -logy is reasoned study.","cn":"hydro- 是水；-logy 是系统研究。"},{"en":"Hydrology follows the whole cycle, not just rivers.","cn":"水文学追踪整个循环，不只是河流。"},{"en":"A hydrograph is the plotted rise and fall of a river.","cn":"水文过程线画的是河流的涨落。"},{"en":"Engineering hydrology supplies design floods and spillway sizes.","cn":"工程水文学提供设计洪水与溢洪道尺寸。"},{"en":"Ecohydrology and planetary hydrology extend the field to life and to other worlds.","cn":"生态水文学与行星水文学把领域扩展到生命与其他世界。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a river drawn as a loop that returns to the sky.","cn":"想象一条河被画成一个回到天空的闭环。"},{"en":"Picture rain that arrives today but reaches the river next week.","cn":"想象今天落下的雨，下周才到达河流。"},{"en":"Picture a gauge on a bank as the pulse of a whole catchment.","cn":"想象岸边一根水尺，是整个流域的脉搏。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Hydrology links rainfall to the water that finally reaches the tap.","cn":"水文学把降雨与最终到达水龙头的水联系起来。"},{"en":"The hydrology of the mountain catchment is changing with less snow.","cn":"随着积雪减少，山地流域的水文情势正在改变。"},{"en":"Hydrology and economics must be planned together in dry regions.","cn":"在干旱地区，水文学与经济学必须一起规划。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「hydro（水）+ -logy（学科）」——研究水的学问 → 水文学","word":"hydrology"},"root":"希腊 hydōr「水」（更深来源不确定，*wed- 为重构）+ -logia「研究、论述」← logos「言词、理性」/ legein「聚集、言说」→ hydrology。英语十八世纪起有记录。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one water science: the discipline, the cycle, a regional regime, its processes, resource assessment, engineering, ecology and other planets.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一门水科学展开：学科、循环、区域情势、过程、资源评估、工程、生态与其他行星。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a river drawn as a closed loop from mountain rain through runoff and evaporation back to cloud.","cn":"核心意象：一条河被画成闭环，从山地降雨经径流与蒸发回到云。"},"chain":["DISCIPLINE","WATER CYCLE","REGIONAL REGIME","PROCESSES","ASSESSMENT","ENGINEERING"],"branches":[{"senses":"02 · 04","en":"CYCLE TO PROCESS: the loop is studied by separating infiltration, runoff and evaporation.","cn":"从循环到过程：把闭环拆成下渗、径流与蒸发来研究。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"REGIME TO SUPPLY: a place's measured pattern becomes its safe yield.","cn":"从情势到供水：某地实测的格局变成安全开采量。"},{"senses":"06","en":"ENGINEERING: estimates of extremes become spillway widths and drainage capacity.","cn":"工程水文：极值估计变成溢洪道宽度与排水能力。"},{"senses":"07","en":"THE WETLAND: the same water shapes the plants and animals of wetlands.","cn":"生态水文学：同一股水塑造湿地的动植物。"},{"senses":"01 · 08","en":"EARTH TO WORLDS: the methods travel to channels and aquifers on other planets.","cn":"从地球到其他世界：方法可迁移到其他行星的河道与含水层。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Hydrology is a Greek compound of a water root and a study suffix, and the same root builds a large family of English technical words.","cn":"hydrology 是希腊语复合词，由水词根与研究后缀构成，同一词根还构成一大族英语技术词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The word is Greek rather than Latin, but the Greek root reached scientific Latin as hydro- and then entered English; hydrologic forms often pass through Latinized spellings.","cn":"这个词属希腊语而非拉丁语，但希腊词根以 hydro- 进入科学拉丁，再进入英语；水文形容词常经拉丁化拼写。"},"items":[{"word":"hydōr","structure":"Greek hydōr 'water' (neuter noun)","meaning":"water","meaningCN":"水","example":"Hydōr is the root behind hydro-.","exampleCN":"hydōr 是 hydro- 背后的词根。"},{"word":"hydro-","structure":"Greek hydro- combining form","meaning":"water; relating to water","meaningCN":"水；与水有关的","example":"Hydro- opens words such as hydrosphere.","exampleCN":"hydro- 开启 hydrosphere 一类词。"},{"word":"-logy","structure":"Greek -logia 'study of'","meaning":"a field of study","meaningCN":"一个研究领域","example":"Biology and geology use the same suffix.","exampleCN":"生物学与地质学使用同一后缀。"},{"word":"hydrology","structure":"hydro- + -logy","meaning":"the study of water","meaningCN":"研究水的学问","example":"Hydrology measures the whole cycle.","exampleCN":"水文学测量整个循环。"},{"word":"hydrological","structure":"hydrology + -ical (adjective)","meaning":"relating to hydrology","meaningCN":"与水文学有关的","example":"Hydrological models predict the flood peak.","exampleCN":"水文模型预测洪峰。"},{"word":"hydrologic","structure":"hydrology + -ic (US variant)","meaning":"relating to hydrology","meaningCN":"与水文学有关的（美式）","example":"The hydrologic cycle is the same idea.","exampleCN":"水文循环是同一概念。"},{"word":"hydrologist","structure":"hydrology + -ist (person)","meaning":"a practitioner of hydrology","meaningCN":"水文学从业者","example":"The hydrologist read the gauge.","exampleCN":"水文学家读取了水位。"},{"word":"hydrograph","structure":"hydro- + -graph (drawing)","meaning":"a plotted record of water level or flow","meaningCN":"水位或流量的绘制记录","example":"The hydrograph shows the storm peak.","exampleCN":"过程线显示风暴峰值。"},{"word":"hydrosphere","structure":"hydro- + sphere","meaning":"all the water on Earth","meaningCN":"地球上全部的水","example":"The hydrosphere links ocean, ice and cloud.","exampleCN":"水圈把海洋、冰与云联系起来。"},{"word":"hydrogeology","structure":"hydro- + geology","meaning":"the geology of groundwater","meaningCN":"地下水的地质学","example":"Hydrogeology maps the aquifer.","exampleCN":"水文地质学绘制含水层。"}],"latinEntries":[]}},{"word":"hydrological","ipa_uk":"/ˌhaɪdrəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","ipa_us":"/ˌhaɪdrəˈlɑːdʒɪkl/","definition_zh":"水文的；水文学的；水文循环的；水文情势的；水文模型的；水文极值的","definition_en":"relating to the study of water, to the water cycle or to the water conditions of a place","core_image":"一张图上并排画着雨量柱、径流曲线与地下水位线，三条线互相呼应","scene":"工程队的桌面上摊着整年的雨量柱与水位曲线，技术员用尺比对着两个峰值。The engineers compared hydrological records from the last century.","sceneCN":"这里指「与水文学或水文情势有关的」（第 1 个义项：属于水文学研究范围、用于描述水的分布与运动）；句意为工程师比较了上个世纪的水文记录。场景物件：雨量柱、水位曲线、尺、桌面图纸。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"水文的；水文学的（无比较级；美式变体 hydrologic）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"hydrological cycle","zh":"水文循环"},{"phrase":"hydrological model","zh":"水文模型"},{"phrase":"hydrological data","zh":"水文数据"},{"phrase":"hydrological drought","zh":"水文干旱"},{"phrase":"hydrological station","zh":"水文站"},{"phrase":"hydrological year","zh":"水文年"},{"phrase":"hydrological regime","zh":"水文情势"}],"forms":[{"label":"美式变体","form":"hydrologic"},{"label":"副词（从水文角度）","form":"hydrologically"},{"label":"相关名词（水文学）","form":"hydrology"},{"label":"相关名词（水文学家）","form":"hydrologist"},{"label":"相关名词（水文过程线）","form":"hydrograph"},{"label":"相关名词（水圈）","form":"hydrosphere"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"hydrology","pos":"n.","zh":"水文学"},{"word":"hydrologic","pos":"adj.","zh":"水文的（美式变体）"},{"word":"hydrologically","pos":"adv.","zh":"从水文角度"},{"word":"hydrologist","pos":"n.","zh":"水文学家"},{"word":"hydrograph","pos":"n.","zh":"水位过程线"},{"word":"hydrosphere","pos":"n.","zh":"水圈"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Relating to hydrology","titleCN":"与水文学有关的","definition":"relating to the study of water, to the water cycle or to the water conditions of a place","definitionCN":"与水的研究、水文循环或某地水文情势有关","example":"The engineers compared hydrological records from the last century.","exampleCN":"工程师比较了上个世纪的水文记录。","why":"The adjective adds the Latin-derived -ical to hydrology, so it marks anything that belongs to the science or its data.","whyCN":"这个形容词给 hydrology 加上拉丁来源的 -ical，标记属于这门科学或其数据的事物。"},{"no":"02","title":"Of the water cycle","titleCN":"水文循环的","definition":"describing the movement of water between air, land, ocean and living things","definitionCN":"描述水在空气、陆地、海洋与生物之间运动","example":"Hydrological models link rainfall to river flow.","exampleCN":"水文模型把降雨与河流流量联系起来。","why":"The cycle is the central object of the science, so the adjective most often modifies cycle or model.","whyCN":"循环是这门科学的核心对象，因此这个形容词最常修饰 cycle 或 model。"},{"no":"03","title":"Of a regional water regime","titleCN":"区域水文情势的","definition":"describing the actual water conditions of a catchment, wetland or region","definitionCN":"描述某流域、湿地或区域的实际水文条件","example":"The wetland's hydrological regime depends on seasonal flooding.","exampleCN":"湿地的水文情势取决于季节性淹水。","why":"When the noun is regime or condition, the adjective points to measured local behaviour rather than the discipline.","whyCN":"当名词是 regime 或 condition 时，这个形容词指向实测的地方行为，而不是学科。"},{"no":"04","title":"Of models and data","titleCN":"水文模型与数据的","definition":"describing the datasets, models and projections used to represent water systems","definitionCN":"描述用来表示水系统的数据集、模型与预测","example":"Hydrological data are stored as daily gauge readings.","exampleCN":"水文数据以每日水位读数储存。","why":"Modern work is largely model-based, so the adjective often means computational rather than field-based.","whyCN":"现代工作大量基于模型，因此这个形容词常指计算性的，而非野外的。"},{"no":"05","title":"Of monitoring and measurement","titleCN":"水文观测的","definition":"describing gauges, stations and networks that measure water","definitionCN":"描述测量水的尺度、站点与网络","example":"The hydrological station recorded a new high-water mark.","exampleCN":"水文站记录了一个新的高水位标记。","why":"Observation is the empirical base of the science, so the adjective can point to the instruments themselves.","whyCN":"观测是这门科学的经验基础，因此这个形容词可指仪器本身。"},{"no":"06","title":"Of extremes","titleCN":"水文极值的","definition":"describing floods, droughts and low flows that define design and risk","definitionCN":"描述决定工程设计与风险的洪水、干旱与低流量","example":"Hydrological drought begins when river flow falls below normal.","exampleCN":"当河流流量低于常年，水文干旱就开始了。","why":"Planning turns on rare events, so the adjective frequently names the extremes rather than the average.","whyCN":"规划取决于稀有事件，因此这个形容词常指极值而非平均值。"},{"no":"07","title":"Of ecohydrology","titleCN":"生态水文的","definition":"describing the links between water and plants, animals and ecosystems","definitionCN":"描述水与植物、动物及生态系统之间的联系","example":"Hydrological change can decide which wetland plants survive.","exampleCN":"水文变化能决定哪些湿地植物存活。","why":"When the question is which species live where, the adjective joins water science to ecology.","whyCN":"当问题变成哪些物种住在哪里，这个形容词就把水科学与生态学连起来。"},{"no":"08","title":"Of the hydrological year","titleCN":"水文年的","definition":"describing the annual accounting period that begins when storage is lowest","definitionCN":"描述从储水最低时开始的一年核算周期","example":"The hydrological year starts before the first snowmelt.","exampleCN":"水文年在第一次融雪之前开始。","why":"Water budgets cannot follow the calendar year, so water managers fixed a separate year and the adjective names it.","whyCN":"水的收支不能按日历年计算，因此管水者另立一个年度，形容词便用来指它。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Hydrological is hydrology plus the adjective suffix -ical, which reaches Latin -icus and Greek -ikos. The word is a modern technical derivative. Dates are approximate.","cn":"hydrological 是 hydrology 加形容词后缀 -ical，后者上溯拉丁 -icus 与希腊 -ikos。这个词是近代技术派生词。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK HYDOR","en":"Hydōr 'water' is the root; its deeper origin is often linked to a reconstructed *wed- 'water', which is a reconstruction rather than a proven form.","cn":"hydōr「水」是词根；其更深来源常被联系到重构的 *wed-「水」，那是重构而非已证实形式。"},{"era":"HYDROLOGY","en":"Hydrology, the study of water, was formed from hydro- plus -logy and entered English in the eighteenth century.","cn":"hydrology 是对水的研究，由 hydro- 加 -logy 构成，十八世纪进入英语。"},{"era":"GREEK -IKOS","en":"Greek -ikos made adjectives meaning 'of or belonging to'; Latin -icus and French -ique carried it into English.","cn":"希腊 -ikos 构成「属于……的」形容词；拉丁 -icus 与法语 -ique 把它带入英语。"},{"era":"-ICAL","en":"English -ical became the fuller adjective ending, producing hydrological alongside the shorter hydrologic.","cn":"英语 -ical 成为较完整的形容词词尾，产生 hydrological，与较短的 hydrologic 并存。"},{"era":"TECHNICAL SPREAD","en":"In the twentieth century the adjective spread into hydrology, engineering and ecology, attaching to models, data and regimes.","cn":"到二十世纪，这个形容词扩散到水文学、工程与生态学，附着于模型、数据与情势等名词。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin): the pre-Greek source of hydōr is uncertain and *wed- remains a reconstruction; the first use of hydrological is not precisely dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源）：hydōr 的前希腊语来源不确定，*wed- 仍属重构；hydrological 最早的使用没有精确年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds spelling and grammar variants of the same adjective; group two holds other water-related adjectives that describe different things.","cn":"第一组是同一形容词的拼写与语法变体；第二组是描述不同事物的其他水相关形容词。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"hydrologic","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəˈlɒdʒɪk/","tag":"US variant","definition":"The shorter American spelling of the same adjective; it carries no different meaning.","definitionCN":"同一形容词的较短美式拼写；意义没有差别。"},{"word":"hydrology","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒlədʒi/","tag":"the noun","definition":"The science itself; the adjective must attach to a noun such as cycle or model.","definitionCN":"学科本身；形容词必须附着于 cycle 或 model 等名词。"},{"word":"hydrologist","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒlədʒɪst/","tag":"the person","definition":"A practitioner of the science; it is a person, not a quality of data or cycles.","definitionCN":"从事这门科学的人；它指人，而不是数据或循环的性质。"},{"word":"hydraulically","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒlɪkli/","tag":"different root","definition":"Relating to fluid power and pressure, from Greek hydraulikos; it is mechanics, not the study of the whole cycle.","definitionCN":"与流体动力和压力有关，出自希腊 hydraulikos；它属力学，不是对整个循环的研究。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"hydrometeorological","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəʊˌmiːtiərəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","tag":"weather side","definition":"Relating to the atmospheric part of the water cycle; it is narrower than hydrological.","definitionCN":"与水文循环中大气部分有关；它比 hydrological 窄。"},{"word":"ecohydrological","ipa":"/ˌiːkəʊˌhaɪdrəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","tag":"life and water","definition":"Relating to the interaction of water with ecosystems; it is a specialized branch of hydrological work.","definitionCN":"与水及生态系统相互作用有关；它是水文工作的专门分支。"},{"word":"hydrographic","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəˈɡræfɪk/","tag":"mapping","definition":"Relating to the measurement and mapping of water bodies; it describes surveying, not the science of movement.","definitionCN":"与水体的测量与制图有关；它描述测绘，而不是运动科学。"},{"word":"aqueous","ipa":"/ˈeɪkwiəs/","tag":"containing water","definition":"Containing or resembling water; it describes a medium, not a scientific field or cycle.","definitionCN":"含水或像水的；它描述介质，而不是科学领域或循环。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real adjective endings, real technical collocations and real spelling variants.","cn":"正常联想：真实形容词词尾、真实技术搭配与真实拼写变体。"},"normal":[{"en":"Hydrology plus -ical makes the adjective hydrological.","cn":"hydrology 加 -ical 构成形容词 hydrological。"},{"en":"The shorter hydrologic is the American spelling.","cn":"较短的 hydrologic 是美式拼写。"},{"en":"Hydrological cycle, model and data are the common collocations.","cn":"水文循环、水文模型与水文数据是常见搭配。"},{"en":"Hydrological drought is about flow, not rainfall alone.","cn":"水文干旱讲的是流量，不只是降雨。"},{"en":"A hydrological year starts when storage is lowest.","cn":"水文年从储水最低时开始。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture three lines on one graph: rain bars, river curve and groundwater level.","cn":"想象一张图上三条线：雨量柱、河流曲线与地下水位。"},{"en":"Picture a model that turns today's rain into next week's river height.","cn":"想象一个模型，把今天的雨变成下周的河高。"},{"en":"Picture a year that begins not in January but when the water is lowest.","cn":"想象一个不在正月开始、而在水最低时开始的年份。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Hydrological models predict how fast the flood will arrive.","cn":"水文模型预测洪水到达的速度。"},{"en":"The wetland's hydrological regime was altered by drainage.","cn":"排水改变了湿地的水文情势。"},{"en":"Hydrological stations send data every hour during the monsoon.","cn":"季风期间水文站每小时发送数据。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「hydrology（水文学）+ -ical（形容词后缀）」——属于水文学的 → 水文的","word":"hydrological"},"root":"希腊 hydōr「水」+ -logia「研究」→ hydrology；再加希腊 -ikos / 拉丁 -icus 形成的形容词后缀 -ical → hydrological。hydōr 的更深来源不确定，*wed- 为重构。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one adjective: of the science, of the cycle, of a local regime, of models, of monitoring, of extremes, of ecology and of the water year.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一个形容词展开：属于学科、属于循环、属于地方情势、属于模型、属于观测、属于极值、属于生态、属于水文年。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: rainfall bars, a river curve and a groundwater line drawn side by side on one sheet.","cn":"核心意象：雨量柱、河流曲线与地下水位线并排画在同一张纸上。"},"chain":["DISCIPLINE","WATER CYCLE","REGIONAL REGIME","MODELS AND DATA","EXTREMES","ECOHYDROLOGY"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"SCIENCE TO LOOP: the adjective marks both the field and its central object, the cycle.","cn":"从学科到闭环：这个形容词既标记领域，也标记其核心对象——循环。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"REGIME TO GAUGE: a local pattern is known only through stations and measurements.","cn":"从情势到水尺：地方格局只有通过站点与测量才被知道。"},{"senses":"04 · 06","en":"MODEL TO EXTREME: models are tested most sharply on floods and droughts.","cn":"从模型到极值：模型在洪水与干旱中受到最尖锐的检验。"},{"senses":"07","en":"ECO USE: the same water pattern decides which species can live in a wetland.","cn":"生态用法：同一套水格局决定哪些物种能在湿地生存。"},{"senses":"08","en":"THE WATER YEAR: accounting runs on its own calendar, fixed by the lowest storage.","cn":"水文年：水的核算按自己的年度，以最低储水为界。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Hydrological is a derived adjective with a transparent base and a productive ending; the base hydrology is itself a Greek compound.","cn":"hydrological 是派生形容词，基词透明、词尾能产；基词 hydrology 本身又是希腊语复合词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The adjective ending reaches Latin -icus and Greek -ikos; the root is Greek, so the Latin layer here is the ending rather than the stem.","cn":"形容词词尾上溯拉丁 -icus 与希腊 -ikos；词根属希腊语，因此这里的拉丁层是词尾而非词干。"},"items":[{"word":"hydrology","structure":"Greek hydro- + -logy","meaning":"the study of water","meaningCN":"研究水的学问","example":"Hydrology supplies the base of the adjective.","exampleCN":"hydrology 提供这个形容词的基词。"},{"word":"-ic","structure":"Greek -ikos via Latin -icus","meaning":"of or belonging to","meaningCN":"属于……的","example":"Hydrologic is the shorter form.","exampleCN":"hydrologic 是较短形式。"},{"word":"-ical","structure":"English -ic + -al (fuller adjective ending)","meaning":"relating to","meaningCN":"与……有关的","example":"Hydrological is the fuller form.","exampleCN":"hydrological 是较完整形式。"},{"word":"hydrological","structure":"hydrology + -ical","meaning":"relating to hydrology","meaningCN":"与水文学有关的","example":"Hydrological data guide the design.","exampleCN":"水文数据指导设计。"},{"word":"hydrologic","structure":"hydrology + -ic","meaning":"relating to hydrology (US)","meaningCN":"与水文学有关的（美式）","example":"The hydrologic cycle is a closed loop.","exampleCN":"水文循环是一个闭环。"},{"word":"hydrologically","structure":"hydrological + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"from a hydrological point of view","meaningCN":"从水文角度","example":"Hydrologically, the two basins differ.","exampleCN":"从水文角度看，两个盆地不同。"},{"word":"hydrologist","structure":"hydrology + -ist (person)","meaning":"a water scientist","meaningCN":"水文学家","example":"A hydrologist checked the gauge.","exampleCN":"一位水文学家检查了水尺。"},{"word":"hydrograph","structure":"hydro- + -graph (drawing)","meaning":"a plotted flow record","meaningCN":"绘制的流量记录","example":"The hydrograph peaks after the rain.","exampleCN":"过程线在雨后达到峰值。"},{"word":"hydrosphere","structure":"hydro- + sphere","meaning":"all water on Earth","meaningCN":"地球上全部的水","example":"The hydrosphere includes ice and vapour.","exampleCN":"水圈包括冰与水汽。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"-icus","structure":"-icus, -ica, -icum (adjective suffix)","meaning":"of or belonging to","meaningCN":"属于……的"}]}},{"word":"hydrologist","ipa_uk":"/haɪˈdrɒlədʒɪst/","ipa_us":"/haɪˈdrɑːlədʒɪst/","definition_zh":"水文学家；水文工作者；水文观测员；水资源顾问；工程水文专家；生态水文专家","definition_en":"a person who studies or practises hydrology, especially the measurement and modelling of water","core_image":"一个人蹲在河岸，手里拿着水位计，身后的桌上摊着流域图","scene":"勘测队在干涸的河床上打井，年轻的技术员蹲下读取水位计的刻度。A hydrologist traced the missing water to a fissure beneath the valley.","sceneCN":"这里指「从事水文学研究或实践的人」（第 1 个义项：受过水文训练、负责测量与解释水的分布和运动的专业人员）；句意为一位水文学家把消失的水追踪到谷底的一条裂隙。场景物件：水位计、河床、井架、流域图。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"水文学家；水文工作者（可数；复数 hydrologists）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a field hydrologist","zh":"野外水文学家"},{"phrase":"a government hydrologist","zh":"政府水文学家"},{"phrase":"the hydrologist's gauge","zh":"水文学家的水尺"},{"phrase":"a consulting hydrologist","zh":"水文顾问"},{"phrase":"a hydrologist with the survey","zh":"勘测机构的水文学家"},{"phrase":"a team of hydrologists","zh":"一个水文学家团队"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数","form":"hydrologists"},{"label":"相关名词（水文学）","form":"hydrology"},{"label":"相关形容词（水文的）","form":"hydrological"},{"label":"相关形容词（美式）（水文的）","form":"hydrologic"},{"label":"相关副词（从水文角度）","form":"hydrologically"},{"label":"相关地点（水文站）","form":"hydrology station"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"hydrology","pos":"n.","zh":"水文学"},{"word":"hydrological","pos":"adj.","zh":"水文的"},{"word":"hydrologic","pos":"adj.","zh":"水文的（美式）"},{"word":"hydrologically","pos":"adv.","zh":"从水文角度"},{"word":"hydrograph","pos":"n.","zh":"水文过程线"},{"word":"hydrogeologist","pos":"n.","zh":"水文地质学家"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A research hydrologist","titleCN":"水文学研究者","definition":"a person who studies or practises hydrology, especially the measurement and modelling of water","definitionCN":"从事水文学研究或实践、尤其负责水的测量与建模的人","example":"A hydrologist traced the missing water to a fissure beneath the valley.","exampleCN":"一位水文学家把消失的水追踪到谷底的一条裂隙。","why":"Hydrology plus -ist marks the person who does the science, so the word names a practitioner rather than the field.","whyCN":"hydrology 加 -ist 标记做这门科学的人，因此这个词命名从业者，而非领域。"},{"no":"02","title":"A field practitioner","titleCN":"野外水文工作者","definition":"a worker who measures rainfall, river level and flow in the field","definitionCN":"在野外测量降雨、河流水位与流量的工作者","example":"The hydrologist waded out to read the staff gauge.","exampleCN":"水文学家涉水过去读取水尺。","why":"Most hydrological data are gathered outdoors, so the word often means the person at the gauge rather than the theorist.","whyCN":"大部分水文数据在户外采集，因此这个词常指站在水尺旁的人，而不是理论家。"},{"no":"03","title":"A monitoring technician","titleCN":"水文观测员","definition":"a technician who maintains stations, sensors and records","definitionCN":"维护水文站、传感器与记录的技术人员","example":"The hydrologist calibrated the pressure sensor before the storm.","exampleCN":"水文学家在风暴前校准了压力传感器。","why":"Instruments need care, so a distinct working role grew around the maintenance of observation networks.","whyCN":"仪器需要照料，于是围绕观测网络的维护长出一个独立的工作角色。"},{"no":"04","title":"A water-resource consultant","titleCN":"水资源顾问","definition":"a specialist who advises on supply, recharge and allocation","definitionCN":"就供水、补给与分配提供建议的专家","example":"The hydrologist advised the city on its aquifer budget.","exampleCN":"水文学家就城市含水层收支向市府提供建议。","why":"When the science is sold as a service, the practitioner becomes an adviser to clients and agencies.","whyCN":"当这门科学作为服务出售，从业者就成了客户与机构的顾问。"},{"no":"05","title":"An engineering hydrologist","titleCN":"工程水文专家","definition":"a specialist who supplies design floods and waterworks calculations","definitionCN":"提供设计洪水与水利工程计算的专家","example":"The engineering hydrologist set the dam's design flood.","exampleCN":"工程水文专家确定了大坝的设计洪水。","why":"Infrastructure needs a specialist who can turn records into design values, so a professional branch is named.","whyCN":"基础设施需要能把记录变成设计值的专家，于是出现一个以专业命名的分支。"},{"no":"06","title":"An ecohydrologist","titleCN":"生态水文专家","definition":"a specialist who studies water together with plants, animals and ecosystems","definitionCN":"把水与植物、动物及生态系统一起研究的专家","example":"The ecohydrologist mapped where the wetland would dry first.","exampleCN":"生态水文专家绘出了湿地最先干涸的位置。","why":"Where water science meets ecology, the practitioner takes a compound title that names both.","whyCN":"当水科学与生态学相遇，从业者获得一个同时命名两者的复合头衔。"},{"no":"07","title":"A climate hydrologist","titleCN":"气候水文专家","definition":"a specialist who studies how climate change alters water cycles","definitionCN":"研究气候变化如何改变水文循环的专家","example":"The climate hydrologist projected a shorter snow season.","exampleCN":"气候水文专家预测雪季会缩短。","why":"Global warming moved water questions into climate science, so a hybrid role emerged.","whyCN":"全球变暖把水的问题推进气候科学，于是出现混合角色。"},{"no":"08","title":"A citizen hydrologist","titleCN":"公民水文学家","definition":"a trained volunteer who records water data for a shared network","definitionCN":"为共享网络记录水数据的受训志愿者","example":"A citizen hydrologist photographed the flood mark.","exampleCN":"一位公民水文学家拍下了洪水痕迹。","why":"Observation networks need many hands, so the title widened to include trained volunteers.","whyCN":"观测网络需要许多双手，因此这个头衔扩展到受训志愿者。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Hydrologist is hydrology plus the person suffix -ist, which reaches Greek -istēs. The word is a nineteenth-century professional label. Dates are approximate.","cn":"hydrologist 是 hydrology 加人物后缀 -ist，后者上溯希腊 -istēs。这个词是十九世纪的职业标签。年代均为约数。"},"items":[{"era":"GREEK HYDOR","en":"Hydōr 'water' is the root; its deeper origin is often linked to a reconstructed *wed- 'water', which remains a reconstruction.","cn":"hydōr「水」是词根；其更深来源常被联系到重构的 *wed-「水」，那仍属重构。"},{"era":"HYDROLOGY","en":"Hydrology, the study of water, entered English in the eighteenth century from Greek hydro- plus -logia.","cn":"hydrology 是对水的研究，十八世纪由希腊 hydro- 加 -logia 进入英语。"},{"era":"GREEK -ISTES","en":"Greek -istēs marked a person who does or follows something; Latin -ista and French -iste carried it into English as -ist.","cn":"希腊 -istēs 标记从事或追随某事的人；拉丁 -ista 与法语 -iste 把它带入英语作 -ist。"},{"era":"PROFESSIONAL LABEL","en":"Hydrologist appeared as water science became a paid profession in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries.","cn":"随着水科学在十九与二十世纪成为有薪职业，hydrologist 作为职业标签出现。"},{"era":"SPECIALIZATION","en":"Later compound titles such as engineering hydrologist and ecohydrologist split the role by application.","cn":"后来工程水文专家、生态水文专家等复合头衔按应用把角色再细分。"},{"era":"UNCERTAIN DETAILS","en":"Source uncertain (deeper origin and first date): the pre-Greek source of hydōr is uncertain, *wed- is a reconstruction, and the first use of hydrologist is not precisely dated.","cn":"来源不确定（更深词源与首见年代）：hydōr 的前希腊语来源不确定，*wed- 属重构，hydrologist 最早的使用没有精确年代。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"Group one holds the same-root person, field and adjective forms; group two holds neighbouring water professions that are not interchangeable.","cn":"第一组是同根的人物、领域与形容词形式；第二组是邻近但不可互换的水相关职业。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"hydrology","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒlədʒi/","tag":"the field","definition":"The science of water; hydrologist is the person who practises it.","definitionCN":"研究水的科学；hydrologist 是从事它的人。"},{"word":"hydrological","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəˈlɒdʒɪkl/","tag":"the adjective","definition":"Relating to the science; it describes data or cycles, not a person.","definitionCN":"与这门科学有关的；它描述数据或循环，不指人。"},{"word":"hydrographer","ipa":"/haɪˈdrɒɡrəfə/","tag":"surveyor, different role","definition":"A person who measures and charts water bodies for navigation; the work is mapping rather than cycle science.","definitionCN":"为航行测量并绘制水体的人；其工作是制图，而不是循环科学。"},{"word":"hydrogeologist","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəʊdʒiˈɒlədʒɪst/","tag":"groundwater specialist","definition":"A person who studies groundwater in rock; it is a branch of hydrology, not the whole profession.","definitionCN":"研究岩石中地下水的人；它是水文学的一个分支，不是整个职业。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"water engineer","ipa":"/ˈwɔːtər ˌendʒɪˈnɪə/","tag":"design role","definition":"An engineer who designs supply and drainage works; a hydrologist supplies the water data that engineer uses.","definitionCN":"设计供水与排水工程的工程师；水文学家提供其使用的水数据。"},{"word":"hydrometeorologist","ipa":"/ˌhaɪdrəʊˌmiːtiəˈrɒlədʒɪst/","tag":"weather side","definition":"A specialist in atmospheric water and precipitation; the focus is weather, not the whole land-water cycle.","definitionCN":"研究大气水与降水的专家；重点在天气，而非整个陆水循环。"},{"word":"ecologist","ipa":"/ɪˈkɒlədʒɪst/","tag":"life focus","definition":"A scientist who studies organisms and their environment; an ecohydrologist works where water and life meet.","definitionCN":"研究生物与其环境的科学家；生态水文专家工作在水与生命交汇处。"},{"word":"citizen scientist","ipa":"/ˈsɪtɪzn ˈsaɪəntɪst/","tag":"volunteer role","definition":"A trained volunteer who collects data; a citizen hydrologist is the water-specific version.","definitionCN":"收集数据的受训志愿者；公民水文学家是水领域的专称。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Normal associations: real agent suffix, real professional titles and real branch names.","cn":"正常联想：真实施事后缀、真实职业头衔与真实分支名称。"},"normal":[{"en":"Hydrology plus -ist makes the person who does hydrology.","cn":"hydrology 加 -ist，就是做水文学的人。"},{"en":"The hydrologist reads the gauge, not just the textbook.","cn":"水文学家读水尺，不只读教科书。"},{"en":"Engineering, ecology and climate give the role its compound titles.","cn":"工程、生态与气候给这个角色带来复合头衔。"},{"en":"A hydrographer maps water; a hydrologist explains its movement.","cn":"水文测量员绘制水，水文学家解释水的运动。"},{"en":"A citizen hydrologist is a trained volunteer in the same network.","cn":"公民水文学家是同一网络中的受训志愿者。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture a person kneeling at a gauge while a whole valley's water passes by.","cn":"想象一个人跪在水尺旁，整个山谷的水从身边流过。"},{"en":"Picture a detective following a missing river underground.","cn":"想象一名侦探在地下去追一条消失的河。"},{"en":"Picture a bridge between a rain cloud and a city's taps.","cn":"想象一座连接雨云与城市水龙头的桥。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The hydrologist warned that the aquifer was being mined.","cn":"水文学家警告含水层正在被透支。"},{"en":"A hydrologist must explain uncertainty, not just averages.","cn":"水文学家必须解释不确定性，而不只是平均值。"},{"en":"The hydrologist's forecast gave the town two days to evacuate.","cn":"水文学家的预报给小镇争取了两天撤离时间。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"拆词记忆 · 非词源","text":"「hydrology（水文学）+ -ist（从事者）」——从事水文学的人 → 水文学家","word":"hydrologist"},"root":"希腊 hydōr「水」（更深来源不确定，*wed- 为重构）+ -logia「研究」→ hydrology；加希腊 -istēs / 拉丁 -ista / 法语 -iste 形成的人物后缀 -ist → hydrologist。十九世纪起成为职业标签。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Eight senses follow one practitioner: researcher, field worker, monitoring technician, consultant, engineering specialist, ecohydrologist, climate hydrologist and citizen volunteer.","cn":"八个义项沿着同一类从业者展开：研究者、野外工作者、观测员、顾问、工程专家、生态水文专家、气候水文专家与公民志愿者。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a person kneeling at a river gauge, a catchment map spread on the table behind.","cn":"核心意象：一个人蹲在河岸水尺旁，身后的桌上摊着流域图。"},"chain":["RESEARCHER","FIELD PRACTITIONER","MONITORING TECHNICIAN","CONSULTANT","ENGINEERING SPECIALIST","SPECIALIST BRANCH"],"branches":[{"senses":"01 · 02","en":"THEORY TO FIELD: the researcher and the gauge reader are the same role in two settings.","cn":"从理论到野外：研究者与读水尺的人是同一角色在两种场景。"},{"senses":"03 · 05","en":"SENSOR TO DESIGN: trustworthy readings become the design flood an engineer can use.","cn":"从传感器到设计：可信的读数变成工程师可用的设计洪水。"},{"senses":"04","en":"THE CONSULTANT: an estimate becomes a dam or drain on the ground.","cn":"顾问：一份估算落到地上，变成大坝或排水沟。"},{"senses":"06","en":"THE ECOLOGIST: the same training extends to how water shapes ecosystems.","cn":"生态水文：同一套训练延伸到水如何塑造生态系统。"},{"senses":"07 · 08","en":"CLIMATE TO CROWD: global projections and volunteer records both feed the same network.","cn":"从气候到公众：全球预测与志愿者记录都汇入同一网络。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Hydrologist is a transparent person noun: the field name plus -ist. The whole word can be read from its base and its agent suffix.","cn":"hydrologist 是透明的人物名词：领域名加 -ist。整个词可从基词与施事后缀读出。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The person suffix reached English through Latin -ista and French -iste from Greek -istēs; the base hydrology is Greek.","cn":"人物后缀经拉丁 -ista 与法语 -iste 上溯希腊 -istēs 进入英语；基词 hydrology 属希腊语。"},"items":[{"word":"hydrology","structure":"Greek hydro- + -logy","meaning":"the study of water","meaningCN":"研究水的学问","example":"Hydrology is the base of the title.","exampleCN":"hydrology 是这个头衔的基词。"},{"word":"-ist","structure":"Greek -istēs via Latin -ista and French -iste","meaning":"a person who does or follows","meaningCN":"从事或追随……的人","example":"Biology plus -ist gives biologist.","exampleCN":"biology 加 -ist 得到 biologist。"},{"word":"hydrologist","structure":"hydrology + -ist","meaning":"a practitioner of hydrology","meaningCN":"水文学从业者","example":"The hydrologist read the gauge at dawn.","exampleCN":"水文学家在黎明读取水尺。"},{"word":"hydrologists","structure":"hydrologist + plural -s","meaning":"several practitioners","meaningCN":"多位水文学家","example":"Hydrologists shared the station data.","exampleCN":"水文学家们共享了站点数据。"},{"word":"hydrological","structure":"hydrology + -ical","meaning":"relating to hydrology","meaningCN":"与水文学有关的","example":"The hydrological record spans a century.","exampleCN":"水文记录跨越一个世纪。"},{"word":"hydrologic","structure":"hydrology + -ic (US)","meaning":"relating to hydrology","meaningCN":"与水文学有关的（美式）","example":"The hydrologic model runs daily.","exampleCN":"水文模型每日运行。"},{"word":"hydrograph","structure":"hydro- + -graph","meaning":"a plotted water record","meaningCN":"绘制的水文记录","example":"The hydrograph showed a sharp peak.","exampleCN":"过程线显示一个尖峰。"},{"word":"hydrogeologist","structure":"hydro- + geologist","meaning":"a groundwater geologist","meaningCN":"水文地质学家","example":"The hydrogeologist logged the borehole.","exampleCN":"水文地质学家记录了钻孔。"},{"word":"hydrometeorologist","structure":"hydro- + meteorologist","meaning":"a specialist in atmospheric water","meaningCN":"大气水专家","example":"The hydrometeorologist forecast the rainfall.","exampleCN":"水文气象学家预报了降雨。"},{"word":"ecohydrologist","structure":"eco- + hydrologist","meaning":"a specialist in water and ecosystems","meaningCN":"生态水文专家","example":"The ecohydrologist mapped the drying wetland.","exampleCN":"生态水文专家绘出了干涸的湿地。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"-ista","structure":"-ista (m./f. agent suffix, medieval and modern Latin)","meaning":"one who practises","meaningCN":"从事者"}]}}]);
